B.aR0=s(["White moves first. Tap a piece, then a square it can reach.","Rook: any number of squares along a row or a column. Bishop: any number along a diagonal. Queen: like a rook and a bishop together.","Knight: an L shape, two squares one way and one to the side. It is the only piece that jumps over others.","King: one square in any direction, never onto a square that is attacked. Pawn: one square forward (two from its first move), and it captures one square diagonally forward.","Check means your king is attacked. You must answer it at once: move the king, block the attack or capture the attacker. If you cannot, it is checkmate.","Win by checkmate. A stalemate, the same position three times, fifty moves with no capture or pawn move, or too few pieces left are draws.","Castling, en passant and choosing your promotion piece all work. You can undo, ask for a hint, offer a draw or resign. A clock is optional and off unless you choose one."],t.s)
