B.ast=new A.X("home-enter-say",B.bcd,B.aRw,"The Sunnah when you go into your home is to mention Allah's name. The Prophet \ufdfa said: when a person enters his house and mentions the name of Allah when entering and while eating, Satan says to himself that there is no place to spend the night and no evening meal for him there, but when he enters without mentioning Allah's name, Satan says he has found a place to spend the night (Sahih Muslim 2018).\n\nSo the simple practice is to say \"Bismillah\" (in the name of Allah) as you enter. The Qur'an also tells believers to greet one another when entering houses, with a greeting from Allah (Qur'an 24:61), so saying \"As-salamu alaykum\" to the people inside, or to the house if it is empty, is part of it too.\n\nA longer du'a for entering and leaving the home is reported in Abu Dawud, but its chain is graded weak by the scholars I checked, so I do not give it as a Sunnah wording.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2018; Qur'an 24:61.\n[GO:/adhkar]","entering the home",!0,"")
B.byH=s(["\\b(?:which|what) (?:surah|sura|surat|ayah|ayat|verse|verses|quran|dua|du a)\\b.*\\b(?:protect|protects|protection|bless|blessing|hang|hung|put|place|read|recite)\\b.*\\b(?:home|house|door|entrance|doorway|entry)\\b","\\b(?:surah|sura|surat|ayah|ayat|verse|verses)\\b.*\\b(?:hang|hung|hanging|over|above|on)\\b.*\\b(?:entrance|door|doorway|entry|front door)\\b","\\b(?:protect|protecting|protection|bless|blessing|safe(?:guard)?) (?:of |for |my |the |our )?(?:home|house)\\b.*\\b(?:quran|surah|sura|verse|ayah|ayat|dua|du a|recite|read)\\b","\\b(?:quran|surah|sura|verse|ayah|ayat|dua|du a|recite|read)\\b.*\\b(?:protect|protecting|protection|bless|blessing|safe(?:guard)?) (?:of |for |my |the |our )?(?:home|house)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|can|should) i (?:protect|bless|purify|cleanse|safeguard|keep (?:safe|protected)) (?:my |the |our )?(?:home|house|family)\\b","\\bprotect(?:ing)? (?:my |the |our )?(?:home|house)\\b","\\bwhat (?:keeps?|drives?|chases?|makes?) (?:shaytan|satan|devil|jinn)s? (?:away|out|leave)\\b.*\\b(?:home|house)\\b"],t.s)
B.bq0=s(["\\b(?:haram|ruling|permissible|allowed|halal)\\b"],t.s)
B.aq4=new A.X("home-protect-surah",B.byH,B.bq0,"The reports are about reciting, not hanging. Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: do not make your houses into graveyards, for Satan runs away from the house in which Surah Al-Baqarah is recited (Sahih Muslim 780). So reading Al-Baqarah, or parts of it, at home is the practice the hadith points to.\n\nOther well-known recitations: the last two verses of Al-Baqarah (Qur'an 2:285-286), as reported by Abu Mas'ud: the Prophet said that whoever recites the last two verses of Surat Al-Baqarah at night, that is sufficient for him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5009); and Ayat al-Kursi (Qur'an 2:255), which Abu Hurayrah was taught as a guard for the night (Abu Hurayrah was taught that reciting Ayat al-Kursi at bedtime means Allah appoints a guard and no devil comes near until morning (Sahih al-Bukhari 2311)). Also saying Bismillah as you enter and leave.\n\nAbout hanging verses or writing them over the door: I did not find a report where the Prophet \ufdfa did that or told people to. Scholars differ on wearing or hanging Qur'anic verses as protection,. Many scholars therefore advise relying on recitation and du'a rather than on a hung object. For a ruling on a framed verse in your own home, please ask a scholar of your school.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 780; Qur'an 2:285-286, 2:255; Sahih al-Bukhari 5009, 2311.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/quran]","protecting the home",!0,"")
B.bAK=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|dhikr|words?)\\b.*\\b(?:travel|travelling|traveling|journey|trip|car|vehicle|plane|flight|riding|mount|setting out)\\b","\\b(?:travel|travelling|traveling|journey|trip|car|vehicle|plane|flight|riding|setting out)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:when|before|as) (?:i )?(?:travel|get in(?:to)? (?:a |the |my )?(?:car|vehicle|taxi)|board|start (?:a |my |the )?(?:trip|journey)|set out|take off)\\b","\\bsubhana (?:alladhi|allazi|lladhi) sakhkhara\\b"],t.s)
B.bvu=s(["\\b(?:prayer|salah|shorten|qasr|combine|jam|fasting|ramadan|haram|ruling)\\b"],t.s)
B.asl=new A.X("travel-dua",B.bAK,B.bvu,"Ibn Umar reported how the Prophet \ufdfa began a journey: whenever he mounted his camel to set out on a journey he said Allahu Akbar three times and then said \"Glory be to Him who subjected this to us, and we could not have done it ourselves, and to our Lord we shall return\" (Sahih Muslim 1342).\n\nThe words are from the Qur'an (Qur'an 43:13-14). People say them when they get into a car, board a plane or start any trip. The full du'a in the hadith continues with asking Allah for goodness and piety on the journey; the Dhikr and Du'a screen has it in full.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1342; Qur'an 43:13-14.\n[GO:/adhkar]","travel du'a",!0,"")
B.aWK=s(["\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i|do you) say (?:when|if|after) (?:i |you |someone |he |she )?sneez(?:e|es|ed|ing)\\b","\\b(?:sneez(?:e|es|ed|ing)|achoo)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|say|islam|islamic|sunnah|respond|reply|etiquette|manners)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|islamic|islam|sunnah|etiquette|manners)\\b.*\\bsneez(?:e|es|ed|ing)\\b","\\b(?:yarhamukallah|yarhamuka allah|yarhamuk allah|tashmeet|tashmit)\\b"],t.s)
B.anK=new A.X("sneeze-etiquette",B.aWK,B.b,'Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: if anyone of you sneezes he should say "Al-hamdu lillah" (praise be to Allah), and his Muslim brother or companion should say to him "Yarhamuka Allah" (may Allah have mercy on you), and when he says that the sneezer should reply "Yahdikum Allah wa yuslih balakum" (may Allah guide you and put your affairs right) (Sahih al-Bukhari 6224).\n\nSo: the one who sneezes says Alhamdulillah, the listener says Yarhamukallah, and the sneezer answers Yahdikumullah wa yuslihu balakum.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6224.',"sneezing",!0,"")
B.bsb=s(["\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i|do you) say (?:when|if|during|as) (?:it )?(?:rains?|raining|rainfall|there is rain|it is raining)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:rain|raining|rainfall|storm|thunder)\\b","\\b(?:rain|raining|rainfall)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|sunnah|islam|islamic)\\b"],t.s)
B.bq5=s(["\\b(?:istisqa|prayer for rain|salat|salah)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqH=new A.X("rain-dua",B.bsb,B.bq5,"Aisha reported: whenever Allah's Messenger \ufdfa saw the rain he used to say \"O Allah, let it be a strong, fruitful rain\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 1032).\n\nIn Arabic: Allahumma sayyiban nafi'a. Many people also make du'a while it rains, since scholars count it as a time when du'a is hoped to be accepted; I am not citing a report for that here.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1032.\n[GO:/adhkar]","rain du'a",!0,"")
B.b8O=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|dhikr|adhkar|supplication|words?)\\b.*\\b(?:protect|protection|protected|harm|safe(?:ty)?|sudden)\\b.*\\b(?:morning|evening|every (?:day|night)|day|night)\\b","\\b(?:protect\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|dhikr|adhkar)\\b.*\\b(?:morning|evening)\\b","\\b(?:morning|evening)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|dhikr|adhkar)\\b.*\\b(?:protect\\w*)\\b","\\bbismillahi? ?(?:alladhi|allazi|lladhi) la yadurru\\b","\\b(?:protect\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:from )?(?:harm|sudden affliction|calamity)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|dhikr|say|recite)\\b","\\bnothing (?:on|in) (?:earth|the earth|heaven|the heavens) can (?:cause )?harm\\b"],t.s)
B.SV=s(["\\b(?:haram|ruling)\\b"],t.s)
B.arc=new A.X("morning-evening-protection",B.b8O,B.SV,"Uthman ibn Affan reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: there is no servant who says every morning and every evening \"In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in the heavens can cause harm, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing\" three times, but nothing will harm him (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3388, hasan sahih per al-Albani).\n\nAbu Dawud has the same report with sudden affliction named (whoever says it three times will not suffer a sudden affliction until the morning, and whoever says it in the morning will not suffer sudden affliction until the evening (Sunan Abu Dawud 5088, sahih per Darussalam)).\n\nIn Arabic: Bismillahi alladhi la yadurru ma'a ismihi shay'un fil-ardi wa la fis-sama'i wa huwa as-Sami'u al-'Alim. It is a trust in Allah, not a charm: the protection is by His permission.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3388, hasan sahih per al-Albani; Sunan Abu Dawud 5088, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/adhkar]","morning and evening protection",!0,"")
B.bAI=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:backbiting|gheebah|ghibah)\\b","\\b(?:backbiting|gheebah|ghibah|gossip(?:ing)?|speaking ill|talking behind (?:someones|his|her|their|my) back)\\b","\\bis (?:it )?(?:backbiting|gheebah|ghibah) if (?:it is|its|he|she) (?:true|there)\\b"],t.s)
B.arw=new A.X("backbiting",B.bAI,B.b,"The Prophet \ufdfa defined it: backbiting is talking about your brother in a way he does not like (Sahih Muslim 2589). When he was asked what if what is said is true of the brother, he explained that if it is true that is backbiting, and if it is not true it is slander.\n\nThe Qur'an forbids it with a vivid picture: do not spy on one another or backbite, would any of you like to eat the flesh of his dead brother (Qur'an 49:12). Scholars list narrow exceptions, such as warning someone about a real danger or asking a scholar about an injustice; for your own case, ask a scholar.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2589; Qur'an 49:12.","backbiting",!0,"")
B.aYx=s(["\\b(?:is )?(?:smiling|a smile|smile)\\b.*\\b(?:charity|sadaqah|sadaqa|sunnah|reward|islam)\\b","\\b(?:charity|sadaqah|sadaqa)\\b.*\\b(?:smile|smiling|kind word|small act|every good|without money|no money)\\b","\\bhow (?:can|do) i give (?:charity|sadaqah|sadaqa)\\b.*\\b(?:without money|no money|nothing|for free)\\b","\\b(?:every )?good (?:deed|act)\\b.*\\b(?:charity|sadaqah|sadaqa)\\b"],t.s)
B.arS=new A.X("smile-charity",B.aYx,B.b,"Abu Dharr reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, giving directions to a man lost in the land is charity, helping a man of poor sight is charity, and removing a rock, a thorn or a bone from the road is charity (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 1956, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nSo charity is not only money. Zakat itself is a fixed duty on wealth, and the Zakat calculator in the app is for that.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 1956, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/zakat]","small acts that are charity",!0,"")
B.bkG=s(["\\b(?:how|what) (?:do|can|should) (?:i|we) (?:increase|spread|grow) (?:love|brotherhood|friendship)\\b","\\b(?:spread(?:ing)?|giv(?:e|ing)) (?:the )?(?:salam|salaam|greeting|greetings)\\b","\\b(?:hadith|saying)\\b.*\\b(?:love one another|love each other)\\b","\\byou will not (?:enter paradise|believe)\\b.*\\blove\\b"],t.s)
B.ar7=new A.X("love-one-another-salam",B.bkG,B.b,'Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not direct you to something that, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread the greeting of peace among yourselves (Sahih Muslim 54).\n\nSo the Prophet \ufdfa named the way: spreading "As-salamu alaykum" among yourselves.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 54.',"love and greeting",!0,"")
B.b4p=s(["\\b(?:why|what is the) (?:benefit|reward|importance|value|point) (?:of )?(?:dhikr|remembering allah|remembrance)\\b","\\b(?:why|how) (?:should|do|must) (?:i|we) (?:do|make|say) dhikr\\b","\\b(?:living|alive)\\b.*\\b(?:dead)\\b.*\\b(?:dhikr|remembers?|remembering|praises?)\\b","\\bwhat is dhikr\\b"],t.s)
B.anD=new A.X("dhikr-living-dead",B.b4p,B.b,"Dhikr means remembering Allah: with the tongue (saying His praise), and with the heart. The Qur'an says: remember Me and I will remember you (Qur'an 2:152).\n\nAbu Musa reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the example of the one who remembers his Lord compared to the one who does not is that of a living creature compared to a dead one (Sahih al-Bukhari 6407).\n\nThe Tasbeeh counter and the Dhikr and Du'a screen are in the app.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:152; Sahih al-Bukhari 6407.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/tasbeeh]","dhikr",!0,"")
B.bss=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|prayer)\\b.*\\b(?:yunus|yunis|jonah|dhun nun|dhul nun|whale|fish)\\b","\\b(?:yunus|yunis|jonah|dhun nun|dhul nun)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|said|prayed|called)\\b","\\bla ilaha illa anta subhanaka\\b","\\bdua (?:when|for) (?:i am |im |in )?(?:distress|trouble|hardship|difficulty|anguish)\\b"],t.s)
B.ao7=new A.X("yunus-dua",B.bss,B.b,"When Prophet Yunus was in the darkness of the whale, the Qur'an records his call: there is no god but You, glory be to You, I was among the wrongdoers (Qur'an 21:87), and says that Allah answered him and saved him (Qur'an 21:88).\n\nSa'd reported the Prophet \ufdfa said: the supplication of Dhun-Nun when he supplicated in the belly of the whale was \"There is none worthy of worship except You, glory be to You, I was among the wrongdoers\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3505, sahih per al-Albani), and that no Muslim calls on Allah with it for anything except that Allah answers him.\n\nIn Arabic: La ilaha illa anta subhanaka inni kuntu min adh-dhalimin.\n\nSource: Qur'an 21:87, 21:88; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3505, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/adhkar]","dua of Yunus",!0,"")
B.biY=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|explain|meaning of) (?:tawakkul|tawakul|trust in allah|reliance on allah)\\b","\\b(?:tawakkul|tawakul)\\b.*\\b(?:action|effort|work|do (?:my )?part|tie|camel)\\b","\\b(?:tie|tying)\\b.*\\bcamel\\b","\\bshould i (?:just )?(?:do nothing|rely on allah|trust allah)\\b.*\\b(?:effort|try|work|means)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqV=new A.X("tawakkul-tie-camel",B.biY,B.b,"A man asked the Prophet \ufdfa whether he should tie his camel and rely on Allah or leave it loose and rely on Allah. He answered \"Tie it and rely on Allah\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2517, hasan per Darussalam).\n\nThat is the usual meaning scholars give of tawakkul: do the means that are in your hand, then put the result with Allah. The Qur'an says: when you have decided, then rely on Allah (Qur'an 3:159).\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2517, hasan per Darussalam; Qur'an 3:159.","tawakkul",!0,"")
B.bqV=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|benefit|benefits|virtue|virtues|reward|importance|meaning) (?:of )?(?:ayat|ayah|aya) (?:al )?kursi\\b","\\bayat(?:ul)? ?kursi\\b","\\bthrone verse\\b","\\b(?:verse|ayah|ayat) of the throne\\b"],t.s)
B.anN=new A.X("ayat-kursi-benefit",B.bqV,B.b,"Ayat al-Kursi is verse 255 of Surah Al-Baqarah (Qur'an 2:255), the verse of the Throne. Abu Hurayrah was told this by a thief, and the Prophet \ufdfa confirmed it was true: Abu Hurayrah was taught that reciting Ayat al-Kursi at bedtime means Allah appoints a guard and no devil comes near until morning (Sahih al-Bukhari 2311).\n\nI do not give other rewards here beyond this report.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:255; Sahih al-Bukhari 2311.\n[GO:/quran]","Ayat al-Kursi",!0,"")
B.brX=s(["\\b(?:forgot|forget|forgotten|forgetting) to say bismillah\\b","\\bwhat if (?:i |you )?forget to (?:mention|say) (?:allahs? name|bismillah)\\b.*\\b(?:eat|eating|food|meal)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|what to say|say) after (?:eating|finishing (?:a )?meal|food|a meal)\\b","\\b(?:alhamdulillah|alhamdu lillah|alhamdu lillahi) (?:alladhi|allazi|lladhi) at amani\\b"],t.s)
B.arF=new A.X("eat-after-forgot-bismillah",B.brX,B.b,"If you forget to say Bismillah at the start of the meal: Aisha reported the Prophet \ufdfa said when one of you eats he should mention Allah's name, and if he forgets to do so at the beginning he should say \"In the name of Allah at the beginning and at the end of it\" (Sunan Abu Dawud 3767, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nAfter the meal: Mu'adh ibn Anas reported the Prophet \ufdfa said whoever eats food and then says \"All praise is due to Allah who fed me this and granted it to me without any strength or power from me\", his earlier sins will be forgiven (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3458, hasan per al-Albani).\n\nAnd for children and everyone at the table: the Prophet told the boy Umar ibn Abi Salamah to mention the name of Allah, eat with his right hand, and eat from what is nearer to him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5376).\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 3767, sahih per al-Albani; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3458, hasan per al-Albani; Sahih al-Bukhari 5376.","etiquette of eating",!0,"")
B.b7K=s(["\\b(?:someone|somebody|person|friend|mother|father|mum|mom|dad|brother|sister|family|relative|parent|grandmother|grandfather|he|she|they) (?:is|was|are|who is|whos) (?:sick|ill|unwell|in hospital|not well)\\b.*\\b(?:say|saying|prayer|dua|du a|supplication|comfort|feel better|get well|cheer|help)\\b","\\b(?:what|which) (?:can|should|do|to) (?:i|you|we)? ?(?:say|recite|read|pray|ask)\\b.*\\b(?:sick|ill|unwell|patient)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|prayer|saying)\\b.*\\b(?:for|to)\\b.*\\b(?:sick|ill|unwell|patient|get well|recover|healing|heal)\\b","\\b(?:visit(?:ing)?|comfort(?:ing)?|cheer(?:ing)?)\\b.*\\b(?:sick|ill|unwell|patient|hospital)\\b","\\b(?:sick|ill|unwell)\\b.*\\b(?:feel better|get well|get better|recover|recovery)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)s? (?:for|when) (?:sickness|illness|being sick|an illness|a sick|someone sick|sick)\\b","\\bget well (?:soon )?(?:message|dua|words|wishes)\\b"],t.s)
B.bkJ=s(["\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|zakat|janazah|funeral|salah|prayers? (?:when|while|if) (?:i|im|i am))\\b"],t.s)
B.ap4=new A.X("sick-visit-comfort",B.b7K,B.bkJ,"Yes. Visiting the sick is a duty of a Muslim to a Muslim: al-Bara' reported that the Prophet \ufdfa commanded us to visit the sick, follow the funeral procession, answer the sneezer, fulfil the vow, help the poor, accept the invitation and greet everybody (Sahih Muslim 2066).\n\nWhen you visit, make good du'a: Umm Salamah reported the Prophet \ufdfa said when you visit the sick or the dead, say good things, because the angels say Amen to whatever you say (Sahih Muslim 919).\n\nA du'a the Prophet \ufdfa used for the sick: Aisha reported that he used to pass his right hand over the place of ailment and say \"O Allah, Lord of the people, remove the trouble and heal the patient, for You are the Healer, no healing is of any avail but Yours, a healing that leaves behind no ailment\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 5743).\n\nIn Arabic: Allahumma rabban-nas, adhhibil-ba's, washfi anta ash-Shafi, la shifa'a illa shifa'uk, shifa'an la yughadiru saqama. You can also simply ask Allah to heal them in your own words, and be kind and gentle with the person.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2066, 919; Sahih al-Bukhari 5743.\n[GO:/adhkar]","visiting and praying for the sick",!0,"")
B.b9O=s(["\\bsayyid(?:ul|ul-| al| ul)? ?istighfar\\b","\\b(?:best|greatest|master|most (?:superior|excellent)) (?:way|dua|du a|words?|form)?\\s*(?:of|for)? ?(?:asking )?(?:for )?(?:forgiveness|istighfar|repentance)\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|should i say for|do i say for) (?:the )?(?:dua|du a)? ?(?:for|of) (?:forgiveness|istighfar)\\b","\\bdua (?:for|to ask) forgiveness\\b","\\bhow (?:do|can|should) i ask (?:allah )?for forgiveness\\b"],t.s)
B.aq9=new A.X("istighfar-sayyid",B.b9O,B.b,"The Prophet \ufdfa called one du'a the best way of asking forgiveness. Shaddad ibn Aws reported: the most superior way of asking forgiveness is to say \"O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, I keep Your covenant and promise as best I can, I seek refuge in You from the evil I have done, I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306).\n\nHe added that whoever says it with firm faith in the day and dies that day before evening is among the people of Paradise, and likewise at night. Starting words: Allahumma anta Rabbi la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduka.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6306.\n[GO:/adhkar]","asking forgiveness",!0,"")
B.aVI=s(["\\bhow (?:do|can|should|to) (?:i )?(?:repent|make tawbah|do tawbah|make tawba|do tawba)\\b","\\b(?:what is|whats|meaning of|explain) (?:tawbah|tawba|repentance)\\b","\\b(?:will|does|would|can) allah forgive (?:me|my sins|everything|any sin|big sins|a sinner)\\b","\\bconditions? of (?:tawbah|tawba|repentance)\\b","\\bi (?:committed|did|made) (?:a )?(?:big |major )?sin\\b.*\\b(?:forgive|forgiven|repent|tawbah)\\b"],t.s)
B.aob=new A.X("tawbah-repent",B.aVI,B.b,"Repentance (tawbah) means turning back to Allah. The Qur'an invites it sincerely: turn to Allah in sincere repentance (Qur'an 66:8), and says Allah loves those who repent (Qur'an 2:222).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa described Allah's joy at it: Anas reported that Allah is more pleased with the repentance of a servant who turns to Him than a man on a camel in a waterless desert who loses it with his food and drink and then finds it (Sahih Muslim 2747).\n\nScholars usually list the parts of repentance as: stop the sin, feel regret, resolve not to return, and, if someone's right was wronged, return it or ask their pardon. That list is the scholars' summary, not a hadith quotation. For a specific sin, ask a scholar.\n\nSource: Qur'an 66:8, 2:222; Sahih Muslim 2747.\n[GO:/adhkar]","repentance",!0,"")
B.bxC=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|meaning of|explain|define) (?:sabr|patience|being patient)\\b","\\b(?:how|why) (?:do|can|should|to) (?:i )?(?:have|be|stay|keep|show|practise|practice) (?:sabr|patient|patience)\\b","\\b(?:sabr|patience)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|hadith|reward|hardship|trial|test)\\b","\\bhow to (?:cope|deal) with (?:hardship|trials|tests|difficult times)\\b"],t.s)
B.bw7=s(["\\bfast\\w*\\b"],t.s)
B.anZ=new A.X("sabr-patience",B.bxC,B.bw7,"Sabr is patience: holding yourself steady in hardship, in obedience and away from sin. The Qur'an says: seek help through patience and prayer, for Allah is with the patient (Qur'an 2:153).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa taught that a believer's affairs are all good: if he has an occasion for delight he thanks Allah and there is good in it, and if he gets into trouble and endures it patiently there is good in it (Sahih Muslim 2999). And nobody is given a blessing better and greater than patience (Sahih al-Bukhari 1469).\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:153; Sahih Muslim 2999; Sahih al-Bukhari 1469.","patience",!0,"")
B.byo=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:hasad|envy|jealousy)\\b","\\b(?:hasad|envy|envious|jealous|jealousy)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|hadith|sin|haram|cure|stop|remove)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:stop|get rid of|overcome|remove|deal with) (?:hasad|envy|jealousy)\\b","\\bwhat to do if i am (?:jealous|envious)\\b"],t.s)
B.apD=new A.X("hasad-envy",B.byo,B.b,"Hasad is envy: disliking a blessing someone has, and wishing it were taken from them. It is different from wishing for the same good for yourself, which scholars do not count as hasad.\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa said: beware of suspicion, do not look for others' faults, do not spy, do not envy one another, and do not desert one another, but be servants of Allah and brothers (Sahih al-Bukhari 6064). Scholars advise giving thanks for what you have and praying for good for the other person; that advice is the scholars' guidance, not a hadith quotation.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6064.","envy",!0,"")
B.aUD=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:kibr|kibar|arrogance|pride)\\b","\\b(?:kibr|arrogance|arrogant|pride)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|hadith|sin|paradise|haram)\\b","\\bis (?:it )?(?:haram|a sin) to be (?:proud|arrogant)\\b","\\b(?:atom|mustard seed) of (?:pride|arrogance)\\b"],t.s)
B.asy=new A.X("kibr-pride",B.aUD,B.b,"Ibn Mas'ud reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: he who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride will not enter Paradise (Sahih Muslim 91). A man asked whether liking fine clothes and shoes counts. The Prophet \ufdfa answered that Allah is beautiful and loves beauty, and that pride is disdaining the truth and holding people in contempt (Sahih Muslim 91).\n\nSo taking care of how you look is not pride; rejecting the truth and looking down on people is.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 91.","pride",!0,"")
B.b6x=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:nifaq|hypocrisy|a hypocrite|munafiq|munafiqun)\\b","\\b(?:signs?|characteristics?|traits?) of (?:a )?(?:hypocrite|hypocrisy|munafiq|nifaq)\\b","\\bhypocrit\\w*\\b.*\\b(?:hadith|islam|signs?)\\b"],t.s)
B.att=new A.X("hypocrisy-signs",B.b6x,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is trusted he betrays the trust (Sahih al-Bukhari 33).\n\nScholars explain that this describes hypocrisy in conduct, and warn a believer to check himself against it; it is not a judgment you pass on another person's faith.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 33.","signs of hypocrisy",!0,"")
B.biQ=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:sadaqah|sadaqa|sadaqat) ?(?:jariyah|jariya)\\b","\\bongoing (?:charity|reward)\\b","\\bcontinuous charity\\b","\\bwhat (?:deeds|good) (?:continue|keep (?:giving|going)) after (?:death|you die)\\b","\\bdeeds? that continue after death\\b"],t.s)
B.aqx=new A.X("sadaqah-jariyah",B.biQ,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: when a man dies his deeds come to an end except three: recurring charity, knowledge from which people benefit, or a pious son who prays for him (Sahih Muslim 1631).\n\nSadaqah jariyah is the first: charity whose benefit keeps going, such as a well, a school or a masjid. Scholars give these as examples; the hadith names the category.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1631.\n[GO:/zakat]","ongoing charity",!0,"")
B.bey=s(["\\b(?:what|who) is a good (?:friend|companion)\\b","\\b(?:choose|choosing|pick|picking|find|finding) (?:good )?(?:friends|a friend|companions?)\\b","\\b(?:friends?|friendship|companions?)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|hadith|quran|influence|bad|evil|good)\\b"],t.s)
B.bAz=s(["\\b(?:opposite|boyfriend|girlfriend|dating)\\b"],t.s)
B.ap8=new A.X("good-friends",B.bey,B.bAz,"The Prophet \ufdfa gave a picture, reported by Abu Musa: a good companion and an evil one are like a person carrying musk and a person blowing a pair of bellows: the musk carrier gives you perfume, or you buy some or at least smell a good scent, while the bellows blower burns your clothes or you get a bad smell (Sahih al-Bukhari 5534).\n\nSo friends rub off on you. Choose people who remind you of Allah and are kind and honest.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5534.","good friends",!0,"")
B.aUO=s(["\\b(?:best|good|right|accepted|answered) (?:time|times|moment|moments|place|state) (?:to|for) (?:make |making |do |doing )?(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b","\\bwhen (?:is|are) (?:dua|du a|duas)\\b.*\\b(?:accepted|answered)\\b","\\bwhen (?:does|will) allah (?:accept|answer) (?:my )?(?:dua|du a)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a)\\b.*\\b(?:accepted|answered)\\b.*\\b(?:time|when|night|prostrat\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqQ=new A.X("dua-best-time",B.aUO,B.b,"Two reports are clear. Jabir reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: there is an hour in the night in which no Muslim asks Allah for good in this world and the next without Allah giving it to him, and that applies to every night (Sahih Muslim 757).\n\nAnd Abu Hurayrah reported: the nearest a servant comes to his Lord is when he is prostrating himself, so make du'a in it (Sahih Muslim 482).\n\nThe Qur'an also tells you Allah is near and answers: when My servants ask about Me, I am near, I answer the call of the caller when he calls (Qur'an 2:186).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 757, 482; Qur'an 2:186.\n[GO:/adhkar]","best times for dua",!0,"")
B.b4R=s(["\\bhow (?:do|can|should|to) (?:i )?(?:make|get|have) (?:my )?(?:dua|du a|duas|prayers?) (?:accepted|answered|work|come true)\\b","\\bwhy (?:is|isnt|isnt|was|wasnt) (?:my )?(?:dua|du a|duas) (?:not )?(?:accepted|answered)\\b","\\bwhy (?:does|did|do) allah (?:not|never|doesnt|doesnt) (?:answer|accept) (?:my )?(?:dua|du a|duas|prayers?)\\b","\\bdua (?:not|isnt|isnt) (?:answered|accepted)\\b"],t.s)
B.asK=new A.X("dua-answered",B.b4R,B.b,"The Qur'an says: call on Me and I will respond to you (Qur'an 40:60), and: I am near, I answer the call of the caller when he calls on Me (Qur'an 2:186).\n\nScholars teach that an answer can come in different forms: what you asked, something better, or something kept back for you. That teaching is the scholars' explanation, not a quotation I can name here. What the sources do say is to ask with certainty in Allah, with presence of heart, and to keep asking.\n\nIf a du'a seems unanswered, that does not mean you are rejected; stay patient and keep asking.\n\nSource: Qur'an 40:60, 2:186.\n[GO:/adhkar]","when dua seems unanswered",!0,"")
B.buv=s(["\\bhow (?:do|can|should|to) (?:i )?(?:give|offer|say|send|express|write) (?:my )?(?:condolences|sympathy)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i|can i) say (?:to|when) (?:someone|somebody|a person|a friend|my \\w+)?\\s*(?:who )?(?:lost|loses|lose|has lost|is grieving|is mourning|is sad)\\b","\\b(?:condolences|condolence)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|islamic|muslim|dua|say)\\b","\\bwhat to say (?:at|in) (?:a )?(?:funeral|death|bereavement)\\b"],t.s)
B.ar1=new A.X("condolences",B.buv,B.b,"The Prophet \ufdfa gave his own words when his daughter sent news that her child was dying. Usama ibn Zayd reported: he sent word to her that whatever Allah takes is His, whatever He gives is His, and everything with Him has a fixed term, so she should be patient and hope for Allah's reward (Sahih al-Bukhari 1284).\n\nMany people use words like these to console someone: that what Allah took belonged to Him, that He decides the term, and that patience is rewarded. Reported also in the same hadith: the Prophet \ufdfa wept, showing that grief is not wrong.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1284.","condolences",!0,"")
B.aPU=s(["\\b(?:wedding|marriage|nikah|newlywed|congratulat\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|say|words|wish|wishes|message|supplication)\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:wedding|marriage|nikah|newlywed|newly married|bride|groom)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:to|when|at) (?:a )?(?:newly ?weds?|someone (?:who )?(?:gets|got|is getting) married|wedding|marriage|nikah)\\b","\\bbaraka ?allahu laka\\b"],t.s)
B.aPJ=s(["\\b(?:haram|ruling|age|conditions?|rights?|divorce)\\b"],t.s)
B.aox=new A.X("wedding-dua",B.aPU,B.aPJ,"Abu Hurayrah reported how the Prophet \ufdfa congratulated a man on his marriage: he said \"May Allah bless for you and may He bless on you and combine both of you in good\" (Sunan Abu Dawud 2130, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nIn Arabic: Baraka Allahu laka wa baraka 'alayka wa jama'a baynakuma fi khayr.\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 2130, sahih per al-Albani.","wedding du'a",!0,"")
B.b3R=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|dhikr|words?|what to say)\\b.*\\b(?:fear|afraid|scared|terrified|danger|threat|worry|worried)\\b","\\b(?:fear|afraid|scared|terrified|danger)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|what to say|say)\\b","\\bhasbunallah\\b","\\bhasbiyallah\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say when (?:i am |im |i m )?(?:scared|afraid|frightened)\\b"],t.s)
B.aSY=s(["\\b(?:nightmare|dream|anxiety|haram|ruling)\\b"],t.s)
B.anP=new A.X("hasbunallah-fear",B.b3R,B.aSY,"Ibn Abbas reported: \"Allah is sufficient for us and He is the best disposer of affairs\" was said by Abraham when he was thrown into the fire, and by Muhammad when people told them an army was gathering against them, and it only increased their faith (Sahih al-Bukhari 4563).\n\nThe words are from the Qur'an (Qur'an 3:173). In Arabic: Hasbunallahu wa ni'mal wakil.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 4563; Qur'an 3:173.\n[GO:/adhkar]","words for fear",!0,"")
B.aOe=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|words?|what to say|what should i say)\\b.*\\b(?:angry|anger|furious|rage|mad)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say when (?:i am |im |i m |i get |i feel )?(?:angry|furious|mad)\\b","\\b(?:angry|anger)\\b.*\\b(?:audhu|auzu|seek refuge|a udhu)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:control|calm|stop|manage) (?:my )?(?:anger|temper)\\b"],t.s)
B.ap6=new A.X("anger-refuge",B.aOe,B.b,'Sulayman ibn Surad reported that two men were abusing each other before the Prophet \ufdfa and one became furious with his face turning red. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "I know a word which, if he said it, would make his anger go away: I seek refuge with Allah from Satan, the outcast" (Sahih al-Bukhari 6115).\n\nIn Arabic: A\'udhu billahi minash-shaytanir-rajim. Another report in the same collection says the strong person is the one who controls himself in anger (the strong is not the one who overcomes people by strength, but the one who controls himself while in anger (Sahih al-Bukhari 6114)).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6115, 6114.',"when angry",!0,"")
B.aOW=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|life of|about) (?:aisha|aishah|ayesha|ayisha|a isha)\\b","\\b(?:aisha|aishah|ayesha)\\b.*\\b(?:wife|prophet|who|mother of the believers|scholar)\\b"],t.s)
B.b8M=s(["\\b(?:age|married at|marriage age|nine|six)\\b"],t.s)
B.aov=new A.X("aisha",B.aOW,B.b8M,"Aisha was a wife of the Prophet \ufdfa and the daughter of Abu Bakr. The Prophet \ufdfa died in her house, leaning on her chest (Sahih al-Bukhari 4449).\n\nAbu Musa reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the superiority of Aisha to other women is like the superiority of tharid, an Arabic dish, to other meals (Sahih al-Bukhari 3769).\n\nShe narrated a large number of hadith and is one of the most important sources of knowledge about the Prophet's \ufdfa home life.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 3769.","Aisha bint Abi Bakr",!0,"")
B.bkt=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|meaning of|explain|define) (?:the )?(?:adhan|azan|athan|iqamah|iqama|call to prayer)\\b","\\bhow (?:is|does) (?:the )?(?:adhan|azan|athan|iqamah|iqama) (?:said|go|work)\\b","\\bdifference between (?:the )?(?:adhan|azan|athan) and (?:the )?(?:iqamah|iqama)\\b"],t.s)
B.aof=new A.X("adhan-meaning",B.bkt,B.b,"The adhan is the call to prayer, and the iqamah is the call made when the prayer is about to start. Anas reported that Bilal was ordered to pronounce the adhan by saying its wordings twice and the iqamah by saying its wordings once (Sahih al-Bukhari 603).\n\nI am not giving the wording here; the Prayer screen has the times, and ask me if you want the sources for the wording.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 603.\n[GO:/prayer]","adhan and iqamah",!0,"")
B.bBh=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|what (?:to|do i|should i) say)\\b.*\\b(?:after|when (?:i )?hear|hearing|listening to)\\b.*\\b(?:adhan|azan|athan|call to prayer|muadhdhin|muezzin)\\b","\\b(?:after|when (?:i )?hear|hearing)\\b.*\\b(?:adhan|azan|athan|call to prayer)\\b.*\\b(?:say|dua|du a)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|reply|respond|answer) (?:when|to) (?:the )?(?:adhan|azan|athan|muadhdhin|muezzin)\\b","\\bwasilah\\b"],t.s)
B.arP=new A.X("adhan-dua",B.bBh,B.b,'When you hear the adhan, repeat what the muadhdhin says. Abdullah ibn Amr reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: when you hear the muadhdhin, repeat what he says, then send blessings on me, for whoever sends one blessing on me Allah sends ten on him, then ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, a rank in Paradise (Sahih Muslim 384).\n\nAfter the adhan, Jabir reported: whoever after hearing the adhan says "O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and of the prayer to be established, give Muhammad the Wasilah and the virtue, and raise him to the praised station You promised him", my intercession for him will be allowed on the Day of Resurrection (Sahih al-Bukhari 614).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 384; Sahih al-Bukhari 614.\n[GO:/adhkar]',"what to say at the adhan",!0,"")
B.aQg=s(["\\bhow many (?:rakat|rakats|rakah|rakahs|raka ?ah|rakaat|rakaats|units|rak ahs?) (?:is|are|in|for|do|does|of) (?:the )?(?:fajr|dawn|morning)\\b","\\b(?:fajr|dawn)\\b.*\\bhow many (?:rakat|rakats|rakah|rakahs|raka ?ah|rakaat|units)\\b","\\bfajr (?:rakat|rakats|rakah|rakahs|rakaat)\\b","\\bsunnah (?:of )?fajr\\b"],t.s)
B.as5=new A.X("rakats-fajr",B.aQg,B.b,"Fajr has two rak'ahs as the obligatory prayer, and the Prophet \ufdfa prayed two more rak'ahs of sunnah before it. Aisha reported he said: the two rak'ahs at dawn are better than this world and what it contains (Sahih Muslim 725).\n\nThe app's Prayer guide shows how each prayer is performed. This answer is the general position; the schools agree on two obligatory rak'ahs.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 725.\n[GO:/prayer]","Fajr rakats",!0,"")
B.b8R=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|meaning of|explain|define) (?:the )?(?:kalimah|kalima|shahada|shahadah|la ilaha illallah|la ilaha illa allah|tawhid statement)\\b","\\b(?:best|greatest|most (?:virtuous|beloved|excellent)) (?:dhikr|remembrance|words?|phrase|statement)\\b","\\bmeaning of la ilaha illa ?(?:allah|allah)\\b","\\bwhat does la ilaha illallah mean\\b"],t.s)
B.apz=new A.X("best-dhikr-tawhid",B.b8R,B.b,"La ilaha illa Allah means there is no god but Allah. The Qur'an says: know that there is no god but Allah (Qur'an 47:19).\n\nJabir reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the best remembrance is \"there is none worthy of worship except Allah\" and the best supplication is \"All praise is due to Allah\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3383, hasan per Darussalam). And 'Uthman reported: he who died knowing that there is no god but Allah entered Paradise (Sahih Muslim 26).\n\nScholars explain that knowing it means understanding and acting on it, not saying it alone.\n\nSource: Qur'an 47:19; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3383, hasan per Darussalam; Sahih Muslim 26.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/tasbeeh]","La ilaha illa Allah",!0,"")
B.b6M=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|meaning of|what does|explain) (?:the )?(?:subhanallah|subhan allah|subhanallahi|subhan allah|tasbeeh|tasbih)\\b","\\bwhat does subhan ?allah mean\\b","\\b(?:benefit|reward|virtue) of (?:saying )?(?:subhanallah|subhan allah|alhamdulillah)\\b","\\bwhat does alhamdulillah mean\\b"],t.s)
B.apt=new A.X("subhanallah-meaning",B.b6M,B.b,'Subhan Allah means glory be to Allah: declaring Him far above any fault or likeness. Alhamdulillah means all praise is for Allah.\n\nAbu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: there are two expressions, light on the tongue, heavy in the balance and dear to the Merciful: "Subhan Allah al-Azim" and "Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi" (Sahih al-Bukhari 6406). Abu Malik al-Ash\'ari reported Alhamdulillah fills the scale, and Subhan Allah and Alhamdulillah fill what is between the heavens and the earth (Sahih Muslim 223).\n\nThe Tasbeeh counter in the app is for these.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6406; Sahih Muslim 223.\n[GO:/tasbeeh]\n[GO:/adhkar]',"Subhan Allah and Alhamdulillah",!0,"")
B.bwc=s(["\\b(?:what (?:are|is)|who (?:are|is)|explain|tell me about) (?:the )?(?:jinn|jinns|djinn|jinni)\\b","\\bare (?:jinn|jinns|djinn) (?:real|in the quran)\\b","\\b(?:jinn|jinns|djinn)\\b.*\\b(?:made of|created from|created|fire|quran)\\b"],t.s)
B.bto=s(["\\b(?:possess\\w*|exorcis\\w*|ruqyah|ruqya|black magic|sihr|magic)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqu=new A.X("jinn-what-are",B.bwc,B.bto,"The jinn are a creation of Allah, unseen by us and given free will like humans. The Qur'an says Allah created humankind and jinn only to worship Him (Qur'an 51:56), and that the jinn were created from smokeless fire (Qur'an 55:15).\n\nThere is a surah named after them, Surah Al-Jinn, which begins with a group of them hearing the Qur'an and saying it is a wonderful recitation (Qur'an 72:1). Some of them believe and some do not.\n\nI do not give details beyond what the Qur'an states, and I do not diagnose possession or magic. For that, speak to a scholar.\n\nSource: Qur'an 51:56, 55:15, 72:1.","the jinn",!0,"")
B.byS=s(["\\b(?:what (?:is|are)|meaning of|explain) (?:a |the )?(?:hasanat|hasanah|hasana|good deeds?)\\b","\\bhow many (?:hasanat|hasanah|rewards?) (?:for|do i get)\\b","\\b(?:ten|10) (?:times|fold) (?:reward|hasanat|good)\\b","\\bwhat is the reward for (?:a )?good deeds?\\b"],t.s)
B.aoq=new A.X("hasanat-reward",B.byS,B.b,"Hasanat (singular hasanah) are good deeds and their reward. The Qur'an says: whoever brings a good deed will have ten times the like of it (Qur'an 6:160), and whoever brings an evil deed is only paid the like of it.\n\nSo a good deed is multiplied, and a sin is counted as one. I am not giving counts for specific deeds here.\n\nSource: Qur'an 6:160.","hasanat",!0,"")
B.b8Z=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:knowledge|study|studying|exam|exams|test|tests|school|memoris\\w*|memoriz\\w*|learning|homework)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:before|when) (?:i )?(?:study|studying|an exam|a test|learn|learning|taking an exam)\\b","\\bdua before (?:an )?(?:exam|test|studying)\\b","\\brabbi (?:zidni|zidnee) ilma\\b"],t.s)
B.atr=new A.X("dua-knowledge-exam",B.b8Z,B.b,"The Qur'an gives the du'a: and say, \"My Lord, increase me in knowledge\" (Qur'an 20:114).\n\nProphet Musa asked Allah for ease when given a hard task: my Lord, expand my chest, ease my task for me, and untie the knot from my tongue so they may understand my speech (Qur'an 20:25-28). Many students use these words before an exam or a hard task.\n\nMaking the effort comes first and the du'a goes with it; I am not citing a hadith for exam du'as.\n\nSource: Qur'an 20:114, 20:25-28.\n[GO:/adhkar]","dua for knowledge and exams",!0,"")
B.aT6=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a)\\b.*\\b(?:rizq|rizk|provision|sustenance|wealth|money|income|job|work)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|can|should|to) (?:i )?(?:increase|get|ask for|seek) (?:my )?(?:rizq|rizk|provision|sustenance)\\b","\\b(?:what is|meaning of|explain) (?:rizq|rizk)\\b","\\bwho provides (?:for )?(?:us|everyone|sustenance)\\b"],t.s)
B.bc_=s(["\\b(?:debt|haram|riba|interest)\\b"],t.s)
B.app=new A.X("rizq-provision",B.aT6,B.bc_,"Rizq is what Allah provides: money, food, health, family and more. The Qur'an says there is no creature on earth but its provision is on Allah (Qur'an 11:6), and that whoever has taqwa, Allah makes a way out for him and provides for him from where he does not expect (Qur'an 65:2-3).\n\nSeeking provision is a duty of effort, and trust in Allah goes with it. Ali reported a du'a the Prophet \ufdfa taught: \"O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your prohibited, and make me independent of all besides You by Your grace\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam), and he said Allah would fulfil even a mountain of debt.\n\nSource: Qur'an 11:6, 65:2-3; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam.\n[GO:/adhkar]","rizq",!0,"")
B.aPR=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:debt|debts|loan|owe|owing|in debt)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:when|if) (?:i am |im |i m )?in debt\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:pay|get out of|repay) (?:my )?debts? (?:islam|islamic|dua|with allah)\\b"],t.s)
B.bd_=s(["\\b(?:interest|riba|haram|ruling|mortgage)\\b"],t.s)
B.at4=new A.X("dua-debt",B.aPR,B.bd_,"Ali reported that the Prophet \ufdfa taught this du'a: \"O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your prohibited, and make me independent of all besides You by Your grace\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam), and said that if you had a debt like a mountain, Allah would fulfil it for you.\n\nIn Arabic: Allahumma-kfini bihalalika 'an haramik, wa aghnini bifadlika 'amman siwak. The Prophet \ufdfa also sought refuge from being heavily in debt, in a du'a recorded in Sahih al-Bukhari 6369. Paying what you owe, with the effort of earning, goes with the du'a.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam.\n[GO:/adhkar]","dua for debt",!0,"")
B.bxs=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|what (?:to|do i|should i) say)\\b.*\\b(?:new clothes|new clothing|new garment|new dress|new shirt|new shoes|wearing something new|put(?:ting)? on (?:something )?new|wear(?:ing)? (?:new|clothes))\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:when|if) (?:i )?(?:wear|put on|buy) (?:something )?new\\b"],t.s)
B.as3=new A.X("dua-new-clothes",B.bxs,B.b,'Abu Sa\'id al-Khudri reported: when the Prophet \ufdfa put on a new garment he mentioned it by name, whether turban or shirt, and said "O Allah, praise be to You as You have clothed me with it, I ask You for its good and the good of that for which it was made, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of that for which it was made" (Sunan Abu Dawud 4020, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nAbu Nadrah added that when a Companion put on a new garment, he was told: may you wear it out, and may Allah give you another in its place.\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 4020, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/adhkar]',"dua for new clothes",!0,"")
B.bnO=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|what (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|do))\\b.*\\b(?:bad dream|bad dreams|nightmare|nightmares|scary dream|evil dream|disturbing dream)\\b","\\b(?:bad dream|bad dreams|nightmare|nightmares|scary dream)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|islamic|dua|what to do|say|sunnah)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) do (?:after|if i have|when i have|when i get) (?:a )?(?:bad dream|nightmare)\\b"],t.s)
B.asx=new A.X("dua-bad-dream",B.bnO,B.b,"Abu Qatada reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: a good dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan, so if anyone sees something he dislikes in a dream, when he wakes he should blow three times on his left side and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, and it will not harm him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5747).\n\nIn Arabic the refuge is: A'udhu billahi min sharri ma ra'ayt. Do not fear it: the hadith says it will not harm you.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5747.","after a bad dream",!0,"")
B.aTa=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|how)\\b.*\\b(?:protect\\w*|safe\\w*|refuge|defen\\w*|guard)\\b.*\\b(?:shaytan|satan|devil|whisper\\w*|waswas|waswasa)\\b","\\b(?:protect|protection|refuge|safe)\\b.*\\b(?:from|against)\\b.*\\b(?:shaytan|satan|the devil)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:stop|resist|fight|defeat|beat|avoid) (?:the )?(?:shaytan|satan|devil|whispers|waswas)\\b","\\bwaswas(?:a)?\\b"],t.s)
B.aYZ=s(["\\b(?:house|home|sleep|dream)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoA=new A.X("dua-shaytan-protection",B.aTa,B.aYZ,"The Qur'an says: if an evil suggestion from Satan comes to you, seek refuge in Allah, for He is the Hearing, the Knowing (Qur'an 7:200). It also gives a du'a: my Lord, I seek refuge in You from the whisperings of the devils (Qur'an 23:97).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa taught the same words to someone furious: Sahih al-Bukhari 6115. So \"A'udhu billahi minash-shaytanir-rajim\" is the first thing to say. The last three surahs, Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq and An-Nas, are also commonly recited for refuge; I am not citing a hadith for that here.\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:200, 23:97; Sahih al-Bukhari 6115.\n[GO:/adhkar]","protection from Shaytan",!0,"")
B.b99=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:newborn|new born|new baby|newly born|baby (?:is )?born|birth)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|should i) (?:name|choose a name for) (?:a |my |the )?(?:baby|child|son|daughter|newborn)\\b","\\bwhat (?:are|is) (?:the )?(?:best|good|recommended) (?:names?|name) (?:for|in|according to) (?:a )?(?:baby|child|islam|the prophet)\\b","\\bwhat to say (?:when|to) (?:someone|a friend|a person|a muslim)? ?(?:has|had|gets|got|having) a (?:baby|child|newborn)\\b","\\bislamic (?:naming|names?) (?:for|of) (?:a )?(?:baby|child)\\b","\\b(?:what is|whats|explain) (?:the )?aqiqah\\b"],t.s)
B.aqF=new A.X("dua-new-baby-name",B.b99,B.b,"Ibn Umar reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the names dearest to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman (Sahih Muslim 2132). Scholars also recommend a name with a good meaning and a good link to Allah's servants or prophets; that recommendation is the scholars' guidance, not a quotation.\n\nFor congratulating parents, Muslims commonly pray that Allah bless the child and make the parents grateful. I am not citing a hadith for that wording. For the aqiqah (a sacrifice on the seventh day), I have not checked a source to cite here, so please ask a scholar.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2132.","newborn and naming",!0,"")
B.bmm=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|prayer)\\b.*\\b(?:ibrahim|abraham|ibraheem)\\b","\\b(?:ibrahim|abraham|ibraheem)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|prayed|asked)\\b","\\b(?:who was|tell me about|story of|life of) (?:prophet )?(?:ibrahim|abraham|ibraheem)\\b"],t.s)
B.apQ=new A.X("dua-ibrahim",B.bmm,B.b,"Ibrahim is called Allah's friend, and the Qur'an gives his du'as. At the Ka'bah he and Ismail asked: our Lord, accept this from us, You are the Hearing, the Knowing (Qur'an 2:127). He prayed for the land to be safe and for his offspring to establish prayer (Qur'an 14:35-37), and asked forgiveness for himself and his parents (Qur'an 14:41).\n\nWhen he was thrown into the fire, he said \"Allah is sufficient for us and the best disposer of affairs\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 4563).\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:127, 14:35-37, 14:41.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Ibrahim",!0,"")
B.bh6=s(["\\b(?:story|tale|life) of (?:prophet )?(?:musa|moses|moosa)\\b","\\b(?:who was|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:musa|moses|moosa)\\b","\\b(?:musa|moses|moosa)\\b.*\\b(?:story|pharaoh|firaun|fir aun|red sea|staff|torah)\\b"],t.s)
B.as8=new A.X("story-musa",B.bh6,B.b,"Musa is the prophet named most often in the Qur'an. He was raised in Pharaoh's house, was sent to Pharaoh with signs, and led the Children of Israel out of Egypt (Qur'an 20:77). He spoke with Allah (Qur'an 4:164), and was given the Torah.\n\nThe full account is spread across many surahs, with a long telling in Surah Ta-Ha and Surah Al-Qasas. I am only giving a short outline; ask me about a part of it.\n\nSource: Qur'an 20:77, 4:164.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Musa",!0,"")
B.b7U=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:ihsan|ihsaan|excellence in faith)\\b","\\b(?:ihsan|ihsaan)\\b.*\\b(?:mean|hadith|jibril|gabriel|worship)\\b","\\bworship allah as if you (?:see|saw) (?:him|allah)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoI=new A.X("ihsan-meaning",B.b7U,B.b,"Ihsan means doing good with excellence, and in worship it means awareness that Allah sees you. In the hadith of Gabriel, Abu Hurayrah reported that the angel asked the Prophet \ufdfa about Ihsan, and he answered: to worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you cannot achieve this state, then to know that He sees you (Sahih al-Bukhari 50).\n\nIn the same hadith Gabriel asked about faith, which the Prophet \ufdfa described as belief in Allah, His angels, the meeting with Him, His messengers and the resurrection, and about Islam, which he described as worshipping Allah alone, prayer, zakat and fasting Ramadan.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 50.","ihsan",!0,"")
B.b9S=s(["^(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:halal|haram|halal and haram|haram and halal)$","^what (?:does )?(?:halal|haram) mean$","\\bhow (?:do|can) (?:i )?(?:know|tell) (?:if )?(?:something|it) is (?:halal|haram)\\b","\\bwhat (?:are|is) (?:the )?(?:doubtful|unclear|grey|gray) (?:matters|things|areas)\\b","\\bshubuhat\\b"],t.s)
B.ato=new A.X("halal-haram-general",B.b9S,B.b,"Halal means permitted and haram means forbidden. The Prophet \ufdfa said, as reported by An-Nu'man ibn Bashir: the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and in between are doubtful matters that most people do not know, so whoever avoids the doubtful has protected his religion and his honour (Sahih al-Bukhari 52).\n\nFor particular cases such as food, money or a product, ask me about that case; I answer from the Qur'an, hadith and the scholars' views, and I do not rule on your own situation.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 52.","halal and haram",!0,"")
B.aSN=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:bidah|bidaah|bida a|bid ah|innovation in (?:islam|religion))\\b","\\b(?:bidah|bidaah|innovation)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|hadith|religion|sin|mawlid|good)\\b","\\bis (?:there|it) (?:a )?good (?:bidah|innovation)\\b","\\bevery innovation is (?:misguidance|error)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqf=new A.X("bidah-innovation",B.aSN,B.b,"Bid'ah means innovation. Aisha reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: if somebody innovates something which is not in harmony with the principles of our religion, that thing is rejected (Sahih al-Bukhari 2697). And in his sermons, as Jabir reported, he said the best of speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the most evil affairs are the innovations, and every innovation is error (Sahih Muslim 867).\n\nScholars differ on what counts. Some say every new religious practice is bid'ah; others divide innovations into good and bad. The difference is in how the words \"every innovation\" are understood, so I do not label a particular practice. For a specific one, ask a scholar of your school.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2697; Sahih Muslim 867.","bid'ah",!0,"")
B.bm4=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:itikaf|i tikaf|e tikaf|etikaf|itikaaf)\\b","\\b(?:itikaf|i tikaf|etikaf)\\b.*\\b(?:how|rules|conditions|last ten|days|nights|reward|woman|women)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|to|can) (?:i )?(?:do|perform|make|observe) (?:itikaf|i tikaf|etikaf)\\b"],t.s)
B.ap0=new A.X("itikaf-seclusion",B.bm4,B.b,"I'tikaf is staying in the masjid for worship for a period, usually in the last days of Ramadan. Ibn Umar reported: Allah's Messenger \ufdfa used to practise i'tikaf in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan (Sahih al-Bukhari 2025).\n\nThe Qur'an mentions it in the verses on fasting, where it speaks of those in i'tikaf in the masjids (Qur'an 2:187).\n\nThe conditions (minimum time, leaving for needs, who may do it) differ between the schools, and I do not give one school's rules as the answer; ask a scholar of your school.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2025; Qur'an 2:187.\n[GO:/academy]","itikaf",!0,"")
B.aWX=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:rahmah|rahma|mercy in islam|compassion in islam)\\b","\\b(?:mercy|compassion|merciful)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|hadith|prophet|quran|allah)\\b","\\b(?:be|being) merciful\\b","\\bar rahman\\b.*\\bmean\\b"],t.s)
B.apS=new A.X("rahmah-mercy",B.aWX,B.b,"Rahmah is mercy. The Qur'an says Allah sent the Prophet \ufdfa as a mercy to the worlds (Qur'an 21:107).\n\nJarir reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: he who is not merciful to others will not be treated mercifully (Sahih al-Bukhari 6013).\n\nSo mercy is both something Allah shows to people and something people are told to show one another.\n\nSource: Qur'an 21:107; Sahih al-Bukhari 6013.","mercy",!0,"")
B.b7R=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:adl|justice|fairness)(?: in islam)?$","\\b(?:justice|fairness|just)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|allah|command)\\b","\\bbe just even (?:against|to)\\b","\\bwhat does islam say about justice\\b"],t.s)
B.atg=new A.X("adl-justice",B.b7R,B.b,"Adl is justice. The Qur'an says Allah commands justice and doing good (Qur'an 16:90), and tells believers to stand firmly for justice as witnesses to Allah, even against themselves or their parents or relatives (Qur'an 4:135). It also says not to let hatred of a people lead you away from justice (Qur'an 5:8).\n\nSource: Qur'an 16:90, 4:135, 5:8.","justice",!0,"")
B.bv0=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:amanah|amana|trust in islam|a trust)\\b","\\b(?:amanah|amana)\\b","\\bkeep(?:ing)? (?:a )?(?:trust|promise|promises)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|hadith)\\b","\\b(?:what does islam say about|islam on) (?:keeping )?(?:promises|trust|being trustworthy)\\b"],t.s)
B.apu=new A.X("amanah-trust",B.bv0,B.b,"Amanah is a trust: whatever someone puts in your care, and every duty you hold. The Qur'an says Allah commands you to return trusts to their owners (Qur'an 4:58).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa listed betrayal of trust among the signs of a hypocrite (Sahih al-Bukhari 33).\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:58; Sahih al-Bukhari 33.","trust",!0,"")
B.aUh=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:qadr|qadar|qada|destiny|fate|predestination|taqdir)\\b","\\b(?:qadr|qadar|taqdir)\\b.*\\b(?:free will|choice|islam|belief|mean)\\b","\\bdo (?:we|humans|people) have free will\\b","\\bis (?:everything|my life) (?:written|predestined|destined)\\b"],t.s)
B.apH=new A.X("qadr-destiny",B.aUh,B.b,"Qadr is Allah's decree, one of the six articles of faith. The Qur'an says that everything has been created with a measure (Qur'an 54:49), and that no disaster strikes the earth or yourselves except that it is in a record before it is brought into being (Qur'an 57:22).\n\nMuslim scholars hold that this does not remove human choice or responsibility: people are accountable for what they choose. That is the scholars' position in general terms; the sources do not settle every question about how the two fit, and I do not go beyond them.\n\nSource: Qur'an 54:49, 57:22.","qadr",!0,"")
B.aPB=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:ikhlas|ikhlaas|sincerity)(?: in islam)?\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:be|have|get|become) sincere\\b","\\b(?:sincerity|ikhlas)\\b.*\\b(?:allah|worship|deeds|actions|intention)\\b"],t.s)
B.bfb=s(["\\b(?:surah|sura)\\b"],t.s)
B.as7=new A.X("ikhlas-sincerity",B.aPB,B.bfb,"Ikhlas is sincerity: doing worship purely for Allah. The Qur'an says people were only commanded to worship Allah, sincere to Him in religion (Qur'an 98:5), and tells the Prophet \ufdfa to worship Allah, making the religion sincerely His (Qur'an 39:2).\n\nThe opposite is riya, doing a deed to be seen by people. Ask me about it if you want.\n\nSource: Qur'an 98:5, 39:2.","sincerity",!0,"")
B.aUg=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|who is|who was|tell me about|explain) (?:shaytan|shaitan|satan|iblis|the devil|devil)\\b","\\bwhy (?:did|does) (?:shaytan|iblis|satan) (?:refuse|hate|rebel|disobey)\\b","\\b(?:iblis|shaytan)\\b.*\\b(?:adam|jinn|angel|fire|created|refuse)\\b"],t.s)
B.byt=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|protect\\w*|refuge|waswas\\w*|whisper\\w*|haram)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoS=new A.X("shaytan-iblis",B.aUg,B.byt,"Iblis is the one who refused when Allah told the angels to prostrate to Adam. The Qur'an says he refused and was arrogant and became one of the disbelievers (Qur'an 2:34), and that his reason was that he was made from fire while Adam was from clay (Qur'an 7:12).\n\nThe Qur'an calls Shaytan a clear enemy to humankind (Qur'an 35:6) and tells people to take him as an enemy. For what to say against his whispers, ask me for the du'a for protection.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:34, 7:12, 35:6.","Iblis and Shaytan",!0,"")
B.b0n=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain|who is) (?:a )?(?:shaheed|shahid|martyr|martyrdom)\\b","\\b(?:martyr|shaheed|shahid)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|paradise|reward|dead)\\b"],t.s)
B.aTV=s(["\\b(?:terror\\w*|suicide|bomb\\w*|attack)\\b"],t.s)
B.arK=new A.X("shahid-martyr",B.b0n,B.aTV,"Shahid means witness, and it is the word for a martyr. The Qur'an says not to think of those killed in the way of Allah as dead; they are alive with their Lord, provided for (Qur'an 3:169).\n\nI am not listing every kind of shahid or ruling on a particular case here; for that ask a scholar.\n\nSource: Qur'an 3:169.","shahid",!0,"")
B.aOI=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|explain|tell me about) (?:the )?(?:islamic|hijri|muslim) (?:calendar|year|months)\\b","\\bhow many months (?:are )?(?:in|are there in) (?:the )?(?:islamic|hijri|lunar) (?:year|calendar)\\b","\\b(?:hijri|islamic) (?:calendar|year)\\b.*\\b(?:start|begin|count|moon)\\b","\\bwhen does the (?:islamic|hijri) (?:year|calendar) (?:start|begin)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqr=new A.X("islamic-calendar",B.aOI,B.b,"The Islamic (Hijri) calendar is a lunar calendar of twelve months. The Qur'an says the number of months with Allah is twelve (Qur'an 9:36), four of them sacred.\n\nYears are counted from the Hijrah, the migration of the Prophet \ufdfa to Madinah. A lunar year is about eleven days shorter than a solar year, so Ramadan and the other months move through the seasons. The first month is Muharram.\n\nSource: Qur'an 9:36.\n[GO:/prayer]","the Islamic calendar",!0,"")
B.bnz=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|tell me|story of|who (?:are|were)|explain) (?:the )?(?:people|companions|youths?|young men|sleepers) of (?:the )?cave\\b","\\bashab (?:al )?kahf\\b","\\bseven sleepers\\b","\\b(?:story of|about) (?:the )?(?:cave|surah al kahf)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoy=new A.X("people-of-the-cave",B.bnz,B.b,"The story is told in Surah Al-Kahf, which begins by saying the youths of the cave were one of Allah's wonders (Qur'an 18:9). In outline: some young believers fled their people to protect their faith, took refuge in a cave, and Allah caused them to sleep for years (Qur'an 18:10-12). When they woke, they thought they had slept only a day or part of one (Qur'an 18:19), and the people of the town found out about them.\n\nThe Qur'an notes that people disagree about their number, and says Allah knows best (Qur'an 18:22). The lesson stressed is to rely on Allah and keep faith in hardship.\n\nSource: Qur'an 18:9, 18:10-12, 18:19, 18:22.\n[GO:/quran]","the People of the Cave",!0,"")
B.b4g=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:dhul|dhu al|zul|zul al|dhu l) ?qarnayn\\b","\\b(?:dhul|zul|dhu) ?qarnayn\\b","\\balexander the great\\b.*\\b(?:quran|islam)\\b","\\bgog and magog\\b|\\byajuj\\b.*\\bmajuj\\b"],t.s)
B.asq=new A.X("dhul-qarnayn",B.b4g,B.b,"Dhul-Qarnayn is a righteous ruler whose story is in Surah Al-Kahf (Qur'an 18:83). The Qur'an says Allah gave him power on earth and means to everything (Qur'an 18:84), and that he travelled to the west and the east. He met a people who asked for protection from Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and he built a barrier against them (Qur'an 18:93-98), then said it was a mercy from his Lord.\n\nWho he was is a matter of difference among scholars, and I do not name him.\n\nSource: Qur'an 18:83, 18:84, 18:93-98.\n[GO:/quran]","Dhul-Qarnayn",!0,"")
B.bql=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) luqman\\b","\\bluqman\\b.*\\b(?:wisdom|advice|son|surah)\\b","\\bsurah luqman\\b","\\bluqmans (?:advice|wisdom)\\b"],t.s)
B.ar5=new A.X("luqman-wisdom",B.bql,B.b,"Luqman is a man to whom Allah gave wisdom (Qur'an 31:12), and the surah named after him records his advice to his son. He tells him not to associate anything with Allah, because shirk is a great wrong (Qur'an 31:13); to establish prayer, enjoin good and forbid evil and be patient (Qur'an 31:17); not to turn his cheek away from people in pride, and to be moderate in his walk and lower his voice (Qur'an 31:18-19).\n\nSource: Qur'an 31:12, 31:13, 31:17, 31:18-19.\n[GO:/quran]","Luqman",!0,"")
B.b7S=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:prophet )?(?:nuh|noah|nooh)\\b","\\b(?:nuh|noah|nooh)\\b.*\\b(?:ark|flood|boat|ship|people|story|prophet)\\b","\\bsurah nuh\\b"],t.s)
B.aqY=new A.X("prophet-nuh",B.b7S,B.b,"Nuh called his people to worship Allah alone for a very long time. The Qur'an says he stayed among them a thousand years less fifty (Qur'an 29:14), and Surah Nuh (surah 71) records how he called them night and day (Qur'an 71:5). Allah told him to build the ship (Qur'an 11:37), and the flood came (Qur'an 11:40).\n\nThe surah named after him gives his du'a for his people and the believers.\n\nSource: Qur'an 29:14, 71:5, 11:37, 11:40.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Nuh",!0,"")
B.aX_=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:prophet )?(?:ayyub|ayub)\\b","\\b(?:ayyub|ayub)\\b.*\\b(?:patience|illness|sickness|story|prophet|trial)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoH=new A.X("prophet-ayyub",B.aX_,B.b,"Ayyub is the Qur'an's example of patience in sickness and loss. He called to his Lord that harm had touched him and that He is the most merciful of the merciful (Qur'an 21:83), and Allah answered, removed his harm and gave him his family and more like them (Qur'an 21:84). Surah Sad also describes him as an excellent servant, one who constantly turned to Allah (Qur'an 38:44).\n\nSource: Qur'an 21:83, 21:84, 38:44.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Ayyub",!0,"")
B.aWB=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:prophet )?(?:sulayman|suleiman|sulaiman|solomon)\\b","\\b(?:sulayman|suleiman|solomon)\\b.*\\b(?:jinn|birds|ants|wind|kingdom|queen|bilqis|sheba|story)\\b","\\bqueen of sheba\\b|\\bbilqis\\b"],t.s)
B.asB=new A.X("prophet-sulayman",B.aWB,B.b,"Sulayman was a prophet and a king, the son of Dawud. The Qur'an says Allah gave him knowledge (Qur'an 27:15) and that he was given the language of the birds (Qur'an 27:16). His armies of jinn, men and birds were gathered before him (Qur'an 27:17), and he heard an ant tell the others to enter their homes (Qur'an 27:18). He also wrote to the queen of Saba, who came to believe (Qur'an 27:44).\n\nThe surah says all of this was by Allah's favour, and Sulayman asked to be grateful for it (Qur'an 27:19).\n\nSource: Qur'an 27:15, 27:16, 27:17, 27:18, 27:44, 27:19.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Sulayman",!0,"")
B.bm0=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:prophet )?(?:dawud|daud|dawood)\\b","\\b(?:dawud|dawood|prophet david)\\b.*\\b(?:psalms|zabur|goliath|jalut|iron|mountains|story)\\b"],t.s)
B.asL=new A.X("prophet-dawud",B.bm0,B.b,"Dawud was a prophet and a king. The Qur'an says Allah gave him the Zabur (Qur'an 4:163), that the mountains and birds joined him in glorifying Allah (Qur'an 38:18-19), and that Allah made iron soft for him (Qur'an 34:10). It also records that he killed Jalut (Goliath), and that Allah gave him kingdom and wisdom (Qur'an 2:251).\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:163, 38:18-19, 34:10, 2:251.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Dawud",!0,"")
B.bvd=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of|what is the story of|explain) (?:prophet )?(?:aadam)\\b","\\bprophet adam\\b","\\b(?:adam|aadam)\\b.*\\b(?:first man|created|clay|eve|hawwa|paradise|garden|tree|story)\\b","\\bwho was the first (?:man|human|person)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoe=new A.X("prophet-adam",B.bvd,B.b,"Adam is the first human being and a prophet. The Qur'an says Allah told the angels He would place a vicegerent on earth (Qur'an 2:30), taught Adam the names (Qur'an 2:31), and told the angels to prostrate to him; Iblis refused (Qur'an 2:34). Adam and his wife were told to live in the Garden but not to approach one tree (Qur'an 2:35); Shaytan made them slip, and they were sent down to the earth (Qur'an 2:36). Adam then received words from his Lord and Allah accepted his repentance (Qur'an 2:37).\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:30, 2:31, 2:34, 2:35, 2:36, 2:37.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Adam",!0,"")
B.aNF=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|whats) (?:the )?(?:opening|starting|first|istiftah|thana|sana) (?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b","\\bdua (?:of|for) (?:the )?(?:opening|istiftah|starting the prayer)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:after|between) (?:the )?(?:takbir|takbeer|allahu akbar)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|recite) (?:at|in) (?:the )?(?:start|beginning) of (?:the )?(?:prayer|salah|salat)\\b","\\ballahumma ba ?id (?:bayni|baini)\\b"],t.s)
B.asY=new A.X("opening-dua-prayer",B.aNF,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported that he asked the Prophet \ufdfa what he said in the pause between the takbir and the recitation, and the Prophet \ufdfa answered: \"O Allah, set me apart from my sins as You set the east and west apart from each other; O Allah, clean me from sins as a white garment is cleaned of dirt; O Allah, wash my sins with water, snow and hail\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 744).\n\nIn Arabic it begins: Allahumma ba'id bayni wa bayna khatayaya kama ba'adta baynal-mashriqi wal-maghrib. Other openings are reported too, and the schools differ on which they use; I do not pick one school's opening.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 744.\n[GO:/prayer]","opening du'a of prayer",!0,"")
B.bAD=s(["\\b(?:what (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|recite|do)|dua|du a|dhikr|adhkar)\\b.*\\bafter (?:the |each )?(?:prayer|salah|salat|namaz|fard prayer)\\b","\\bafter (?:the |each )?(?:prayer|salah|salat)\\b.*\\b(?:say|recite|dhikr|tasbih|tasbeeh|33)\\b","\\b(?:33|thirty three)\\b.*\\b(?:subhanallah|alhamdulillah|allahu akbar)\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|are) the (?:dhikr|adhkar|tasbeeh) after (?:salah|prayer)\\b"],t.s)
B.asC=new A.X("dhikr-after-prayer",B.bAD,B.b,'Abu Hurayrah reported that poor Companions complained that the wealthy had higher ranks because they gave more in charity. The Prophet \ufdfa answered: say "Subhan Allah", "Alhamdulillah" and "Allahu Akbar" thirty-three times each after every obligatory prayer (Sahih al-Bukhari 843).\n\nThe Tasbeeh counter in the app can count it. Different hadith give slightly different totals; I am giving the one cited here.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 843.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/tasbeeh]',"dhikr after prayer",!0,"")
B.btv=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|whats) (?:the )?(?:dua|du a|supplication) (?:in|during) (?:sujud|sajda|sajdah|prostration)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|do|ask|recite) (?:in|during) (?:sujud|sajda|sajdah|prostration)\\b","\\b(?:can i|may i|should i) (?:make|do) (?:dua|du a) (?:in|during) (?:sujud|sajda|prostration)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:get|become|be) (?:closer|close|near) (?:to )?allah\\b","\\bhow (?:do|can) i (?:gain|increase|build) (?:closeness|nearness) (?:to|with) allah\\b"],t.s)
B.ao6=new A.X("sujud-dua-closeness",B.btv,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the nearest a servant comes to his Lord is when he is prostrating himself, so make du'a in it (Sahih Muslim 482).\n\nThe Qur'an says the same: prostrate and draw near (Qur'an 96:19). So sujud is a time to ask Allah in your own words, in whatever language you speak, as the hadith says to make du'a in it. For other ways to get closer, the Qur'an says Allah is near and answers when called (Qur'an 2:186).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 482; Qur'an 96:19, 2:186.\n[GO:/adhkar]","nearness to Allah",!0,"")
B.b39=s(["\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i|should i) (?:memori[sz]e|memorise|hifz|learn by heart|revise)\\b.*\\b(?:quran|quran|koran)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:start|begin) (?:learning|memori[sz]ing|reading)\\b.*\\b(?:quran|quran)\\b","\\b(?:best|how to) (?:way|method) (?:to )?(?:memori[sz]e|learn)\\b.*\\b(?:quran|quran)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i|should i) (?:read|recite) (?:the )?(?:quran|quran)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit)\\b.*\\b(?:teach|teaching|learn|learning)\\b.*\\b(?:quran|quran)\\b"],t.s)
B.aRA=s(["\\b(?:without wudu|period|menstruat\\w*|touch\\w*|ruling|haram)\\b"],t.s)
B.apW=new A.X("learn-teach-quran",B.b39,B.aRA,"'Uthman reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the best among you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027).\n\nOn memorising, Abu Musa reported: commit yourself to the Qur'an, for by Him in whose Hand is my soul, it is more prone to escape than a camel in its tether (Sahih al-Bukhari 5033). The Qur'an says to recite it slowly and distinctly (Qur'an 73:4), and that Allah made it easy to remember (Qur'an 54:17).\n\nPractical points such as a daily portion, revision and a teacher are the scholars' and teachers' advice, not hadith; the Qur'an screen has the reader, and the daily portion guide is in the app.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5027, 5033; Qur'an 73:4, 54:17.\n[GO:/quran]","learning the Qur'an",!0,"")
B.aPd=s(["\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i|should i) (?:be|become|stay|remain) humble\\b","\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:humility|tawadu|tawaadu)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i|should i) forgive (?:someone|somebody|a person|them|him|her|people|others|my \\w+)\\b","\\b(?:forgiving|forgive) (?:others|people|someone)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|quran|hadith|reward|allah)\\b","\\bhow to let go of (?:anger|grudges?|resentment)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoV=new A.X("humility-forgiveness",B.aPd,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: charity does not decrease wealth, no one forgives another except that Allah increases his honour, and no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises his status (Sahih Muslim 2588).\n\nThe Qur'an asks believers to pardon and overlook, and says: would you not love that Allah forgive you (Qur'an 24:22)? It also praises those who restrain anger and pardon people (Qur'an 3:134).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2588; Qur'an 24:22, 3:134.","humility and forgiving others",!0,"")
B.brO=s(["\\b(?:can|may|is it allowed for|are) (?:a )?(?:women|woman|females?|ladies|girls?) (?:allowed )?(?:to )?(?:go|pray|attend|come|enter|visit)\\b.*\\b(?:mosque|masjid)\\b","\\b(?:women|woman|females?|ladies)\\b.*\\b(?:mosque|masjid)\\b.*\\b(?:allowed|permitted|pray|prayer|attend|jamaah|jummah|jumuah)\\b","\\bwomens? (?:section|area|prayer)\\b.*\\b(?:mosque|masjid)\\b"],t.s)
B.b6f=s(["\\b(?:period|menstruat\\w*|imam|lead|leader)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoo=new A.X("women-in-the-masjid",B.brO,B.b6f,"Ibn Umar reported that the Prophet \ufdfa said: do not stop Allah's women from going to Allah's mosques (Sahih al-Bukhari 900).\n\nSo women may go to the masjid. The scholars discuss conditions such as safety and dress, and say that for women the prayer at home is also valid; the schools differ in how they weigh these. I do not give a ruling on a particular situation.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 900.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-mosque]","women in the masjid",!0,"")
B.bhd=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:the )?(?:ummah|umma|ummah of muhammad|muslim ummah)\\b","\\b(?:ummah|umma)\\b.*\\b(?:mean|meaning|brotherhood|one body|united)\\b","\\bwhat does (?:the )?ummah mean\\b"],t.s)
B.arA=new A.X("ummah-meaning",B.bhd,B.b,"The ummah is the community of Muslims worldwide. The Qur'an says: you are the best community brought out for mankind, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong and believing in Allah (Qur'an 3:110), and: this ummah of yours is one ummah, and I am your Lord, so worship Me (Qur'an 21:92).\n\nSource: Qur'an 3:110, 21:92.","the ummah",!0,"")
B.aVD=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:a |an |the )?(?:fatwa|fatawa|mufti|imam|sheikh|shaykh|alim|scholar|ulama)\\b","\\bdifference between (?:a |an )?(?:imam|mufti|sheikh|shaykh|scholar|alim)\\b","\\bwho (?:is|are) (?:the )?(?:mufti|imam|ulama|scholars)\\b","\\bwhat is the role of (?:an |the )?(?:imam|mufti|scholar)\\b"],t.s)
B.apf=new A.X("fatwa-imam-mufti",B.aVD,B.b,"A fatwa is a scholar's answer to a question about Islamic law. A mufti is the scholar qualified to give fatwas. An imam, in a masjid, is the person who leads the prayer, and often teaches and advises the community; the word is also used for the great scholars of the schools. A shaykh or alim is a person of religious knowledge.\n\nA fatwa is an opinion given on a case, not a revelation, and it can differ between scholars and schools. That is why I give the range of views and do not issue fatwas.","fatwa, imam, mufti",!0,"")
B.aOE=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:fiqh|ijma|ijmaa|qiyas|usul al fiqh|usul|ijtihad)\\b","\\bsources of (?:islamic )?(?:law|fiqh|sharia|shariah)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|did) scholars (?:decide|derive|get) (?:rulings|laws)\\b","\\bwhere does (?:islamic law|sharia|shariah) come from\\b"],t.s)
B.ar0=new A.X("fiqh-ijma-qiyas",B.aOE,B.b,"Fiqh is the scholars' understanding of Islamic law, drawn from the sources. The agreed primary sources are the Qur'an and the Sunnah. Beyond them, scholars use ijma (the agreement of scholars on a ruling) and qiyas (extending a ruling to a new case with the same reason). Ijtihad is the scholar's effort to reach a ruling from the sources.\n\nThe schools weigh these sources differently, which is why they sometimes differ. The app's guide on the four schools explains how.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-madhhab-overview]","sources of Islamic law",!0,"")
B.bap=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:the )?(?:elephant|people of the elephant|abraha|abrahah)\\b","\\b(?:what is|tell me about|explain) (?:surah|sura|surat) (?:al )?fil\\b","\\bsurah (?:al )?fil\\b","\\b(?:year of the elephant|ashab (?:al )?fil|people of the elephant)\\b"],t.s)
B.asT=new A.X("story-elephant",B.bap,B.b,"Surah Al-Fil (surah 105) tells of the people of the elephant. It asks whether you have not seen how your Lord dealt with them (Qur'an 105:1): He made their plan go astray (Qur'an 105:2), sent flocks of birds against them (Qur'an 105:3) that struck them with stones of baked clay (Qur'an 105:4), and left them like eaten straw (Qur'an 105:5).\n\nThe surah does not name the army or its commander. Scholars say it refers to the army that came against the Ka'bah in the year the Prophet \ufdfa was born; that is the scholars' reading, not a statement of the surah itself.\n\nSource: Qur'an 105:1, 105:2, 105:3, 105:4, 105:5.\n[GO:/quran]","the People of the Elephant",!0,"")
B.b6i=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:qarun|qaroon|korah|karun)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:qarun|qaroon|karun)\\b","\\b(?:qarun|qaroon|karun)\\b.*\\b(?:wealth|treasure|earth|swallowed|arrogant)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqA=new A.X("story-qarun",B.b6i,B.b,"Qarun is the Qur'an's example of arrogance in wealth. He was from the people of Musa and was given treasures so great that their keys were a burden to a group of strong men (Qur'an 28:76). His people told him not to exult, and to seek the home of the Hereafter with what Allah gave him (Qur'an 28:77). He claimed the wealth came by his own knowledge (Qur'an 28:78). Then Allah caused the earth to swallow him and his home (Qur'an 28:81).\n\nSource: Qur'an 28:76, 28:77, 28:78, 28:81.\n[GO:/quran]","Qarun",!0,"")
B.bhG=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:firaun|fir aun|pharaoh|firawn|fir awn)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:firaun|fir aun|pharaoh|firawn)\\b","\\b(?:firaun|pharaoh)\\b.*\\b(?:drown\\w*|sea|body|mummy|arrogant|lord most high)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqD=new A.X("story-firaun",B.bhG,B.b,"Fir'awn was the tyrant ruler of Egypt in the time of Musa. The Qur'an says he exalted himself in the land and divided its people, weakening a group of them (Qur'an 28:4), and that he claimed to be their lord, the most high (Qur'an 79:24). He pursued Musa and the Children of Israel and was drowned; when drowning he said he believed, but it was too late (Qur'an 10:90-91). The Qur'an says his body would be preserved as a sign for those after him (Qur'an 10:92).\n\nSource: Qur'an 28:4, 79:24, 10:90-91, 10:92.\n[GO:/quran]","Fir'awn (Pharaoh)",!0,"")
B.bAo=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:talut|taloot|saul|jalut|jaloot|goliath)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:talut|taloot|jalut|jaloot|goliath)\\b","\\b(?:talut|taloot|jalut|goliath)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoi=new A.X("story-talut-jalut",B.bAo,B.b,"The story is in Surah Al-Baqarah. The leaders of the Children of Israel asked their prophet for a king to fight with (Qur'an 2:246), and he told them Allah had appointed Talut (Qur'an 2:247). As they marched, Talut tested them at a river, and those who drank more than a sip did not stay with him (Qur'an 2:249). The believers who were sure they would meet Allah said how often a small group had beaten a large one by Allah's permission (Qur'an 2:249). Dawud killed Jalut (Goliath) and Allah gave him kingdom and wisdom (Qur'an 2:251).\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:246, 2:247, 2:249, 2:251.\n[GO:/quran]","Talut and Jalut",!0,"")
B.aPx=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:ismail|ishmael|ismael|ismaeel)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:ismail|ishmael|ismael|ismaeel)\\b","\\b(?:ismail|ishmael)\\b.*\\b(?:sacrific\\w*|ibrahim|abraham|kaaba|kaaba|dream|knife|ram)\\b","\\bwhy do muslims sacrifice\\b.*\\b(?:ibrahim|abraham|eid)\\b"],t.s)
B.atj=new A.X("story-ismail",B.aPx,B.b,"Ismail is the son of Ibrahim, and the Qur'an describes him as true to his promise, a messenger and prophet (Qur'an 19:54). With his father he raised the foundations of the Ka'bah (Qur'an 2:127).\n\nSurah As-Saffat tells that Ibrahim saw in a dream that he was to sacrifice his son, and the son said to do what he was commanded and that he would be among the patient (Qur'an 37:102). When both submitted, Allah called to Ibrahim that he had fulfilled the vision (Qur'an 37:104-105) and ransomed the son with a great sacrifice (Qur'an 37:107). The Eid al-Adha sacrifice remembers this.\n\nThe Qur'an does not name the son in that passage; scholars differ on whether he was Ismail or Ishaq, and many hold he was Ismail. That is a difference of opinion and I do not decide it here.\n\nSource: Qur'an 19:54, 2:127, 37:102, 37:104-105, 37:107.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Ismail",!0,"")
B.bky=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:lut|lot|loot)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:lut|loot)\\b","\\b(?:lut|loot)\\b.*\\b(?:people|sodom|city|cities|wife|punish\\w*|destroyed)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoF=new A.X("story-lut",B.bky,B.b,"Lut was sent to a people who had gone astray. The Qur'an says he asked them why they committed an indecency that no one in the worlds had committed before them (Qur'an 7:80), and that they only answered by saying to drive his family out of their town (Qur'an 7:82). Allah saved Lut and his family except his wife, who was among those who stayed behind (Qur'an 7:83). The punishment was a rain upon them (Qur'an 7:84), and the cities were overturned (Qur'an 11:82).\n\nThe Qur'an also notes that his wife was unfaithful to him in faith (Qur'an 66:10).\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:80, 7:82, 7:83, 7:84, 11:82, 66:10.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Lut",!0,"")
B.bpT=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:salih|saleh|thamud|samud)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:salih|saleh)\\b","\\b(?:salih|saleh|thamud)\\b.*\\b(?:camel|she camel|people|punish\\w*|destroyed|tribe)\\b"],t.s)
B.apx=new A.X("story-salih-thamud",B.bpT,B.b,"Salih was sent to the people of Thamud, who were told to worship Allah alone and that a she-camel of Allah was a sign for them (Qur'an 7:73). They were told to let her graze on Allah's land and not to harm her (Qur'an 7:73). They disobeyed and slaughtered the camel, challenging Salih to bring on what he threatened (Qur'an 7:77). Then the earthquake seized them, and they lay lifeless in their homes (Qur'an 7:78).\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:73, 7:77, 7:78.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Salih and Thamud",!0,"")
B.bBk=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:hud|hood|ad|aad|people of ad|people of aad)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:hud|hood)\\b","\\b(?:hud|prophet hud)\\b.*\\b(?:ad|aad|wind|people)\\b","\\b(?:people of )?(?:ad|aad)\\b.*\\b(?:hud|wind|tribe|punish\\w*|destroyed|iram)\\b"],t.s)
B.ao2=new A.X("story-hud-ad",B.bBk,B.b,"Hud was sent to the people of Ad, who were told to worship Allah alone (Qur'an 7:65). They rejected him, and the Qur'an says Allah rescued Hud and those with him and cut off the roots of those who denied (Qur'an 7:72). Surah Al-Haqqah says Ad were destroyed by a furious roaring wind (Qur'an 69:6).\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:65, 7:72, 69:6.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Hud and the people of Ad",!0,"")
B.aW4=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:shuayb|shuaib|shoaib|jethro|madyan|midian)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:shuayb|shuaib|shoaib)\\b","\\b(?:shuayb|shuaib)\\b.*\\b(?:madyan|midian|scales|measure|people|people of)\\b"],t.s)
B.anC=new A.X("story-shuayb-madyan",B.aW4,B.b,"Shu'ayb was sent to Madyan. He called them to worship Allah alone and told them to give full measure and weight and not to cheat people of their things (Qur'an 7:85). They rejected him, and the earthquake seized them so that they lay lifeless in their homes (Qur'an 7:91).\n\nThe story is one of the clearest Qur'anic lessons on honesty in business.\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:85, 7:91.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Shu'ayb and Madyan",!0,"")
B.aYF=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:prophet )?(?:zakariyya|zakariya|zechariah|zakaria|yahya|john the baptist)\\b","\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about) (?:prophet )?(?:zakariyya|zakariya|zechariah|yahya)\\b","\\b(?:zakariyya|zakariya|yahya)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|son|child|old age|maryam|elderly)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqc=new A.X("story-zakariyya-yahya",B.aYF,B.b,"Zakariyya was an elderly prophet who called to his Lord secretly (Qur'an 19:3), saying his bones had grown feeble and asking for a successor (Qur'an 19:4-5). He was given the good news of a son named Yahya (Qur'an 19:7). Zakariyya was surprised, since his wife was barren and he was old (Qur'an 19:8), but it was said that this is easy for Allah (Qur'an 19:9).\n\nOf Yahya the Qur'an says he was given wisdom as a child (Qur'an 19:12), was kind and pure and devout, and was not arrogant or disobedient (Qur'an 19:13-14). Peace was upon him the day he was born, the day he dies and the day he is raised (Qur'an 19:15).\n\nSource: Qur'an 19:3, 19:4-5, 19:7, 19:8, 19:9, 19:12, 19:13-14, 19:15.\n[GO:/quran]","Zakariyya and Yahya",!0,"")
B.bzG=s(["\\b(?:who (?:is|was)|tell me about|story of) (?:prophet )?(?:idris|enoch|idrees)\\b","\\b(?:idris|idrees)\\b.*\\b(?:prophet|raised|high|place)\\b"],t.s)
B.asP=new A.X("prophet-idris",B.bzG,B.b,"Idris is named twice in the Qur'an. In Surah Maryam he is described as a man of truth and a prophet, and Allah says He raised him to a high station (Qur'an 19:56-57). In Surah Al-Anbiya he is listed among those who were patient (Qur'an 21:85).\n\nThe Qur'an gives little else about him, and I do not give more than it says.\n\nSource: Qur'an 19:56-57, 21:85.\n[GO:/quran]","Prophet Idris",!0,"")
B.b5e=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:the )?(?:people of the (?:trench|ditch|pit)|ashab (?:al|ul) ?ukhdud|boy and the king|the boy and the king)\\b","\\bukhdud\\b","\\bsurah (?:al )?buruj\\b","\\bpeople of the (?:ditch|trench|pit)\\b"],t.s)
B.ar8=new A.X("ashab-ukhdud",B.b5e,B.b,"Surah Al-Buruj (surah 85) mentions the people of the trench who kindled a fire (Qur'an 85:4-5) and sat by it (Qur'an 85:6), watching what they did to the believers (Qur'an 85:7). They had no complaint against them except that they believed in Allah, the Almighty, the Praiseworthy (Qur'an 85:8).\n\nThe fuller story of the boy and the king is in a hadith in Sahih Muslim; I have not read it here in full, so I do not give that version.\n\nSource: Qur'an 85:4-5, 85:6, 85:7, 85:8.\n[GO:/quran]","the People of the Trench",!0,"")
B.b4G=s(["\\b(?:story|tale) of (?:the )?(?:sabbath|saturday) (?:breakers|people)\\b","\\bpeople of (?:the )?(?:sabbath|saturday)\\b","\\bashab (?:al )?sabt\\b","\\b(?:people|those) (?:who )?(?:turned into|became) (?:apes|monkeys)\\b"],t.s)
B.ar_=new A.X("sabbath-breakers",B.b4G,B.b,"Surah Al-A'raf mentions a town by the sea whose people broke the Sabbath: the fish came to them openly on the day they were not to fish and not on other days, as a test for their disobedience (Qur'an 7:163). A group of them asked why advise a people Allah will destroy, and the advisers said it was to be free of blame before their Lord (Qur'an 7:164). When they persisted, the Qur'an says Allah said to them: be despised apes (Qur'an 7:166).\n\nScholars differ on whether this was literal or figurative; I do not decide it.\n\nSource: Qur'an 7:163, 7:164, 7:166.\n[GO:/quran]","the Sabbath-breakers",!0,"")
B.aVV=s(["\\b(?:the )?(?:splitting|split|splitting of) (?:of )?(?:the )?moon\\b","\\bmoon (?:was )?split\\b","\\b(?:shaqq|shaqq al) ?qamar\\b","\\bsurah (?:al )?qamar\\b"],t.s)
B.aq_=new A.X("moon-splitting",B.aVV,B.b,"Surah Al-Qamar begins: the Hour has come near and the moon has split (Qur'an 54:1). Ibn Mas'ud reported: during the lifetime of the Prophet \ufdfa the moon was split into two parts, and the Prophet said \"Bear witness to this\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 3636).\n\nThe hadith says this happened in the Prophet's lifetime. I do not add detail beyond what the report gives.\n\nSource: Qur'an 54:1; Sahih al-Bukhari 3636.\n[GO:/quran]","the splitting of the moon",!0,"")
B.aQi=s(["\\b(?:is|was|has) the (?:quran|quran|koran) (?:been )?(?:preserved|changed|corrupted|altered|original|unchanged)\\b","\\b(?:how|why) (?:is|was) the (?:quran|quran) (?:preserved|protected)\\b","\\b(?:preservation|protection) of the (?:quran|quran)\\b","\\bhas the (?:quran|quran) (?:ever )?changed\\b"],t.s)
B.at2=new A.X("quran-preserved",B.aQi,B.b,"The Qur'an says: indeed We sent down the Reminder, and indeed We will be its guardian (Qur'an 15:9).\n\nMuslims point to two means: memorisation, handed down from person to person, and writing. Zayd ibn Thabit reported that after many reciters were killed at the Battle of Yamama, Umar feared that much of the Qur'an would be lost, and Abu Bakr asked Zayd to collect it (Abu Bakr sent for Zayd after the people of Yamama were killed, and Umar told Abu Bakr that many reciters had died and he feared more would die and much of the Qur'an be lost, so Zayd was asked to collect it (Sahih al-Bukhari 4986)).\n\nThe details of the later compilation under Uthman are in other reports; I am not summarising them here.\n\nSource: Qur'an 15:9; Sahih al-Bukhari 4986.\n[GO:/quran]","preservation of the Qur'an",!0,"")
B.bwU=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|how is|why is) the (?:quran|quran|koran)(?:s| a| is)? (?:a )?(?:miracle|miraculous)\\b","\\b(?:quran|quran)\\b.*\\b(?:miracle|miraculous|challenge|inimitable|ijaz)\\b","\\bwhat is (?:the )?(?:ijaz|challenge of the quran)\\b","\\bproof (?:that )?(?:the )?(?:quran|quran) is (?:from allah|true|divine)\\b"],t.s)
B.at7=new A.X("quran-miracle",B.bwU,B.b,"The Qur'an challenges people to produce something like it. It says that if the people and the jinn gathered to produce the like of this Qur'an they could not, even if they helped one another (Qur'an 17:88), and it challenges those in doubt to bring a surah like it (Qur'an 2:23).\n\nScholars discuss its language, its message and its preservation as parts of this challenge. That is the scholars' general discussion, not something I can summarise further without a named source.\n\nSource: Qur'an 17:88, 2:23.\n[GO:/quran]","the Qur'an's challenge",!0,"")
B.byg=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|difference between|meaning of|explain) (?:a )?(?:makki|makkan|madani|madinan|meccan|medinan)\\b","\\b(?:makki|makkan|meccan)\\b.*\\b(?:madani|madinan|medinan)\\b","\\bwhich surahs? (?:are|were) (?:makki|makkan|madani|madinan|meccan|medinan)\\b"],t.s)
B.aow=new A.X("makki-madani",B.byg,B.b,"Makki surahs were revealed before the Hijrah and Madani surahs after it. Scholars use the labels to group surahs: the Makki ones are often shorter and focus on belief, the afterlife and the call to worship Allah alone, while the Madani ones often include rules for the community. This grouping is the scholars' classification, and some surahs have verses of both.\n\nThe Surah list in the app marks where each surah was revealed.\n[GO:/quran]","Makki and Madani surahs",!0,"")
B.bqG=s(["\\b(?:what are|what is|meaning of|explain) (?:the )?(?:disjointed|isolated|mysterious|separate|huruf muqatta ?at|muqattaat|muqatta ?at)\\b","\\b(?:alif|alif lam|alif lam mim|ha mim|ya sin|ya seen)\\b.*\\b(?:mean|meaning|letters)\\b","\\bwhat does (?:alif|alif lam mim|ya sin|ha mim|nun|qaf) mean\\b","\\bletters (?:at|in) the (?:start|beginning) of (?:some )?surahs\\b"],t.s)
B.apE=new A.X("disjointed-letters",B.bqG,B.b,"Some surahs begin with separate letters, such as Alif Lam Mim at the start of Surah Al-Baqarah (Qur'an 2:1). Scholars have given several explanations of them, and many say that their meaning is known to Allah. I do not choose one explanation, and the Qur'an itself does not explain them.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:1.\n[GO:/quran]","the disjointed letters",!0,"")
B.bqD=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|define|meaning of|explain) (?:tajweed|tajwid)\\b","\\bis (?:tajweed|tajwid) (?:obligatory|required|fard|wajib|necessary|important)\\b","\\bwhy (?:is|do i need|should i learn) tajweed\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) learn tajweed\\b"],t.s)
B.apI=new A.X("tajweed-meaning",B.bqD,B.SV,"Tajweed is the set of rules for reciting the Qur'an correctly: giving each letter its proper sound and each rule of lengthening, stopping and joining its due. The Qur'an tells you to recite it slowly and distinctly (Qur'an 73:4).\n\nHow much tajweed is required of every Muslim is discussed by scholars, and I do not give a ruling on it. The best way to learn is with a teacher.\n\nSource: Qur'an 73:4.\n[GO:/quran]","tajweed",!0,"")
B.bxr=s(["\\b(?:what|who) does allah love\\b","\\bwho (?:does|do) (?:you think )?allah love\\b","\\bthose whom allah loves\\b","\\b(?:allah loves|allahs love)\\b.*\\b(?:who|whom|what|those)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:get|earn|win|gain) (?:allahs|the love of) (?:allah|love)\\b"],t.s)
B.arW=new A.X("what-allah-loves",B.bxr,B.b,"The Qur'an names whom Allah loves. He loves those who do good (Qur'an 2:195), those who repent and those who purify themselves (Qur'an 2:222), those who are conscious of Him (Qur'an 3:76), the patient (Qur'an 3:146), those who rely on Him (Qur'an 3:159), and those who act justly (Qur'an 5:42).\n\nSo the way to His love is through these qualities: doing good, repenting, patience, trust in Him and justice.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:195, 2:222, 3:76, 3:146, 3:159, 5:42.","whom Allah loves",!0,"")
B.beo=s(["\\b(?:what|who) does allah (?:hate|dislike)\\b","\\bwhat (?:are the things|things) allah (?:hates|dislikes)\\b","\\bwho (?:does|do) allah (?:hate|dislike|not love)\\b","\\bthose (?:whom )?allah does not love\\b"],t.s)
B.asW=new A.X("what-allah-dislikes",B.beo,B.b,"The Qur'an says Allah does not love those who transgress (Qur'an 2:190), the arrogant and boastful (Qur'an 4:36), those who cause corruption (Qur'an 2:205), and the wasteful (Qur'an 7:31).\n\nSo these are the qualities to avoid: transgression, arrogance, corruption and waste.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:190, 4:36, 2:205, 7:31.","whom Allah does not love",!0,"")
B.bhw=s(["\\b(?:what are|list|name|tell me) (?:the )?(?:major sins|great sins|big sins|kabair|kaba ir|kabaair|seven (?:major|great|deadly) sins)\\b","\\b(?:major|great|big|biggest) sins? (?:in|of) islam\\b","\\bwhat is the biggest sin\\b","\\bseven (?:destructive|deadly) sins?\\b"],t.s)
B.arj=new A.X("major-sins",B.bhw,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: avoid the seven great destructive sins: joining others in worship with Allah, sorcery, killing a life Allah has forbidden without a just cause, taking riba, taking an orphan's wealth, fleeing from the battlefield, and accusing chaste women (Sahih al-Bukhari 2766).\n\nAbu Bakrah reported he said the biggest of the great sins are: joining partners with Allah and being undutiful to parents, and a forged statement and false witness (Sahih al-Bukhari 5976).\n\nThese lists are not the only places the major sins are named; scholars have collected more. I give these two lists only.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2766, 5976.","major sins",!0,"")
B.bAO=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|ruling on|islam on|islam say about|what does islam say about) (?:cheating|fraud|deception|dishonesty)\\b","\\bis (?:it )?(?:cheating|fraud|deceiving|deception) (?:haram|allowed|a sin)\\b","\\b(?:honesty|honest) in (?:trade|business|selling|buying)\\b","\\b(?:business|trade|trading|selling) (?:ethics|honesty)\\b","\\b(?:islamic|muslim) business ethics\\b"],t.s)
B.bku=s(["\\b(?:husband|wife|exam|test)\\b"],t.s)
B.arp=new A.X("cheating-trade",B.bAO,B.bku,"The Prophet \ufdfa said, as Abu Hurayrah reported: he who acted dishonestly towards us is not of us (Sahih Muslim 101).\n\nHakim ibn Hizam reported about trade: if both parties speak the truth and describe the defects and qualities of the goods, they will be blessed in their transaction, and if they tell lies or hide something, the blessing will be lost (Sahih al-Bukhari 2079).\n\nThe Qur'an also tells believers to give full measure and weight (Qur'an 6:152).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 101; Sahih al-Bukhari 2079; Qur'an 6:152.","honesty in business",!0,"")
B.bs9=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|ruling on|islam on|islam say about|what does islam say about) (?:hoarding|bribery|bribes?|corruption)\\b","\\bis (?:it )?(?:hoarding|bribery|bribing|taking bribes?|paying bribes?) (?:haram|allowed|a sin|permitted)\\b","\\b(?:hoarding|bribe|bribery)\\b.*\\b(?:hadith|islam|islamic|prophet)\\b"],t.s)
B.as2=new A.X("hoarding-bribery",B.bs9,B.b,"On hoarding, Ma'mar reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: he who hoards is a sinner (Sahih Muslim 1605). Scholars discuss what this covers, namely holding back basic needs to raise their price, and I do not extend it to a particular case.\n\nOn bribery, Abdullah ibn Amr reported: the Messenger of Allah \ufdfa cursed the one who gives a bribe and the one who takes it (Sunan Abu Dawud 3580, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1605; Sunan Abu Dawud 3580, sahih per al-Albani.","hoarding and bribery",!0,"")
B.bxS=s(["\\b(?:what are|what is|rights of) (?:the )?(?:rights of )?(?:an |the )?(?:employee|employees|worker|workers|labou?rer|labou?rers|staff)\\b","\\b(?:islam|islamic|hadith|prophet)\\b.*\\b(?:wages|paying (?:workers|employees)|employer|employee)\\b","\\bhow (?:should|to) (?:i|an employer) treat (?:an |my )?(?:employee|employees|workers?)\\b","\\bis it (?:haram|a sin) to (?:not pay|withhold) (?:wages|salary)\\b"],t.s)
B.arZ=new A.X("employee-rights",B.bxS,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet \ufdfa said Allah says: I will be against three on the Day of Resurrection: one who makes a covenant in My name and betrays it, one who sells a free person and eats the price, and one who hires a labourer, gets the full work from him and does not pay him his wages (Sahih al-Bukhari 2227).\n\nSo paying a worker what was agreed is a serious right. Disputes about particular contracts are for a scholar or a court.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2227.","rights of workers",!0,"")
B.baf=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|reward for|reward of|virtue of|benefit of|islam on|islam say about) (?:sponsoring|looking after|caring for|kafalah|kafala|supporting|helping) (?:an |the )?(?:orphan|orphans)\\b","\\b(?:orphan|orphans)\\b.*\\b(?:reward|paradise|sponsor|sponsorship|hadith|islam|care)\\b","\\b(?:kafalah|kafala)\\b"],t.s)
B.anY=new A.X("orphan-sponsorship",B.baf,B.b,"Sahl ibn Sa'd reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: I and the one who looks after an orphan and provides for him will be in Paradise like this (Sahih al-Bukhari 6005), and he joined his index and middle fingers.\n\nTaking an orphan's wealth wrongly is among the great sins in the hadith on major sins (Sahih al-Bukhari 2766).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6005, 2766.\n[GO:/zakat]","caring for orphans",!0,"")
B.bdW=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|what are|explain) (?:the )?(?:fitrah|fitra|sunnahs? of fitrah|acts of fitrah|natural practices)\\b","\\b(?:circumcision|khitan|trimming (?:the )?nails|clipping (?:the )?nails|cutting (?:the )?nails|armpit hair|pubic hair|shaving pubic)\\b","\\bis (?:it|trimming|cutting|clipping) (?:the )?(?:nails|moustache|mustache)\\b","\\b(?:five|5) (?:things|practices|acts) of (?:the )?fitrah\\b"],t.s)
B.b7y=s(["\\b(?:ruling|haram|fard|wajib)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoN=new A.X("fitrah-sunnahs",B.bdW,B.b7y,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: five are the acts of fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, cutting the nails, plucking the hair under the armpits, and clipping the moustache (Sahih Muslim 257).\n\nThe Bukhari version lists them too: five practices are characteristics of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic region, clipping the nails and cutting the moustache short (Sahih al-Bukhari 5889). Scholars discuss whether each is obligatory or recommended, and I do not rule on it here.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 257; Sahih al-Bukhari 5889.","the fitrah practices",!0,"")
B.bn3=s(["\\b(?:what was|what is|describe|tell me about) (?:the )?(?:prophets|prophets|muhammads|prophet muhammads) (?:character|manners|ethics|akhlaq|behaviou?r)\\b","\\bhow was the prophet (?:with|towards|to) (?:people|others|children|family)\\b","\\bwhat was the prophet (?:like|s personality)\\b","\\bakhlaq of the prophet\\b","\\b(?:good|best) (?:manners|character|akhlaq)\\b.*\\b(?:prophet|hadith|islam)\\b"],t.s)
B.aso=new A.X("prophets-character",B.bn3,B.b,"The Qur'an says to the Prophet \ufdfa: you are of great moral character (Qur'an 68:4).\n\nAbdullah ibn Amr reported that the Prophet \ufdfa never used bad language, and used to say that the best among you are those with the best manners and character (Sahih al-Bukhari 3559).\n\nFor stories of his conduct, the Seerah section of the app has them.\n\nSource: Qur'an 68:4; Sahih al-Bukhari 3559.\n[GO:/quran]","the Prophet's character",!0,"")
B.bbj=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|protection)\\b.*\\b(?:protect\\w*|safe\\w*|guard\\w*)?\\b.*\\b(?:my )?(?:children|kids|child|son|daughter|baby|babies)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) protect (?:my )?(?:children|kids|child|baby)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|evil eye|shaytan|islam|islamic)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|recite|read) (?:over|for) (?:my )?(?:children|kids|child|baby|son|daughter)\\b","\\buidhukuma bi kalimat\\b|\\bu idhu\\b"],t.s)
B.b__=s(["\\b(?:name|naming|aqiqah|newborn|new born|sick|ill|haram|ruling|eating|sleep)\\b"],t.s)
B.apq=new A.X("dua-protect-children",B.bbj,B.b__,"Ibn Abbas reported that the Prophet \ufdfa used to seek refuge for Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn, saying that their forefather Ibrahim used to seek refuge for Ismail and Ishaq with these words: I seek refuge with Allah's perfect words from every devil and from poisonous pests and from every evil, harmful eye (Sahih al-Bukhari 3371).\n\nIn Arabic it begins: U'idhukuma bi kalimatillahit-tammati min kulli shaytanin wa hammatin wa min kulli 'aynin lammah.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 3371.\n[GO:/adhkar]","du'a to protect children",!0,"")
B.bxL=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b.*\\b(?:guidance|guided|right path|straight path|hidayah|hidaya|steadfast\\w*|firm\\w*)\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) (?:say|ask|pray) (?:for|to get|to ask for) (?:guidance|hidayah|the right path|steadfastness)\\b","\\bhow (?:to|do i|can i) (?:ask for|get|seek) (?:guidance|hidayah)\\b","\\bihdina (?:as|al) ?sirat\\b"],t.s)
B.art=new A.X("dua-guidance",B.bxL,B.b,"The most frequent du'a for guidance is in Surah Al-Fatihah: guide us to the straight path (Qur'an 1:6), which Muslims recite in every rak'ah of prayer.\n\nAli reported that the Prophet \ufdfa told him to say: O Allah, direct me to the right path and make me adhere to the straight path (Sahih Muslim 2725). For steadfastness, the Qur'an gives the du'a: our Lord, do not let our hearts deviate after You have guided us (Qur'an 3:8).\n\nSource: Qur'an 1:6, 3:8; Sahih Muslim 2725.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/quran]","du'a for guidance",!0,"")
B.aXb=s(["\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication|what (?:to|do i|should i) say)\\b.*\\b(?:end of|ending|leaving|after|when leaving)\\b.*\\b(?:gathering|meeting|majlis|sitting|party)\\b","\\bkaffarat (?:al )?majlis\\b","\\bwhat (?:to|do i|should i) say (?:before|when) (?:i )?(?:get up|stand up|leave) (?:from )?(?:a |the )?(?:gathering|meeting|sitting|majlis)\\b","\\bexpiation (?:of|for) (?:the )?(?:gathering|meeting|majlis|sitting)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqJ=new A.X("dua-end-of-gathering",B.aXb,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: whoever sits in a sitting and engages in much empty, meaningless speech and then says before getting up \"Glory is to You, O Allah, and praise, I bear witness that there is none worthy of worship except You, I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You\", whatever occurred in that sitting will be forgiven to him (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3433, sahih per Darussalam).\n\nIn Arabic: Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3433, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/adhkar]","du'a at the end of a gathering",!0,"")
B.aWh=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats|tell me|explain) (?:the )?(?:most (?:comprehensive|common|frequent)|comprehensive|jami|jaami)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b","\\brabbana (?:atina|aatina|atinaa|aatinaa) (?:fid|fi d|fil|fi l) ?dunya\\b","\\b(?:dua|du a)\\b.*\\b(?:good in this world|world and the hereafter|dunya and akhirah|dunya and akhira)\\b","\\bwhat (?:was|is) the prophets? (?:most )?(?:frequent|common|favou?rite) (?:dua|du a|supplication)\\b"],t.s)
B.anA=new A.X("dua-comprehensive",B.aWh,B.b,"Anas reported that the most frequent du'a of the Prophet \ufdfa was: \"O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the torment of the Fire\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 6389).\n\nIt is also a verse of the Qur'an (Qur'an 2:201). In Arabic: Rabbana atina fid-dunya hasanatan wa fil-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhaban-nar.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6389; Qur'an 2:201.\n[GO:/adhkar]","the Prophet's most frequent du'a",!0,"")
B.bc1=s(["\\b(?:what is the|whats the) (?:reward|virtue|benefit) (?:of|for) (?:performing |doing |going on )?hajj\\b","\\bwhat (?:happens|does hajj do) to (?:your |my |a persons )?sins\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of hajj\\b","\\b(?:hajj|hajj mabrur|accepted hajj)\\b.*\\b(?:reward|sins|forgiven|born anew|newborn)\\b"],t.s)
B.aon=new A.X("hajj-reward-lahawla",B.bc1,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: whoever performs Hajj for Allah's pleasure and does not have sexual relations nor do wrong, will return as if he were born anew (Sahih al-Bukhari 1521).\n\nThe scholars say the hadith refers to an accepted Hajj; I am not adding conditions to it.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1521.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-hajj-intro]","the reward of Hajj",!0,"")
B.aWj=s(["\\b(?:what is|whats) the (?:reward|virtue|benefit|difference) (?:of|for|between) (?:praying|prayer|salah|salat) in (?:congregation|jamaah|jamaat|jama ah)\\b","\\b(?:praying|prayer|salah) (?:in )?(?:congregation|jamaah|jamaat)\\b.*\\b(?:reward|times|better|virtue|twenty|27)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of (?:praying )?(?:fajr|the morning prayer|dawn prayer)\\b","\\bhow many times (?:is|better|more) (?:the )?(?:congregation|jamaah)\\b"],t.s)
B.asb=new A.X("reward-congregation-fajr",B.aWj,B.b,"Ibn Umar reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the prayer in congregation is twenty-seven times superior to the prayer offered by a person alone (Sahih al-Bukhari 645).\n\nOn Fajr, Jundub reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: he who prayed the morning prayer in congregation is under the protection of Allah (Sahih Muslim 657).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 645; Sahih Muslim 657.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-congregation]","the reward of congregation and Fajr",!0,"")
B.bme=s(["\\b(?:what is the|whats the) (?:reward|virtue|benefit) (?:of|for) (?:feeding|giving food to|feeding the)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of (?:feeding|giving) (?:the )?(?:poor|hungry|needy)\\b","\\b(?:best|good|what are the best) (?:deeds?|actions?|qualities)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|muslim|feed\\w*|greet\\w*)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of (?:sending |saying |giving )?(?:salawat|durood|darood|salat)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of (?:saying )?(?:la hawla|la hawl)\\b","\\bla hawla wa la quwwata illa billah\\b"],t.s)
B.aoE=new A.X("reward-feeding-salam-salawat",B.bme,B.b,'A man asked the Prophet \ufdfa which deeds are best in Islam, and he answered, as Abdullah ibn Amr reported: to feed the poor and greet those whom you know and those whom you do not know (Sahih al-Bukhari 12).\n\nOn sending blessings on the Prophet \ufdfa, Abu Hurayrah reported: he who blesses me once, Allah will bless him ten times (Sahih Muslim 408).\n\nOn "La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah", Abu Musa reported the Prophet \ufdfa said it is one of the treasures of Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 6384).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 12, 6384; Sahih Muslim 408.\n[GO:/adhkar]\n[GO:/tasbeeh]',"rewards of small deeds",!0,"")
B.baI=s(["\\b(?:what is the|whats the) (?:reward|virtue|benefit) (?:of|for) (?:reading|reciting) (?:the )?(?:quran|quran|koran)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|benefit) of (?:reading|reciting) (?:the )?(?:quran|quran|koran)\\b","\\bhow many (?:hasanat|rewards?|good deeds) (?:for|per) (?:reading|reciting|each letter)\\b","\\b(?:each|every) letter (?:of|in) (?:the )?(?:quran|quran)\\b"],t.s)
B.arl=new A.X("qur-an-recite-reward",B.baI,B.b,"The Qur'an says that those who recite the Book of Allah, establish prayer and spend from what We provided them, secretly and openly, hope for a trade that will never perish (Qur'an 35:29), so that Allah gives them their full reward and increases it from His bounty (Qur'an 35:30).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa also said, as 'Uthman reported, that Sahih al-Bukhari 5027.\n\nI am not giving a count per letter, because I have not checked a graded report to cite.\n\nSource: Qur'an 35:29, 35:30; Sahih al-Bukhari 5027.\n[GO:/quran]","the reward of reciting the Qur'an",!0,"")
B.aX1=s(["\\b(?:importance of|keep\\w*|maintain\\w*|break\\w*|cut\\w*|sever\\w*|strengthen\\w*) (?:the )?(?:family |kinship )?ties\\b","\\bsilat (?:al )?rahim\\b","\\bties of kinship\\b","\\bkeep\\w* (?:in )?touch with (?:my )?(?:relatives|family)\\b","\\bqat(?:i|a)?\\s?(?:ah|a) (?:al )?rahim\\b"],t.s)
B.aoJ=new A.X("family-ties-kinship",B.aX1,B.b,"Keeping the ties of kinship is a duty the Qur'an links with fearing Allah (Qur'an 4:1).\n\nAbu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: whoever is pleased to have his provision widened and his life prolonged should keep good relations with his relatives (Sahih al-Bukhari 5985).\n\nJubayr ibn Mut'im reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the one who cuts the bond of kinship will not enter Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 5984).\n\nKeeping ties can be as simple as a call, a visit, a gift or a kind word, even when the relative has not kept theirs. If a relative is harming you, you may keep your distance and still be polite; ask a scholar about a hard case.\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:1; Sahih al-Bukhari 5985, 5984.\n[GO:/huda]","keeping family ties",!0,"")
B.b3D=s(["\\braising (?:my )?(?:daughters?|girls)\\b","\\b(?:reward|virtue|blessing) (?:of )?(?:having|raising|bringing up|looking after|caring for) (?:daughters?|girls)\\b","\\bdaughters? in islam\\b","\\bbring(?:ing)? up (?:two |my )?(?:daughters?|girls)\\b"],t.s)
B.arR=new A.X("raising-daughters",B.b3D,B.b,"Anas reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: whoever brings up two girls properly until they reach maturity, he and I will come on the Day of Resurrection like this, and he joined his fingers (Sahih Muslim 2631).\n\nThe hadith is about caring for girls well: feeding, educating, protecting and treating them with kindness and fairness. It is a reward the Prophet \ufdfa gave to the father or guardian who does this.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2631.\n[GO:/huda]","raising daughters",!0,"")
B.bh9=s(["\\bwhat (?:to|should i|do i) look for in (?:a |my )?(?:spouse|husband|wife|partner)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|should|can) i (?:choose|pick|select|find) (?:a |my )?(?:spouse|husband|wife)\\b","\\bwho (?:is|should i marry|is the best to marry)\\b.*\\bmarry\\b","\\bwhom should i marry\\b","\\bbest (?:person|man|woman) to marry\\b","\\bqualities (?:of|in) (?:a )?(?:good )?(?:spouse|husband|wife)\\b"],t.s)
B.apU=new A.X("choosing-spouse",B.bh9,B.b,"Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: a woman is married for four things: her wealth, her family, her beauty and her religion, so marry the one with religion (Sahih al-Bukhari 5090).\n\nThe Qur'an describes marriage as a sign of Allah: He made spouses from yourselves so you may find rest in them, and placed affection and mercy between you (Qur'an 30:21). It also urges marrying those who are single and righteous (Qur'an 24:32).\n\nMany scholars apply the same advice to men: look for faith and good character first. If you cannot decide, pray the two-rak'ah istikhara prayer, take counsel from people you trust, and meet the person with a guardian or family involved.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5090; Qur'an 30:21, 24:32.\n[GO:/huda]","choosing a spouse",!0,"")
B.ben=s(["\\b(?:hudaybiyyah|hudaybiyah|hudaibiyah|hudaibiyyah|hudaibiya|hudaybiya)\\b","\\b(?:treaty|truce|pact) (?:of|at) (?:al )?hud\\w+\\b"],t.s)
B.anU=new A.X("hudaybiyyah",B.ben,B.b,"In the sixth year after the Hijrah the Prophet \ufdfa set out toward Makkah to perform 'Umrah and the Quraysh tried to stop him. Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan reported: the Prophet \ufdfa set out at the time of Hudaybiyyah, his camel sat down, and he said she was stopped by the One who stopped the elephant; he said that if the Quraysh asked for anything that honoured Allah's sanctities he would grant it (Sahih al-Bukhari 2731).\n\nHe told their envoy Budayl that he had come to perform 'Umrah and not to fight, and offered a truce. The long hadith goes on to the talks that followed.\n\nSurah Al-Fath opens with Allah saying: We have given you a clear victory (Qur'an 48:1). Many scholars say it was revealed after Hudaybiyyah, and that the truce opened the way for the later conquest of Makkah.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2731; Qur'an 48:1.\n[GO:/stories]","the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah",!0,"")
B.bwz=s(["\\b(?:conquest|opening|victory) of (?:makkah|mecca|makka)\\b","\\bfath (?:al )?(?:makkah|mecca)\\b","\\b(?:how|when|what happened when) (?:did )?(?:the prophet|muhammad|prophet muhammad)?.*\\b(?:conquer\\w*|enter\\w*|return\\w*) (?:to )?(?:makkah|mecca)\\b","\\bsurah (?:an )?nasr\\b"],t.s)
B.asz=new A.X("conquest-makkah",B.bwz,B.b,"Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) reported: when the Prophet \ufdfa entered Makkah on the day of the conquest there were 360 idols around the Ka'bah, and he struck them with a stick saying that truth has come and falsehood will neither start nor return (Sahih al-Bukhari 4287).\n\nThis echoes the verse Qur'an 17:81. Ibn Abbas reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying on that day: there is no migration after the conquest, but striving and good intentions, and when you are called to strive, respond (Sahih al-Bukhari 3077).\n\nSurah An-Nasr speaks of Allah's help and the conquest, and of people entering Allah's religion in crowds (Qur'an 110:1-3).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 4287, 3077; Qur'an 17:81, 110:1-3.\n[GO:/stories]","the conquest of Makkah",!0,"")
B.bjN=s(["\\bfarewell (?:sermon|speech|khutbah|hajj|pilgrimage)\\b","\\blast (?:sermon|speech|khutbah) of (?:the )?(?:prophet|muhammad)\\b","\\bkhutbat(?:ul)? (?:al )?wada\\b","\\bwhat did the prophet say (?:in|at) (?:his )?(?:last|final) (?:hajj|sermon)\\b"],t.s)
B.ara=new A.X("farewell-sermon",B.bjN,B.b,"On the Day of Sacrifice in his last Hajj the Prophet \ufdfa gave a sermon. Ibn Abbas reported: he asked which day, which town and which month it was, and when they said it was sacred he said that their blood, their property and their honour are sacred to one another like this day, in this town, in this month; he repeated it, asked whether he had conveyed the message, and told those present to pass it on to those absent (Sahih al-Bukhari 1739).\n\nThat sermon is also known for its words that the Muslims should not return to disbelief after him by striking one another's necks.\n\nThe same Hajj is linked to the verse Qur'an 5:3, in which Allah says He has perfected the religion for the believers.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1739; Qur'an 5:3.\n[GO:/hadith]","the Farewell Sermon",!0,"")
B.blD=s(["\\b(?:story of |what happened (?:at|in) |tell me about )(?:the )?(?:taif|ta if)\\b","\\bprophet\\b.*\\b(?:taif|ta if)\\b","\\b(?:taif|ta if)\\b.*\\b(?:prophet|muhammad|stoned|angel of the mountains)\\b","\\bangel of the mountains\\b","\\byear of (?:sorrow|grief|sadness)\\b"],t.s)
B.arv=new A.X("taif-journey",B.blD,B.b,"Aisha asked the Prophet \ufdfa whether he had met a day harder than Uhud. he said the hardest was the day of 'Aqabah, when he presented himself to Ibn Abd Yalil and was not answered; he left overwhelmed with sorrow, and at Qarn ath-Tha'alib Gabriel and the Angel of the Mountains came and offered to crush the people between two mountains, but he said no, hoping Allah would bring from them people who worship Allah alone (Sahih al-Bukhari 3231).\n\nIt shows his mercy: he was offered revenge and chose hope for them instead. Allah describes him as a mercy to the worlds (Qur'an 21:107).\n\nThe hadith does not itself name Ta'if or give the year; scholars link it to his journey to Ta'if, which is also known as the 'year of sorrow' with the deaths of Khadijah and Abu Talib. Those details are the scholars' account.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 3231; Qur'an 21:107.\n[GO:/stories]","the Prophet's journey to Ta'if",!0,"")
B.bi6=s(["\\b(?:who (?:are|were)|what (?:are|is|were)|tell me about|meaning of) (?:the )?(?:ansar|muhajir\\w*|muhajireen|muhajiroon)\\b","\\b(?:ansar|muhajir\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:difference|meaning|who|brother\\w*|madinah|medina)\\b","\\bbrotherhood (?:between|of) (?:the )?(?:ansar|muhajir\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoW=new A.X("ansar-muhajirun",B.bi6,B.b,"The Muhajirun are the Companions who left Makkah for Allah's sake; the Ansar ('helpers') are the people of Madinah who gave them shelter and support.\n\nThe Qur'an praises both: the poor emigrants who were driven from their homes (Qur'an 59:8), and those who made their home in Madinah, love those who came to them and prefer them over themselves even in need (Qur'an 59:9). It also speaks of the foremost of the emigrants and the helpers (Qur'an 9:100).\n\nAnas reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: love of the Ansar is a sign of faith and hatred of the Ansar is a sign of hypocrisy (Sahih al-Bukhari 17).\n\nSource: Qur'an 59:8, 59:9, 9:100; Sahih al-Bukhari 17.\n[GO:/stories]","the Muhajirun and the Ansar",!0,"")
B.aOK=s(["\\bzuhd\\b","\\bwhat is (?:the )?(?:asceticism|detachment from (?:this )?(?:world|dunya))\\b","\\bbe in this world (?:as|like) a (?:stranger|traveller|traveler)\\b","\\bdetach\\w* from (?:this )?(?:world|dunya)\\b"],t.s)
B.anI=new A.X("zuhd-detachment",B.aOK,B.b,"Zuhd is not owning less for its own sake; it is keeping the world in your hand and not in your heart.\n\nIbn Umar reported: the Prophet \ufdfa took hold of his shoulder and said to be in this world as if a stranger or a traveller (Sahih al-Bukhari 6416). Ibn Umar used to say that in the evening you should not expect the morning, nor in the morning the evening, and to take from your health for your sickness and from your life for your death.\n\nThe Qur'an reminds that the life of this world is only play and amusement while the home of the Hereafter is better for those who fear Allah (Qur'an 6:32).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6416; Qur'an 6:32.\n[GO:/hadith]","zuhd and being a traveller in this world",!0,"")
B.brD=s(["\\b(?:days? of )?(?:tashreeq|tashriq|tashreek|tashrik)\\b","\\bdays? after (?:eid|eid ul adha|eid al adha|adha)\\b.*\\b(?:eating|fasting|takbir)\\b"],t.s)
B.arQ=new A.X("days-of-tashreeq",B.brD,B.b,"The days of Tashriq are the three days after the Day of Sacrifice (the 11th, 12th and 13th of Dhul Hijjah).\n\nNubayshah al-Hudhali reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking (Sahih Muslim 1141). Because of this, fasting on those days is generally not allowed, with a narrow exception reported for pilgrims who could not afford a sacrificial animal; ask a scholar about your case.\n\nThey are also days of remembering Allah, as Allah says: remember Allah during the numbered days (Qur'an 2:203).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1141; Qur'an 2:203.\n[GO:/calendar]","the days of Tashriq",!0,"")
B.bpB=s(["\\bwhat (?:should|do|to|must) (?:i|we|you) do (?:when|after|once) (?:a |the |my )?(?:baby|child|son|daughter|newborn) (?:is )?(?:born|arrives?)\\b","\\bsunnah\\w* (?:of|for|after|at) (?:a )?(?:new ?born|birth|baby)\\b","\\bnew ?born\\b.*\\b(?:sunnah|islam\\w*|do)\\b","\\btahnik\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|are) (?:the )?(?:sunnah|rights of) (?:a )?(?:new ?born|baby)\\b"],t.s)
B.ar9=new A.X("newborn-sunnah",B.bpB,B.b,"Abu Musa reported: a son was born to him and he took him to the Prophet \ufdfa, who named him Ibrahim, put a chewed date in his mouth (tahnik), prayed for blessing for him and returned him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5467).\n\nSamurah reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: a boy is in pledge for his 'aqiqah, which is sacrificed for him on the seventh day, when his head is shaved and he is named (Sunan Abu Dawud 2838, sahih per Darussalam).\n\nSo: give thanks, give a good name, say a du'a for the child, and the 'aqiqah is done around the seventh day. Scholars differ on whether the 'aqiqah is strongly recommended or obligatory, and on the details such as the number of animals.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5467; Sunan Abu Dawud 2838, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/huda]","what is done when a baby is born",!0,"")
B.bgv=s(["\\b(?:choos\\w*|pick\\w*|best|good|islamic|beautiful) names? for (?:my |a |the )?(?:baby|child|son|daughter|boy|girl)\\b","\\bnames? (?:dearest|most beloved|best) to allah\\b","\\bwhat (?:name|names) (?:should|can) i (?:give|name)\\b","\\bwhich names? (?:are|is) (?:best|disliked|forbidden|haram) (?:in islam)?\\b"],t.s)
B.aqZ=new A.X("good-names-child",B.bgv,B.b,"Ibn Umar reported the Prophet \ufdfa saying: the names dearest to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman (Sahih Muslim 2132).\n\nChoose a name with a good meaning, preferably that of a prophet, a righteous person or a servant of Allah (Abd followed by one of His names). Avoid names with a bad meaning, or names that claim a quality that belongs to Allah alone.\n\nFor the du'a at the naming, see the du'a for a new baby.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 2132.\n[GO:/huda]","choosing a name for a child",!0,"")
B.bd9=s(["\\btara[wv]ee?h\\b","\\btarawih\\b","\\bhow many (?:rakats?|rakahs?|rakaat|raka ?ah) (?:in|for|is|are) (?:the )?tara\\w*\\b","\\bnight prayers? in ramadan\\b","\\bqiyam (?:al )?(?:layl|lail) (?:in )?ramadan\\b"],t.s)
B.aqB=new A.X("tarawih-prayer",B.bd9,B.b,"Tarawih is the voluntary night prayer of Ramadan, prayed after the 'Isha' prayer, often in congregation.\n\nAisha was asked how the Prophet \ufdfa prayed in Ramadan: she said he never exceeded eleven rak'ahs in Ramadan or other months, four, then four, then three (Sahih al-Bukhari 1147).\n\nUnder 'Umar, the people were gathered behind a single reciter: Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari reported that 'Umar gathered the people behind Ubayy ibn Ka'b (Sahih al-Bukhari 2010). Scholars differ on the number of rak'ahs: the schools commonly pray twenty and some pray eight with witr. Both are accepted by scholars, and the most important thing is to pray it with calm and presence.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1147, 2010.\n[GO:/ramadan]","the Tarawih prayer",!0,"")
B.btB=s(["\\b(?:solar|lunar|sun|moon)? ?eclipse\\b","\\bsalat(?:ul)? (?:al )?(?:kusuf|khusuf|kusoof)\\b","\\bprayer (?:of|for|during) (?:an |the )?eclipse\\b"],t.s)
B.as9=new A.X("eclipse-prayer",B.btB,B.b,"Aisha reported: in the Prophet's lifetime the sun eclipsed and he led the people in a prayer with long standing, a long bow, a second shorter standing and bow, and long prostrations, in each rak'ah; then he gave a sermon, and said the sun and moon are two signs of Allah that do not eclipse for anyone's death or life, so when you see it remember Allah, say takbir, pray and give charity (Sahih al-Bukhari 1044).\n\nIt is two rak'ahs, each with two standings and two bows, as described, followed by a short sermon.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1044.\n[GO:/prayer]","the eclipse prayer",!0,"")
