B.Mp=s(["Ch\u1ee7 Nh\u1eadt","Th\u1ee9 Hai","Th\u1ee9 Ba","Th\u1ee9 T\u01b0","Th\u1ee9 N\u0103m","Th\u1ee9 S\xe1u","Th\u1ee9 B\u1ea3y"],t.s)
B.cFz=new A.rS("Every Soul Will Taste It","Every soul will taste death, and only on the Day of Judgment will you be paid in full (3:185). The verse is not a threat; it is the calendar. The one who knows the appointment prepares for it \u2014 and preparation is worship.",u.h6)
B.cFx=new A.rS("The Will \u2014 Writing It Is a Sunna","The Prophet \ufdfa said: it is not right for a Muslim who has something to bequeath to sleep two nights without having his will written (Bukhari 2738). Two nights. The will is not for the dying; it is for the living who will grieve you.\n\nTwo limits apply. First, no more than a third: Sa\u2019d ibn Abi Waqqas asked to leave half and was told it was too much; of one third the Prophet \ufdfa said, \u2018One-third, yet even one-third is too much\u2019 (Bukhari 2744). Second, no bequest to an heir: \u2018Allah has given everyone who has a right his due, so no bequest may be made to an heir\u2019 (Abu Dawud 2870, hasan sahih per al-Albani; Tirmidhi 2120, sahih per al-Albani). The heirs\u2019 shares are fixed by Allah in Surah an-Nisa\u2019, and the will is for people who are not heirs, for debts and for charity.\n\nThe schools: the one-third limit is held in all four schools. The majority hold that a bequest to an heir is not valid unless the other heirs agree after the death. Scholar review needed: ask a scholar of your school before you write it.","Draft your will this month \u2014 even a page: debts, guardianship, the small bequests. Templates exist; the intention is the act.")
B.cFC=new A.rS("The Estate \u2014 Fair Before the End","Allah commands you concerning your children: the male receives the share of two females (4:11). That is one rule among several. The shares depend on who survives you (spouse, parents, children, siblings) and are set in Surah an-Nisa\u2019 (4:11, 4:12 and 4:176), so they are Allah\u2019s math, not the family\u2019s negotiation. Debts and the will (up to one third, and not for an heir) are settled before the shares are divided. Working it out for a real family is a scholar\u2019s task: scholar review needed here.",u.Al)
B.cFv=new A.rS("Plant What Outlives You","When a person dies, their deeds end except three: ongoing charity, knowledge that benefits, and a righteous child who prays for them (Muslim 1631). The grave is not a wall; it is a garden you can still plant.",u.zq)
B.bmR=s([B.cFz,B.cFx,B.cFC,B.cFv],t.Wx)
B.cFD=new A.U3("Preparing Before the Hour","The Prophet \ufdfa said: remember often the destroyer of pleasures \u2014 death (Tirmidhi 2307, hasan per Darussalam). Not to darken the day, but to brighten the scale.",B.bmR)
B.cFB=new A.rS("La Ilaha Illa Allah \u2014 the Last Word","The Prophet \ufdfa said: whoever\u2019s last words are la ilaha illa Allah enters Paradise (Abu Dawud 3116, sahih per al-Albani). And he advised: prompt your dying to say it, gently, without burden \u2014 the tongue loosens at the end, and the heart follows.",u.q8)
B.cFw=new A.rS("The Prayer Over the Dead","The janazah prayer is offered standing, without bowing or prostration. Four takbirs, salawat on the Prophet, dua for the deceased, and the salah is complete. The community carries the dead to their Lord on its shoulders.",u.fT)
B.cFu=new A.rS("Grieving Is Allowed","The Prophet \ufdfa wept at the death of his son Ibrahim and said: the eyes weep and the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord \u2014 and we are surely saddened by your departure, Ibrahim (Bukhari 1303). Tears are not weakness; the prohibition was only of wailing and despair.",u.dX)
B.bpj=s([B.cFB,B.cFw,B.cFu],t.Wx)
B.cFE=new A.U3("The Final Days","How the believer meets the end is a lesson the living need before the dying.",B.bpj)
B.cFA=new A.rS("The Grave Is a Garden","The Prophet \ufdfa said the grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of Fire (Tirmidhi 2460, weak per Darussalam \u2014 hold it as a reminder, not a ruling). What you send ahead decides which \u2014 and the sending is still in your hands.",u.kw)
B.cFy=new A.rS("The Meeting You Are Walking Toward","Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him (Tirmidhi 2309, sahih per Darussalam). The companions lived with this hadith the way travelers live with a map \u2014 not in dread of the road, but in anticipation of the arrival.",u.hh)
B.b3m=s([B.cFA,B.cFy],t.Wx)
B.cFF=new A.U3("Hope Forward","The school ends where the grave begins: with light.",B.b3m)
