B.Q8=s(["I am so sorry for your loss. Grief like this is love with nowhere to go, and there is no right way or right speed to carry it. The Prophet \ufdfa wept as his son Ibrahim was dying and said: \u201cThe eyes are shedding tears and the heart is grieved, and we will not say except what pleases our Lord.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 1303). Allah says: \u201cIndeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.\u201d (Qur'an 2:156). Make du\u2019a for them, lean on the people near you, and take today one hour at a time. I am here if you want to say more, or if you would like the du\u2019a for the deceased.","May Allah have mercy on them and give you patience. Your tears are not a lack of faith: the Prophet \ufdfa wept as his son Ibrahim was dying (Sahih al-Bukhari 1303). Allah says: \u201cIndeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.\u201d (Qur'an 2:156). Eat when you can, rest when you can, and let someone sit with you. If it would help, tell me about them, or I can share the du\u2019a for the deceased.","I am so sorry. Losing someone you love is among the heaviest things a heart carries, and you do not have to be strong right now. Allah says: \u201cIndeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.\u201d (Qur'an 2:156), and the Prophet \ufdfa taught that real patience is at the first stroke of a calamity (Sahih Muslim 926). Be gentle with yourself. I am listening, and I can share the du\u2019a for the deceased if you would like it."],t.s)
