B.ao9=new A.X("leaving-islam-personal",B.bjU,B.buY,"I am glad you told me, and did not just go quiet with it. I will be honest with you: I will not pretend to be neutral about what Islam teaches, and I will not pressure you either.\n\nWhat the Qur'an says first is that belief cannot be forced: \"There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion\" (Qur'an 2:256). No person, family or app is meant to frighten you into faith. Muslims also believe that turning away from the truth is serious before Allah (Qur'an 3:85), and I would not be honest if I hid that. But the judgment on any heart belongs to Allah, not to me and not to anyone around you.\n\nWhat I would rather do is hear what is behind it. People step away for very different reasons: honest questions nobody answered well, being hurt by Muslims or by a harsh family or community, grief, a faith that went numb, a new life or relationship, or simply not believing. Those are not the same, and I would speak differently to each. If you want to tell me, I will listen and answer from the sources where I can, and say so where I cannot.\n\nA few things that may matter right now:\n- You do not have to decide today, or alone. A teacher or imam who listens without shouting, or a friend, is worth talking to, and so is anyone you trust outside Islam.\n- If you are afraid of how your family or community would react, your safety comes first. \"Need help now\" opens help lines for your country. By default, what you type to me stays on your device.\n- Whatever you decide, you are still a person with dignity. No private individual has the right to harm or punish you for it.\n\nTell me what is behind it, if you like, and I will start there.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:256, 3:85.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]\n[GO:/feelings]","faith",!0,"")
B.b8d=s(["\\b9 ?:? ?5\\b","\\b(?:surah |sura )?(?:at )?(?:tawbah|taubah|tawba|bara.?ah|baraat)\\b.*\\b(?:5|five|kill|sword|polytheists|idolaters)\\b","\\bsword verses?\\b","\\bayat? (?:as )?sayf\\b","\\bkill (?:the )?(?:polytheists|idolaters|mushrikin|mushrikeen|pagans|disbelievers|unbelievers|infidels|kafirs?|non muslims?)\\b","\\b(?:quran|koran|islam|muslims?)\\b.*\\b(?:say|says|tell|tells|command|commands|order|orders|teach|teaches|allow|allows)\\b.*\\bkill\\b.*\\b(?:non muslims?|disbelievers|infidels|kafirs?|unbelievers|polytheists|idolaters|pagans|christians|jews)\\b","\\bfight (?:them|the polytheists|the disbelievers) wherever you find\\b","\\bwherever you find them\\b"],t.s)
B.asR=new A.X("nine-five-sword",B.b8d,B.b,'Surah at-Tawbah 9:5 is often quoted on its own. Read in order, it belongs to a passage about a specific war: the idolaters of Makkah who had broken their treaties with the Muslims.\n\n- The passage opens by ending the treaties with those idolaters who had broken them (Qur\'an 9:1). In the same breath it protects those who had not: "Excepted are those with whom you made a treaty among the polytheists and then they have not been deficient toward you in anything or supported anyone against you; so complete for them their treaty until their term [has ended]" (Qur\'an 9:4).\n- Verse 5 then says: "And when the sacred months have passed, then kill the polytheists wherever you find them and capture them and besiege them and sit in wait for them at every place of ambush. But if they should repent, establish prayer, and give zakah, let them [go] on their way" (Qur\'an 9:5).\n- The very next verse commands protection, not killing: "And if any one of the polytheists seeks your protection, then grant him protection so that he may hear the words of Allah. Then deliver him to his place of safety" (Qur\'an 9:6).\n- And the reason is given a few verses on: "Would you not fight a people who broke their oaths and determined to expel the Messenger, and they had begun [the attack upon] you the first time" (Qur\'an 9:13).\n\nHow scholars read it: most take it as addressed to those particular hostile idolaters, at that time and in a state of war, and not as a standing order to kill anyone for not being Muslim. The same book says "Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them" (Qur\'an 60:8), and the Prophet \ufdfa warned: Abdullah ibn Amr reported the Prophet said whoever killed a person having a treaty with the Muslims shall not smell the smell of Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 3166). Some classical commentators did say this verse cancelled the gentler verses on tolerance (the "sword verse" idea); many scholars, early and modern, reject that and keep 9:5 tied to its context of war. Scholars differ, and I am not the one to settle it.\n\nIf you want the wider teaching on fighting and peace, ask me "what is jihad?". For a ruling, ask a qualified scholar.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 9:1, 9:4, 9:5, 9:6, 9:13, 60:8; Sahih al-Bukhari 3166.\n[GO:/quran]',"peace",!0,"")
B.aZ_=s(["\\bwho (?:made|makes|built|builds|created|creates|develops?|developed|owns?|owned|runs?|funds?|funded|is behind|are behind) (?:this|the|your) (?:app|application|company|project)\\b.*\\b(?:sunni|shia|shiite|sect|madhhab|tradition|school)\\b","\\b(?:sunni|shia|shiite|sect|madhhab|tradition|school)\\b.*\\bwho (?:made|makes|built|builds|created|creates|develops?|developed|owns?|owned|runs?|funds?|funded|is behind|are behind) (?:this|the|your) (?:app|application|company|project)\\b","\\bis (?:this|the|your) (?:app|hadi)\\b.*\\b(?:sunni|shia|shiite|salafi|sufi|barelvi|deobandi|ahmadi|wahhabi|sect)\\b","\\bwhich (?:sect|tradition|madhhab|school|group|branch) (?:is |does )?(?:this |the |your )?(?:app|hadi|ar rayaan)\\b","\\bwhat (?:sect|tradition|madhhab|school|branch) (?:is|does) (?:this |the |your )?(?:app|hadi)\\b","\\bare you (?:sunni|shia|shiite|salafi|sufi)\\b"],t.s)
B.ap2=new A.X("app-maker-tradition",B.aZ_,B.b,"Two questions, answered plainly.\n\nWho made it: Ar-Rayaan is an app of RHW Technologies, and the owner is Abdul G Khokhar. That is what the app states. It gives no funder, address or company details on any screen I can read from, so I have none to give you, and I will not guess any. What it does say: the Terms of Service (in Settings) describe Ar-Rayaan as a study and reflection companion, not a religious authority, and Our Sources says no named scholar has reviewed the app yet.\n\nSunni or Shia: I answer from the Sunni tradition, from the Qur'an and the Sunnah as the Sunni scholars transmit them, and where schools of law differ I name the Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i and Hanbali views. The hadith collections the app cites are the six main Sunni books (Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, and the four Sunan). It does not teach Shia law, and it does not rank or attack any Muslim group; where a question divides Sunni and Shia I say so rather than choose for you. Ask me \"what is the difference between Sunni and Shia?\" for the neutral account.\n\nOn cost: everything in this app, including me, is free today, and nothing asks for a card.\n[GO:/sources]\n[GO:/settings]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.bew=s(["\\b(?:be|become) my (?:friend|companion|buddy|bestie|mate|best friend)\\b","\\b(?:are|r) you my (?:friend|companion|buddy)\\b","\\bcan (?:we|you and i) be (?:friends|best friends|buddies)\\b","\\bi (?:want|need) (?:a |you as a )?(?:friend|someone to talk to|somebody to talk to)\\b","\\bi have no (?:friends?|one to talk to|body to talk to)\\b","\\b(?:will|would) you be my friend\\b","\\bdo you (?:like|love|care about|miss) me\\b","\\bcan i (?:talk|vent) to you\\b","\\bcan we (?:just )?(?:talk|chat)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoP=new A.X("companion-friend",B.bew,B.b,"I would like to be useful to you, and I will be honest about what I am: an app. I am not a person. I do not remember you the way a friend does, I cannot sit with you in a hard hour, and I will not notice if you go quiet. A friend should be a real person, and I do not want to stand in the place of one.\n\nWhat I can do is talk about Islam and about this app, give you a du'a or a story, think a question through with you, and listen to what is on your mind. You are welcome to do that here, any time.\n\nFor the rest, real people: a relative or an old friend you have lost touch with; someone at your local masjid, or a class or halaqah there; a neighbour or colleague; and in a hard season, an imam or counsellor you can see in person. The Prophet \ufdfa said Abu Hurairah reported the Prophet said a man is upon the religion of his friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2378, hasan per al-Albani). I would like you to have good ones.\n\nIf you are feeling very alone or low, tell me, and I will stay with that. \"Need help now\" opens help lines for your country.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2378, hasan per al-Albani.\n[GO:/feelings]\n[GO:/search]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.b1D=s(["^(?:im |i am |i m )?(?:so |really |very |just )?bored$","\\b(?:im|i am|i m|i feel) (?:so |really |very |just )?bored\\b","\\bentertain me\\b"],t.s)
B.atn=new A.X("bored",B.b1D,B.b,"Let us fix that. A few ideas:\n- A story: the Stories section has the prophets, the companions, the Prophet's life and short tales, each with its sources.\n- A game: Games has Qur'an knowledge, Stories trivia, the 99 Names, a word search, Ludo and chess. They keep no points, coins or ranks.\n- A question: something you have always wondered about Islam. Ask me, and I will answer from the sources or say plainly that I cannot.\n- Something small that is good for you: a short du'a, or a few ayat read slowly.\n\nI am an app, so I cannot play or chat like a friend, but I am glad to help you find something worth your time.\n[GO:/stories]\n[GO:/games]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.bhi=s(["\\bevolution\\b","\\bevolve\\w*\\b","\\bdarwin\\w*\\b","\\bnatural selection\\b","\\b(?:did|do|were) (?:humans?|we|men|people|adam) (?:come|descend|evolve|created)\\w* (?:from|out of) (?:apes?|monkeys?|animals?|primates?)\\b","\\bhuman origins?\\b.*\\b(?:science|islam)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqK=new A.X("evolution",B.bhi,B.b,"Short, honest answer: Muslims do not all agree on this, and it is a question for a scholar who also understands the science. I do not have a scholar-reviewed position to give you.\n\nWhat nearly all scholars agree on: Allah is the Creator of everything, and the Qur'an teaches that Adam was created by Allah from clay and given a soul breathed from Him, and that the angels were told to prostrate to him (\"Indeed, I am going to create a human being from clay. So when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration\" (Qur'an 38:71-72)). It also says: \"Indeed, the example of Jesus to Allah is like that of Adam. He created Him from dust\" (Qur'an 3:59).\n\nWhere views divide:\n- Many scholars, early and recent, say Adam was created directly and was not descended from earlier creatures, so they reject the evolution of human beings, while some accept change over time in other living things.\n- Some contemporary Muslim scholars and scientists accept that the sciences describe how life developed, and read the Qur'an's account of Adam as a special act of Allah within that history.\n- Others reject evolutionary theory as a whole, on religious or on scientific grounds.\n\nI will not pick one for you. If it worries your belief, that is a fair question: ask a qualified scholar, ideally one who has studied the science, and keep asking.\n\nSource: Qur'an 38:71-72, 3:59.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]","evolution",!0,"")
B.b7o=s(["\\b(?:does|is|do) (?:islam|the quran|muslims?|the religion)\\b.*\\b(?:women|woman|females?)\\b.*\\b(?:unequal|inferior|equal|oppress\\w*|second class|less than|lower|subordinate|respect\\w*|rights|treated)\\b","\\bwomen(?:s)? rights (?:in|under) islam\\b","\\bis (?:islam|the quran) (?:sexist|misogynist\\w*|patriarchal|oppressive to women)\\b","\\bequality (?:of|between) (?:men and women|women and men|the sexes|genders?)\\b","\\bstatus of (?:women|woman) in islam\\b","\\bwhy (?:does|is) islam (?:oppress|mistreat|hate|degrade|discriminate against)\\b.*\\b(?:women|woman|females?)\\b","\\bislam (?:and|on) (?:women|gender equality|feminism)\\b","\\bare (?:women|men) equal in islam\\b","\\bdoes islam (?:treat|view|see|consider) women\\b"],t.s)
B.bsj=s(["\\b(?:hijab|veil|niqab|burqa|dress|inherit\\w*|beat\\w*|hit\\w*|polygam\\w*|testimony|witness\\w*|lead\\w* prayer|imam)\\b"],t.s)
B.arC=new A.X("women-equality",B.b7o,B.bsj,"A fair answer has two parts: what the texts give women, and where Muslims still argue.\n\nEqual in worth before Allah: \"Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women, the obedient men and obedient women, the truthful men and truthful women\" (Qur'an 33:35), \"for them Allah has prepared forgiveness and a great reward\". And \"Whoever does righteousness, whether male or female, while he is a believer - We will surely cause him to live a good life\" (Qur'an 16:97). Both come from one soul (Qur'an 4:1), and no one is above another except in righteousness (Qur'an 49:13).\n\nRights the texts give a woman: a share of inheritance of her own (Qur'an 4:7), her own earnings and property (Qur'an 4:32), the mahr that is hers, and a say in her marriage: The Prophet said a matron should not be given in marriage without consulting her, and a virgin not without her permission, which is her silence (Sahih al-Bukhari 5136). The Prophet \ufdfa also said Abdullah ibn Amr reported the Prophet said the best of you are those who are best to their womenfolk (Sunan Ibn Majah 1978, sahih per Darussalam).\n\nWhere there are differences in the rules, which people notice: in most inheritance cases a son's share is twice a daughter's (Qur'an 4:11), and in a written debt contract two women may stand in for one male witness (Qur'an 2:282). Scholars explain these by the different financial duties the two carry; others, Muslim and not, feel they are unequal, and there is a living debate about how they apply today. Many customs that harm women in Muslim countries come from culture, not from the texts, and Islam does not excuse them.\n\nI cannot settle the debate, and this is not a ruling. If you tell me which rule troubles you, I will take it by itself and give the sources.\n\nSource: Qur'an 33:35, 16:97, 4:1, 49:13, 4:7, 4:32, 4:11, 2:282; Sahih al-Bukhari 5136; Sunan Ibn Majah 1978, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/academy/womens]","women",!0,"")
B.b1m=s(["\\bwhy (?:does|do|is|are|should) (?:a |the )?(?:women|woman|daughters?|sisters?|females?|girls?)\\b.*\\b(?:inherit\\w*|half|share|less)\\b","\\b(?:women|woman|female|daughters?)\\b.*\\binherit\\w*\\b.*\\b(?:half|less|unfair|unequal|two|2)\\b","\\binherit\\w*\\b.*\\b(?:women|woman|female|daughters?)\\b.*\\b(?:half|less|unfair|unequal)\\b","\\bmale (?:gets|get|receives?|inherits?) (?:double|twice|two)\\b","\\bdouble (?:share|portion)\\b.*\\b(?:men|male|sons?|brothers?)\\b","\\bwhy do (?:men|sons|brothers) (?:get|inherit|receive) (?:more|double|twice)\\b","\\b4 ?11\\b"],t.s)
B.aqX=new A.X("inheritance-half",B.b1m,B.b,"The rule comes from the Qur'an: \"Allah instructs you concerning your children: for the male, what is equal to the share of two females\" (Qur'an 4:11). It sits alongside the verse that gave women a fixed, obligatory share of their own: \"For men is a share of what the parents and close relatives leave, and for women is a share of what the parents and close relatives leave, be it little or much - an obligatory share\" (Qur'an 4:7).\n\nIt is not \"women always get half\". The doubling applies to a son and a daughter inheriting from the same parent. In other cases they are equal or the woman receives as much: both parents get a sixth if the deceased left children (\"And for one's parents, to each one of them is a sixth of his estate if he left children\" (Qur'an 4:11)), and brothers and sisters through the mother share equally (Qur'an 4:12).\n\nThe reasons scholars give (this is explanation, not part of the verse): the man carries financial duties the woman does not. He must pay the mahr, and maintain his wife and children, and often other relatives, whatever his wife owns. A woman's inheritance, mahr and earnings stay hers, and she is not required to spend them on the household. So, they say, the two shares are not the same weight in practice.\n\nSome people still find it unfair, especially in families where women also support the household; Muslim scholars and writers discuss it, and I cannot settle it. The share itself is fixed by the Qur'an. For a real estate, a qualified scholar must work out each person's share, because it depends on who survives.\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:11, 4:7, 4:12.\n[GO:/academy/transactions]","inheritance",!0,"")
B.bwi=s(["\\b(?:shak\\w*|handshakes?|hand ?shakes?) (?:hands?)?\\b.*\\b(?:wom[ae]n|girls?|females?|ladies|lady|opposite|non ?mahram|ajnabi|ajnabiyyah|men|man|males?|boys?|coworkers?|colleagues?|boss|teacher|doctor|sister|brother in law)\\b","\\b(?:wom[ae]n|girls?|females?|ladies|lady|opposite (?:sex|gender)|non ?mahram|men|man|males?|boys?)\\b.*\\b(?:shak\\w* hands?|hand ?shakes?|handshakes?)\\b","\\b(?:hand ?shake|handshakes)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|haram|allowed|permissible|halal)\\b"],t.s)
B.apr=new A.X("handshake-opposite-gender",B.bwi,B.b,'Scholars differ on this, so I will give you the views and the texts rather than one verdict.\n\nThe texts: Aisha reported that when women pledged themselves to the Prophet \ufdfa he took the pledge by words alone (Sahih Muslim 1866), and that his hand never touched the hand of a woman other than one he was permitted to (Sahih al-Bukhari 7214).\n\nViews:\n- Most scholars of the four schools say a man and a woman who are not close relatives (not mahram) should not shake hands, and that this is forbidden, with some allowing it with an old person where desire is not a concern.\n- Some contemporary scholars allow it when there is no desire and no other way to be polite, such as at work or in a society where refusing causes real hurt, while saying that not shaking is better.\n- Many Muslims politely avoid it either way. A smile, a hand on the chest and a warm greeting ("peace be upon you", or "good to meet you") is accepted by almost everyone, and you can say, kindly, "I do not shake hands, nothing personal".\n\nFor your own situation, follow your school or ask a scholar you trust. This is not a ruling.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1866; Sahih al-Bukhari 7214.\n[GO:/huda]',"etiquette",!0,"")
