B.at5=new A.X("travel-prayer",B.aSx,B.bal,"A traveller may shorten the four-rak'ah prayers (Dhuhr, Asr and Isha) to two rak'ahs. Fajr (2) and Maghrib (3) stay as they are. This is a mercy from Allah: \"there is no blame upon you for shortening the prayer\" (Qur'an 4:101). Umar asked the Prophet \ufdfa about it, and he said it is a charity from Allah, so accept His charity (Sahih Muslim 686).\n\nWhen it applies: on a journey of about 80 km (roughly 50 miles) or more, by the view of most scholars. Some scholars say there is no fixed distance. You begin shortening when you leave your town. How long you can keep shortening in one place differs: the Shafi'i, Maliki and Hanbali schools say up to about four days of staying; the Hanafi school says up to fifteen days.\n\nCombining: the Shafi'i, Maliki and Hanbali schools allow a traveller to join Dhuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha, at the time of either. The Prophet \ufdfa did this, delaying Dhuhr to Asr when he set out before noon (Sahih al-Bukhari 1111). The Hanafi school allows joining only at Arafah and Muzdalifah during Hajj. You may not skip a prayer or push it out of its day.\n\nOn a plane or train: face the qibla as far as you can and pray seated if you cannot stand. If the time will run out, pray in your seat; do not leave a prayer to be made up unless you have to.\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:101; Sahih Muslim 686; Sahih al-Bukhari 1111.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-travel]","travel prayer",!0,"")
B.bl_=s(["\\bpray(?:ing)? (?:sitting|seated|lying|while sitting|in a chair|on a chair|from a chair)\\b","\\bsit(?:ting)? down\\b.*\\bpray\\b","\\bpray\\b.*\\bsit(?:ting)? down\\b","\\b(?:sick|ill|illness|injured|elderly|disabled|disability|wheelchair|bed ?ridden|back pain|knee pain|surgery|pregnan\\w*)\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bprayers?\\b.*\\b(?:when|if) (?:i am|im|i m) (?:sick|ill|injured|unwell|pregnant)\\b","\\b(?:pray|salah|salat|namaz)\\b.*\\b(?:when|while|if) (?:i am|im|i m|am) (?:sick|ill|unwell|injured|pregnant)\\b","\\bcannot stand\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bcant stand\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bprayers? (?:in|on) (?:a )?(?:chair|wheelchair|bed)\\b","\\bprayers?\\b.*\\bunable to stand\\b","\\bprayers?\\b.*\\bsick(?:ness)?\\b"],t.s)
B.b5j=s(["\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|zakat|janazah|funeral)\\b","\\b(?:feel better|get well|get better|cheer|comfort|console|visit\\w*|make them|what (?:can|should|do) (?:i|you|we) say|dua for|cure)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqz=new A.X("sitting-prayer",B.bl_,B.b5j,"Yes. Prayer is never dropped because of illness; it is made easier. If you cannot stand, pray sitting; if you cannot sit, pray lying on your side. The Prophet \ufdfa told 'Imran ibn Husayn, who had piles: pray standing, and if you cannot, then sitting, and if you cannot, then on your side (Sahih al-Bukhari 1117).\n\nHow: if you can stand for part of the prayer, stand for that part. If you can stand but not go down to the ground, stand for the standing and bow and prostrate by nodding. If you cannot go down, nod your head for ruku' and again, lower, for sujud. Sitting on a chair is acceptable when sitting on the floor is not possible. The Qur'an says \"Allah does not charge a soul except [with that within] its capacity\" (Qur'an 2:286).\n\nIf you are too ill to pray at the right time, you may combine Dhuhr with Asr and Maghrib with Isha according to the Hanbali school (and some Shafi'i and Maliki scholars); otherwise pray each as best you can. Keep praying as long as you have your mind; if you lose consciousness, ask a scholar about making it up.\n\nThe Illness and Patience guide has more help.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1117; Qur'an 2:286.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-illness]","sick prayer",!0,"")
B.aSX=s(["\\b(?:make up|makeup|make-up|catch up|compensate|repay|replace)\\b.*\\b(?:missed|skipped|forgotten|lost|old|past|backlog)\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bmissed prayers?\\b","\\bqada\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bprayers? qada\\b","\\bqada prayers?\\b","\\bmiss(?:ed|ing)?\\b.*\\b(?:prayers?|fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b","\\b(?:skip(?:ped)?|overslept|slept through|sleep through|woke up late for)\\b.*\\b(?:prayers?|fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b","\\bforgot (?:to pray|my (?:prayers?|fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)|about (?:the )?(?:prayers?|fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha))\\b","\\bhavent prayed\\b","\\bdidnt pray\\b.*\\b(?:years|long|months)\\b","\\bnot prayed for\\b","\\bstopped praying\\b","\\bprayers? (?:i|i have) (?:missed|skipped|not prayed)\\b","\\bmake up\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bprayers? make up\\b"],t.s)
B.bny=s(["\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|period|menstrua\\w*|cycle)\\b","\\bfor (?:many |several |a few |\\d+ )?(?:years|months|decades)\\b"],t.s)
B.arn=new A.X("missed-prayers",B.aSX,B.bny,"If you missed a prayer because you slept through it or forgot, pray it as soon as you remember. The Prophet \ufdfa said: if anyone forgets a prayer, he should pray it when he remembers it, and it has no expiation except that (Sahih al-Bukhari 597) (Sahih Muslim 684).\n\nIf you left a prayer on purpose or over a long time (years): that is a serious matter, so start with sincere tawbah (repentance) and begin praying on time from today. Most scholars (all four schools) say the missed prayers are still owed and should be made up. A minority say they cannot be made up and the way out is repentance and voluntary prayers. Follow the view of your school and ask a trusted scholar if you are unsure.\n\nHow to make them up: pray each missed prayer in its own rak'ah count (Fajr as 2, Dhuhr as 4 and so on), in order if you can. If you do not know how many you missed, estimate honestly and pray until you are sure you have covered them. A practical way is to pray one or two make-up prayers after each of today's prayers until the debt is done, without leaving your current prayers on time. A woman does not make up prayers missed during her period.\n\nThe Making Up Missed Prayers guide in this app lays out the method.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 597; Sahih Muslim 684.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-qada]","missed prayers",!0,"The Prophet \ufdfa said a forgotten prayer has no expiation except to pray it, so it is prayed when remembered; for a prayer left on purpose, most scholars hold the debt is still there, so it is made up along with sincere repentance.")
B.b8E=s(["\\bsocks?\\b","\\bkhuff\\w*\\b","\\bmasah\\b","\\bwip(?:e|ing) over\\b","\\bshoes?\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bprayers?\\b.*\\b(?:shoes?|sandals?|slippers?|footwear)\\b","\\bpray(?:ing)? (?:in|with|wearing) (?:shoes?|sandals?|socks?)\\b"],t.s)
