B.arU=new A.X("prayer-times-overview",B.aWM,B.bAG,"The five daily prayers and when each is prayed:\n- Fajr (dawn): from true dawn, when the white thread of dawn shows, until sunrise.\n- Dhuhr (midday): from just after the sun passes its highest point until Asr begins.\n- Asr (afternoon): from when an object's shadow equals its height (Hanafi: twice its height) until sunset. The best time ends when the sun turns yellow.\n- Maghrib (sunset): from sunset until the red twilight has gone (the Hanafi school waits for the white twilight to go).\n- Isha (night): from the end of twilight until midnight, and by necessity until Fajr begins.\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa said the time of Fajr lasts until the first part of the sun appears, Dhuhr until Asr comes, Asr until the sun turns yellow, Maghrib until the twilight disappears, and Isha until half the night has passed (Sahih Muslim 612). The Qur'an says \"prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times\" (Qur'an 4:103), and the white thread of dawn is in Qur'an 2:187.\n\nThe exact minutes for where you are depend on the calculation method. The Prayer Times screen shows today's times for your location, with alerts.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 612; Qur'an 4:103, 2:187.\n[GO:/prayer]","prayer times",!0,"")
B.bmL=s(["\\bhow many\\b.*\\brakah\\b","\\bnumber of rakah\\b","\\brakah\\b.*\\b(?:in|of|for|is|are)\\b.*\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha|each|every|five|daily|fard|obligatory)\\b","\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b.*\\b(?:how many|rakah)\\b","\\bhow many (?:fard|obligatory|farz) (?:prayers?)\\b","\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b.*\\bsunnah\\b","\\bsunnah\\b.*\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b","\\brawatib\\b","\\bsunnah (?:prayers?|rakah)\\b"],t.s)
