B.anR=new A.X("wudu-howto",B.bxy,B.bol,"Wudu is the washing you do before prayer. Allah says: \"wash your faces and your forearms to the elbows and wipe over your heads and wash your feet to the ankles\" (Qur'an 5:6). The Prophet \ufdfa taught it by doing it, as 'Uthman showed it (Sahih al-Bukhari 159).\n\nThe steps:\n1. Make the intention in your heart and say \"Bismillah\".\n2. Wash both hands up to the wrists, three times.\n3. Rinse your mouth three times.\n4. Sniff water into your nose and blow it out, three times.\n5. Wash your face three times, from the hairline to the chin and ear to ear.\n6. Wash your right arm to the elbow, then your left, three times each.\n7. Wipe your head once with wet hands, from the front back to the nape and forward again; wipe the ears too.\n8. Wash your right foot to the ankle, then your left, three times each, between the toes as well.\n9. Say the shahadah and, if you like, the du'a after wudu.\n\nThe only obligatory parts are the face, the arms, the head and the feet. The rest are sunnah, but do them all if you can. Do not waste water. The Wudu guide in this app shows it step by step.\n\nSource: Qur'an 5:6; Sahih al-Bukhari 159.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-wudu]","wudu",!0,"")
B.bks=s(["\\b(?:break|breaks|breaking|broke|broken|invalidat\\w*|nullif\\w*|cancel\\w*|void\\w*|undo\\w*|end|ends|ruin\\w*)\\b.*\\bwudu\\b","\\bwudu\\b.*\\b(?:break|breaks|breaking|broke|broken|invalidat\\w*|nullif\\w*|cancel\\w*|void\\w*|again|valid|remain|still|stay|stays|last|lasts|renew)\\b","\\bdo i (?:need|have) to (?:redo|repeat|renew|make) wudu\\b","\\bneed (?:to )?(?:make|do|renew|redo) wudu (?:again|after)\\b","\\bwhat (?:cancels?|breaks?|invalidates?) (?:my |the )?(?:wudu|ablution)\\b","\\bis my wudu (?:valid|broken|still)\\b","\\b(?:sleep|sleeping|asleep|nap|dozed|dozing|fell asleep|drowsy)\\b.*\\bwudu\\b","\\bwudu\\b.*\\b(?:sleep|sleeping|asleep|nap|dozed|touch\\w*|blood|bleed\\w*|vomit\\w*|laugh\\w*|camel|private part|wind|gas|fart\\w*|doubt\\w*|unsure|not sure)\\b","\\btouch(?:ing)? (?:my |a |the )?(?:private part|genital|penis|woman|wife|husband|spouse)\\b.*\\b(?:wudu|prayer)\\b","\\b(?:wudu|ablution)\\b.*\\b(?:touch\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.aY6=s(["\\b(?:quran|mushaf)\\b"],t.s)
B.aok=new A.X("wudu-breakers",B.bks,B.aY6,"Wudu is broken by what leaves the body and by loss of consciousness. All schools agree on these:\n- Urine, stool and wind (and the thin fluid called madhy). The Prophet \ufdfa said the prayer of someone who has passed wind is not accepted until he makes wudu (Sahih al-Bukhari 135).\n- Deep sleep, fainting, madness or intoxication, anything that takes away your awareness. Safwan ibn Assal reported that on a journey the Prophet \ufdfa told them to keep their socks on for three days, except for janabah, but not for urine, stool or sleep, meaning these need a fresh wudu (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 96, hasan per al-Albani).\n- Janabah (emission, intercourse) needs a full ghusl, not only wudu.\n\nLight dozing while sitting up, without losing awareness, does not break it. The Companions used to wait for the night prayer until they were nodding off, and then prayed without a new wudu (Sunan Abu Dawud 200, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nSleeping lying down or leaning breaks it. The schools differ on whether it also breaks when you sleep sitting firmly on the ground.\n\nThe schools differ on these:\n- Touching your private part with the hand: it breaks wudu in the Shafi'i and Hanbali schools (and in the Maliki school if with desire); not in the Hanafi school.\n- Touching a woman's skin: it breaks wudu in the Shafi'i school; in the Maliki and Hanbali schools only if with desire; not in the Hanafi school.\n- Flowing blood or a big vomit: it breaks wudu in the Hanafi school and, if a lot, in the Hanbali school; not in the Shafi'i and Maliki schools.\n- Eating camel meat: it breaks wudu in the Hanbali school (Sahih Muslim 360).\n\nIf you doubt whether you broke it, leave the doubt: your wudu stays. The Prophet \ufdfa said that a man who imagines he has broken wind in prayer should not leave unless he hears a sound or smells something (Sahih al-Bukhari 137).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 135, 137; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 96, hasan per al-Albani; Sunan Abu Dawud 200, sahih per al-Albani; Sahih Muslim 360.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-wudu]","wudu",!0,"These are the things that make a person need a fresh wudu, because they are a state of impurity from the body.")
B.b_R=s(["\\bghusl\\b","\\bfull bath\\b","\\britual bath\\b","\\bbath after (?:sex|intercourse|period|menstrua\\w*)\\b","\\bjanabah\\b","\\bjunub\\b","\\bwet dream\\b","\\bnocturnal emission\\b","\\bmajor (?:impurity|ablution)\\b","\\bpurif\\w* after (?:sex|intercourse|marital)\\b","\\bwash after (?:sex|intercourse)\\b","\\bwhen is (?:a )?(?:bath|ghusl) (?:needed|required|obligatory)\\b","\\bhow to (?:take|do|perform) (?:a )?(?:full )?bath\\b"],t.s)
