B.atk=new A.X("fast-teeth",B.aZv,B.byG,"Yes, you may brush your teeth while fasting. It does not break the fast as long as you do not swallow the toothpaste or water. Use a little paste, spit it all out and rinse your mouth well. If some goes down by accident, the fast is still valid: the Qur'an says \"there is no blame upon you for that in which you have erred but [only for] what your hearts intended\" (Qur'an 33:5).\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa greatly valued cleaning the teeth with the siwak: he said that if it were not hard on his followers he would order them to use it for every prayer (Sahih al-Bukhari 887). The Shafi'i school dislikes using the siwak after midday while fasting, because of the smell of the fasting mouth, so if you follow it, brush before noon. Some scholars prefer to avoid strong-tasting paste in the day and brush at suhoor and after iftar; that is a matter of care, not a requirement.\n\nThe same is true in wudu: rinse your mouth and nose, but do not sniff water deep into your nose while fasting. The Prophet \ufdfa said: snuff up water freely unless you are fasting (Sunan Abu Dawud 2366, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nSource: Qur'an 33:5; Sahih al-Bukhari 887; Sunan Abu Dawud 2366, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.blu=s(["\\b(?:medicine|medication|medications|meds?|pill|pills|tablet|tablets|capsule|capsules|ibuprofen|paracetamol|acetaminophen|panadol|aspirin|antibiotic\\w*|painkiller\\w*|pain killer\\w*|syrup|cough|insulin|diabetes|diabetic|blood pressure|prescription|drugs?)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:medicine|medication|medications|meds?|pill|pills|tablet|tablets|capsule|capsules|ibuprofen|paracetamol|acetaminophen|panadol|aspirin|antibiotic\\w*|painkiller\\w*|pain killer\\w*|syrup|cough|insulin|diabetes|diabetic|blood pressure|prescription)\\b","\\b(?:take|taking|swallow\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:medicine|medication|pill|pills|tablet|tablets|ibuprofen|paracetamol)\\b.*\\b(?:while|during|when|if)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b"],t.s)
B.aZW=s(["\\b(?:injection|inhaler|drops?|puffer|patch|suppository|nasal spray|spray)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqO=new A.X("fast-medicine",B.blu,B.aZW,"Swallowed medicine such as a tablet, capsule or syrup breaks the fast, because it goes into the stomach by the mouth. This holds for ibuprofen, paracetamol, antibiotics and the like. I cannot tell you whether any medicine is right for you or safe to delay: for that, ask your doctor or pharmacist.\n\nWhat the religion gives you is ease. Allah says: \"Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship\" (Qur'an 2:185). If you are ill, and fasting would worsen it or you cannot go without the medicine, you may break the fast, take the medicine, and make up the days later: \"whoever among you is ill or on a journey [during them] - then an equal number of days [are to be made up]\" (Qur'an 2:184). If your illness is long-term with no hope of recovering, you give a ransom of feeding a poor person for each day instead (Qur'an 2:184).\n\nBefore you break a fast, see if you can plan the medicine for suhoor and after iftar. Ask your doctor about long-acting forms that cover the day, and ask a scholar if your case is unclear. A person whose doctor says they must not fast should not fast; it is not weakness in faith.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:185, 2:184.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.bon=s(["\\b(?:injection\\w*|inject\\w*|vaccin\\w*|jab|drip|iv|intravenous|blood test|blood tests|blood draw|donat\\w* blood|give blood|cupping|insulin shot|anaesthe\\w*|anesthe\\w*|dialysis|catheter)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:injection\\w*|vaccin\\w*|jab|drip|intravenous|blood test|blood tests|blood draw|donat\\w* blood|give blood|cupping|insulin shot|anaesthe\\w*|anesthe\\w*|dialysis|catheter|surgery)\\b"],t.s)
B.arB=new A.X("fast-injection-tests",B.bon,B.b,"Most contemporary scholars say these do not break the fast, as nothing is taken as food or drink by the mouth or throat: a blood test, giving blood, a vaccine, and a medical injection (such as insulin, an antibiotic or a painkiller). A drip that gives nourishment (glucose, a feeding drip) is treated like food and breaks the fast. Some scholars are stricter, so if you are unsure, plan these for after iftar.\n\nWhatever your case, if the treatment is needed, your health comes first. The Qur'an allows the sick to break the fast and make up the days: \"Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship\" (Qur'an 2:185). Ask your doctor for the timing and a scholar if your case is complicated.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:185.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.aS6=s(["\\b(?:eye ?drops?|ear ?drops?|nose ?drops?|nasal spray|nasal drops?|inhaler|inhalers|asthma|puffer|ventolin|nebuli[sz]er|oxygen|patch|suppository|skin cream|ointment|lotion)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:eye ?drops?|ear ?drops?|nose ?drops?|nasal spray|nasal drops?|inhaler|inhalers|asthma|puffer|ventolin|nebuli[sz]er|oxygen|patch|suppository|ointment)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoL=new A.X("fast-drops-inhaler",B.aS6,B.b,"The scholars differ here, so be careful and, where you can, choose the safer course:\n- Eye drops and ear drops: most contemporary scholars say they do not break the fast, because they are not food or drink. Some classical scholars say the taste reaching the throat does. If you can use them at night, do.\n- Nose spray and drops: avoid them if you can; anything that reaches the throat is treated like drink.\n- An asthma inhaler: many contemporary fatwa bodies say it does not break the fast, since it is a vapour and not food or drink; some scholars are stricter. If asthma is a risk, the need to breathe comes first, and you can make the day up if a scholar rules it broken.\n- Skin creams, patches and ointments: these do not break the fast.\n\nIf you must use something and it may break the fast, health comes first. Allah gives ease: \"Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship\" (Qur'an 2:185). Ask your doctor about timing and a scholar about your case.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:185.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.bxn=s(["\\b(?:smok\\w*|cigarette\\w*|vap(?:e|es|ing)|vapor\\w*|e ?cig\\w*|shisha|hookah|nicotine|tobacco|chewing gum|gum|snuff|paan)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:smok\\w*|cigarette\\w*|vap(?:e|es|ing)|vapor\\w*|e ?cig\\w*|shisha|hookah|nicotine|tobacco|chewing gum|gum|paan)\\b"],t.s)
B.aoc=new A.X("fast-smoking",B.bxn,B.b,"Smoking breaks the fast: the smoke is drawn on purpose into the throat and lungs, and nicotine is taken as a substance. Vaping, shisha and chewing tobacco do too. Chewing gum is best avoided in the day: the flavour dissolves and may be swallowed. If you smoke, Ramadan is a good time to stop, with the help of your doctor: you manage without it from dawn to sunset, and many people find that is the start of quitting.\n\nIf you smoked by mistake, forgot you were fasting, or something went down without intending it, the fast is not broken: the Qur'an says \"there is no blame upon you for that in which you have erred but [only for] what your hearts intended\" (Qur'an 33:5).\n\nSource: Qur'an 33:5.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.bqn=s(["\\b(?:forgot|forgetfully|forgotten|by mistake|accidentally|by accident|unintentionally|without (?:thinking|meaning|realizing|realising)|did not realise|didnt realise|swallowed (?:a )?(?:fly|insect|dust|smoke|water)|water (?:went|going) down|swallowed (?:my )?(?:saliva|spit)|saliva|spit|spitting|phlegm|mucus|dust|fly)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:forgot|forgetfully|by mistake|accidentally|by accident|unintentionally|swallowed (?:a )?(?:fly|insect|dust|smoke|water)|water (?:went|going) down|saliva|phlegm|mucus|dust)\\b","\\b(?:ate|eat|eaten|drank|drink|drunk|had) .*\\b(?:forgot|forgetting) .*\\b(?:fast\\w*|fasting)\\b","\\bforgot i was fasting\\b","\\bforgot (?:that )?(?:i was|it was) (?:fasting|ramadan)\\b"],t.s)
B.at6=new A.X("fast-forgot-accident",B.bqn,B.b,"If you eat or drink because you forgot you were fasting, your fast is still valid. The Prophet \ufdfa said: if somebody eats or drinks forgetfully, he should complete his fast, for what he ate or drank was given to him by Allah (Sahih al-Bukhari 1933). Stop as soon as you remember. You do not make it up.\n\nThe same ease applies to things you do not intend or cannot avoid: a fly or dust going down your throat, water going down when rinsing your mouth in wudu (provided you did not exaggerate), a dream with wetness, or your own saliva. The Qur'an says \"there is no blame upon you for that in which you have erred but [only for] what your hearts intended\" (Qur'an 33:5).\n\nPhlegm that reaches the mouth should be spat out rather than swallowed on purpose; if it goes down by itself, the fast stands.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1933; Qur'an 33:5.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.b5x=s(["\\b(?:kiss\\w*|hug\\w*|embrac\\w*|touch\\w*|cuddl\\w*|intimacy|intimate|sex|sexual|intercourse|masturbat\\w*|wet dream|wife|husband|spouse)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:kiss\\w*|hug\\w*|embrac\\w*|intimacy|intimate|sex|sexual|intercourse|masturbat\\w*|wet dream|wife|husband|spouse)\\b"],t.s)
B.boR=s(["\\b(?:iftar|suhoor) (?:with|invit\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.arM=new A.X("fast-intimacy-kiss",B.b5x,B.boR,"Between sunrise and sunset in Ramadan:\n- Intercourse breaks the fast, and doing it deliberately in the day of Ramadan is a major matter that requires a penalty (kaffarah) on top of making the day up. A man told the Prophet \ufdfa he had been ruined for having relations with his wife while fasting; the Prophet \ufdfa gave him the way of atonement: freeing a slave if he can, otherwise fasting two months in a row, otherwise feeding sixty poor people (Sahih al-Bukhari 1936). The Hanafi and Maliki schools put the same penalty on deliberate eating and drinking; the Shafi'i and Hanbali schools apply it to intercourse only.\n- Kissing and embracing your spouse are allowed if you can control yourself. A'ishah said the Prophet \ufdfa used to kiss and embrace his wives while fasting, and that he had more power to control his desires than any of you (Sahih al-Bukhari 1927). If it leads you to go further, avoid it in the day.\n- Releasing semen on purpose (by hand or any other way) breaks the fast and needs a make-up day, and the person should repent; a wet dream does not break it.\n- The night is free: Allah allows relations with your wife from sunset until dawn (Qur'an 2:187).\n\nIf the fast was broken by a slip, make up the day and ask Allah's forgiveness; ask a scholar if you are unsure which rule applies.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1936, 1927; Qur'an 2:187.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.bhr=s(["\\b(?:vomit\\w*|throw\\w* up|threw up|puk\\w*|nause\\w*|sick to (?:my )?stomach)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:vomit\\w*|throw\\w* up|threw up|puk\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.ao0=new A.X("fast-vomit",B.bhr,B.b,"If vomit comes up on its own (you are ill, or something upset your stomach), your fast is not broken and you do not make it up. If you make yourself vomit on purpose, the fast is broken and you must make the day up. A report attributed to the Prophet \ufdfa says the same, but scholars grade it differently (al-Albani sahih, Darussalam da'if), so the ruling rests on the general view of the scholars rather than on it.\n\nIf some vomit goes back down your throat against your will, the fast stands; if you swallow it on purpose, the fast is broken.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.b8N=s(["\\b(?:invalidat\\w*|nullif\\w*|break|breaks|breaking|broke|spoil\\w*|ruin\\w*|void\\w*|cancel\\w*|ends?)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\bwhat (?:breaks|invalidates|nullifies|spoils) (?:the |my |a )?(?:fast|fasting)\\b","\\bdoes\\b.*\\bbreak (?:the |my )?(?:fast|fasting)\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|are) (?:the )?(?:things? )?(?:that )?(?:allowed|permitted|not allowed|forbidden|haram|prohibited) (?:while|when|during) (?:fast\\w*|ramadan)\\b"],t.s)
B.aUm=s(["\\b(?:kaffar\\w*|fidyah|expiation|penalty|atone\\w*)\\b","\\b(?:iftar|suhoor|say|dua|recite|eat first|meal|when (?:do|should|can))\\b"],t.s)
B.asF=new A.X("fast-breakers",B.b8N,B.aUm,"The fast runs from true dawn until sunset (Qur'an 2:187). What breaks the fast (all schools agree):\n- Eating or drinking on purpose, anything that reaches the stomach by the mouth (including swallowed medicine and smoking).\n- Marital intercourse in the day (with a penalty if deliberate).\n- Deliberately making yourself vomit.\n- Menstruation or postnatal bleeding, even a moment before sunset.\n- Deliberately releasing semen.\n- Leaving the intention, or choosing to stop the fast.\n\nWhat does not break it: eating or drinking by forgetting (Sahih al-Bukhari 1933); things you did not intend such as dust, a fly, or water going down while rinsing; a wet dream; brushing your teeth without swallowing; a bath, swimming or rain on you; perfume or smelling food; kissing your spouse without going further; blood tests and most injections; eye drops and skin creams; swallowing your own saliva.\n\nEach of those has its own answer: ask me about the one you have in mind. Fasting also means guarding the tongue: lying and backbiting do not break the fast but spoil its reward.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:187; Sahih al-Bukhari 1933.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.beS=s(["\\b(?:exempt\\w*|excus\\w*|allowed to (?:skip|miss|break|not)|permitted to (?:skip|miss|break|not)|who (?:does|do|is|are) not have to|who need not|who can skip|who can miss|who must not|who should not|not required to)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:exempt\\w*|excus\\w*|not obligatory on|not required|skip|miss)\\b","\\bwho (?:is|are) exempt\\b","\\bwho (?:can|may) (?:skip|break|miss|not) (?:the )?(?:fast|fasting|ramadan)\\b","\\b(?:pregnan\\w*|breastfeed\\w*|nursing|elderly|old age|travell?er\\w*|travell?ing|sick|ill|illness|child|children|kids?|menstruat\\w*|period|mental\\w*)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:allowed|permit\\w*|must|have to|obligatory|exempt|need|required|should|can)\\b","\\bi am (?:pregnant|sick|ill|travelling|traveling|old|elderly|breastfeeding)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b.*\\b(?:when|while|if)\\b.*\\b(?:pregnan\\w*|breastfeed\\w*|nursing|sick|ill|travell?ing|period)\\b","\\bfasting (?:when|while|if) (?:i am |im )?(?:pregnant|sick|ill|travell?ing|old|breastfeeding)\\b","\\bfasting while (?:pregnant|sick|ill|travell?ing|breastfeeding)\\b","\\bcan i (?:skip|miss|break|not fast)\\b"],t.s)
B.bnU=s(["\\b(?:ibuprofen|medicine|medication|pill|tablet|injection|drops?|inhaler|vomit\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.aqy=new A.X("fast-exempt",B.beS,B.bnU,"Fasting Ramadan is obligatory on every adult Muslim who is sane and able. These people are excused:\n- The sick, if fasting would harm them or delay recovery, and travellers: they break the fast and make up the same number of days later. Allah says: \"whoever among you is ill or on a journey [during them] - then an equal number of days [are to be made up]\" (Qur'an 2:184). The Qur'an also says \"Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship\" (Qur'an 2:185).\n- Women in menstruation or postnatal bleeding: they must not fast, and they make the days up later (not the prayers).\n- Pregnant or breastfeeding women who fear harm to themselves or the baby: they may break the fast. The schools differ on what follows: the Hanafi school says make the days up; the Shafi'i and Hanbali schools add a ransom of feeding a poor person for each day if the fear is for the baby only; some scholars say only the ransom.\n- The elderly, and the chronically ill with no hope of recovery, who cannot fast: they give a ransom of feeding one poor person for each day (Qur'an 2:184).\n- Children before puberty: not obliged, though they can be gently encouraged.\n- Those who have lost their minds: not obliged.\n\nIf you break the fast for a valid reason, do not feel guilty or hide it; it is Allah's permission. For your own case, ask a scholar or your doctor.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:184, 2:185.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fasting",!0,"")
B.aYS=s(["\\b(?:make up|makeup|qada|compensate|repay|replace|owe|owed)\\b.*\\b(?:missed |skipped |broken |old )?(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|days)\\b","\\b(?:missed|skipped|broken)\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan)\\b","\\bfidyah\\b","\\bkaffarah\\b","\\bkaffara\\b","\\bransom\\b.*\\bfast\\w*\\b","\\bfeed(?:ing)? (?:a )?poor\\b.*\\b(?:fast\\w*|ramadan|roza|saum|sawm|siyam)\\b","\\bhow (?:many|much) .*\\bfidyah\\b","\\bfast\\w* (?:i|we) (?:missed|owe)\\b","\\bbroke my fast\\b","\\bbreak my fast (?:on purpose|deliberately|intentionally)\\b","\\bbroken fast\\b"],t.s)
B.ao_=new A.X("fast-makeup-fidyah",B.aYS,B.b,"Three different things, often mixed up:\n1. Qada (making up). If you miss days of Ramadan for a valid reason (illness, travel, period, pregnancy), fast the same number of days before the next Ramadan comes, one day for each day missed. They need not be in a row. Allah says: \"an equal number of days [are to be made up]\" (Qur'an 2:184). If you are late by years, still make them up, and ask a scholar whether anything extra is due (the Hanafi school says nothing extra).\n2. Fidyah (ransom). For someone who cannot fast and cannot make it up (a very old person, a chronic illness): feed one poor person for each day missed (Qur'an 2:184). The amount is a meal or its value; the schools set it differently (about half a sa' of wheat, around 1.6 kg, in the Hanafi school; a mudd, about 750 g of staple food, in the others). Ask your masjid for the local figure.\n3. Kaffarah (penalty). For deliberately breaking a Ramadan fast by intercourse (and, in the Hanafi and Maliki schools, by eating or drinking on purpose): free a slave, or if not possible fast two months in a row, or if not possible feed sixty poor people (Sahih al-Bukhari 1936). On top of it, make up the day.\n\nIf you broke a fast on purpose in some other way, repent sincerely, make the day up and ask a scholar about the penalty for your school.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:184; Sahih al-Bukhari 1936.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]","fidyah",!0,"")
B.aP8=s(["\\bsuhoor\\b","\\biftar\\b","\\bbreak(?:ing)? (?:the |my |a )?(?:fast|fasting)\\b","\\bwhat (?:do|should) (?:i|we) (?:eat|say|recite) (?:at|before|for|when) (?:iftar|suhoor|breaking)\\b","\\bwhen (?:do|should|can) (?:i|we) (?:break|start|stop|end) (?:the |my )?(?:fast|fasting)\\b","\\bfasting (?:times?|hours)\\b","\\bwhen does (?:the )?fast (?:start|begin|end)\\b","\\b(?:pre ?dawn|dawn) meal\\b","\\bwhen to stop eating\\b","\\bdua (?:for|at|when) (?:breaking|iftar|opening)\\b","\\bopen(?:ing)? (?:my |the )?fast\\b","\\bintention (?:for|of) (?:the )?(?:fast|fasting)\\b","\\bniyyah (?:for|of) (?:the )?(?:fast|fasting|ramadan)\\b","\\bniyyat\\b"],t.s)
