B.bAW=s(["Thank you for trusting me with something this personal. I am not disgusted, and I am not going to tell you that Allah hates you. Allah introduces Himself as ar-Rahman, ar-Rahim, and the Prophet \ufdfa told us that Allah's mercy overcomes His anger (Sahih Muslim 2751). Qur'an 39:53 speaks to servants who have wronged themselves and tells them not to despair of Allah's mercy.\n\nI will also be honest, because you deserve that more than comfort that is not true: mainstream Islamic scholarship holds that same-sex acts are not permitted, and I am an app, not a scholar, so I cannot rule on your life. Many scholars also separate feelings a person did not choose from what a person does, and nobody has the right to humiliate you for what you carry. Many Muslims carry this quietly and alone, and that is a heavy way to carry it.\n\nIt can help to talk, in confidence, to a scholar or a counsellor who will treat you with care. Is there anyone you trust enough to tell? And are you safe right now?","I am glad you said it out loud. You are still a person Allah made, and a question like yours comes from someone who cares about their faith. Hatred is not what the sources teach us to expect from Allah: His mercy overcomes His anger (Sahih Muslim 2751), and the door of tawbah is open to everyone.\n\nI will not pretend there is no difficulty. Scholars have long held that same-sex acts are not permitted, and I cannot rule on your case. They have also taught that nobody is to be hated or mistreated for what they feel, and that Allah knows the struggle it is. A scholar or counsellor who listens first can walk with you in private.\n\nHow are you doing with all of this today? If it ever feels too heavy, the lines below are free and confidential."],t.s)
