B.bEa=new A.Q(B.bMu,["/prayer","/zakat","/huda/guide?id=huda-zakat","/quran","/adhkar?set=morning","/hadith","/calendar"],t.w)
B.bMT={"prophet-adam":0,"prophet-nuh":1,"prophet-yunus":2,"prophet-ayyub":3,"prophet-sulayman":4,"tale-cave-people":5,"tale-two-gardens":6}
B.bfx=s(["Allah told the angels that He would put a person on the earth. Allah taught Adam the names of things, and the angels saw how much Adam could learn.","Allah told the angels to bow to Adam, to show respect. They all did, except Iblis. He said no, because he thought he was better than Adam. Being proud like that was wrong.","Adam and his wife lived in the Garden. Allah told them not to go near one tree. Shaytan whispered to them, and they ate from it. They were sorry and asked Allah to forgive them, and Allah forgave them.","Allah sent Adam and his wife down to live on the earth. He promised to send them guidance. Whoever follows Allah\u2019s guidance will not be afraid or sad."],t.s)
B.bvi=s(["Nuh told his people to worship only Allah. He called them for a very long time, by night and by day, but only a few of them listened.","Allah told Nuh to build a ship. Some of his people laughed at him. Nuh kept trusting Allah and kept building.","Then the flood came. Nuh took the believers and pairs of animals on the ship. He called to his son to come aboard, but his son did not listen.","Then Allah told the water to go down, and the ship came to rest on a mountain. Nuh and the people with him were safe.","Nuh was patient for a very long time. Allah tells us that the best end is for those who are patient and try to do right."],t.s)
B.baQ=s(["Yunus was a messenger of Allah. He left his people because he was upset with them, and he left before Allah had allowed it.","A big fish swallowed him, and he was in the dark. Yunus said: there is no god but You, glory to You, I was in the wrong. Allah heard him and saved him.","Allah put Yunus safely on the shore and made a plant grow over him. Later, his people believed in Allah."],t.s)
B.brC=s(["Ayyub was very unwell and in hardship. He stayed patient, and he called out to Allah: I am in trouble, and You are the kindest of all those who are kind.","Allah answered him. He told Ayyub to stamp his foot, and a spring of cool water came out. Ayyub washed and drank, and what was hurting him was taken away.","Allah gave Ayyub his family back, and more like them, as a mercy from Him. Ayyub is a good example of patience."],t.s)
B.b4N=s(["Sulayman was a prophet and a king, the son of Dawud. He asked Allah to forgive him, and Allah gave him a great kingdom.","Allah let Sulayman understand the speech of the birds. One day an ant told the other ants to go into their homes, so that they would not be crushed. Sulayman smiled and thanked Allah.","A bird called the hoopoe told Sulayman about a queen and her people. Sulayman sent her a letter that began: in the name of Allah, the Kind, the Merciful.","Allah asked Sulayman\u2019s family to be thankful. Sulayman thanked Allah for all that he had been given."],t.s)
B.aVO=s(["Some young people believed in Allah when most of the people around them did not. They were brave, and Allah made them stronger in their faith.","They went into a cave, and Allah put them to sleep for a very, very long time. The Qur\u2019an says they stayed there three hundred years, and nine more.","When they woke up, they thought they had slept for only a day. Allah knows best how long it was. The story reminds us that Allah\u2019s promise is true."],t.s)
B.aQe=s(["A man had two beautiful gardens, with grapes, date palms and a river. He was proud, and he said that he thought they would never be lost.","His friend told him to be thankful to Allah and not proud of what he had. The man did not listen.","Then his gardens were ruined. He was sad, and he wished he had not been proud. We should always thank Allah for what we have."],t.s)
B.bEb=new A.Q(B.bMT,[B.bfx,B.bvi,B.baQ,B.brC,B.b4N,B.aVO,B.aQe],t.VJ)
