B.bM1={"prophet-ibrahim":0,"prophet-musa":1,"prophet-yusuf":2,"prophet-isa":3,"prophet-idris":4,"prophet-hud":5,"prophet-salih":6,"prophet-lut":7,"prophet-ismail":8,"prophet-dawud":9,"prophet-ishaq":10,"prophet-yaqub":11,"prophet-shuayb":12,"prophet-dhul-kifl":13,"prophet-harun":14,"prophet-ilyas":15,"prophet-alyasa":16,"prophet-basket":17,"prophet-zakariya":18}
B.bnW=s(["Ibrahim asked his father and his people why they prayed to statues. Statues cannot hear, or see, or help anyone. He spoke kindly. His father was angry and told him to go away. Ibrahim said peace to him and left, and he kept worshipping only Allah.","One day, when the people were away, Ibrahim broke their statues, all except the biggest one. When the people came back, he asked them to ask the statues who did it. They knew the statues could not speak. The people were angry and made a big fire. Allah said: fire, be cool and safe for Ibrahim. The fire did not hurt him.","Ibrahim took his wife Hajar and their baby Ismail to a valley with no people and no water, because Allah told him to. Hajar asked if Allah had told him to. He said yes. She said then Allah will not leave us. Later, Ibrahim and Ismail built the Ka\u2019bah together and asked Allah to accept it from them.","Allah tested Ibrahim. In a dream he saw that he must give up his son. His son was kind and brave and said to do what Allah commands. Both obeyed Allah. Then Allah said that Ibrahim had passed the test, and Allah gave them a great animal to give instead. The son was safe.","Allah chose Ibrahim as a close friend. Allah tells us that Ibrahim is a good example for us. Every time we pray for blessings on the Prophet Muhammad, we also ask for blessings on Ibrahim."],t.s)
B.bf8=s(["Pharaoh was a cruel ruler who hurt the Children of Israel. When Musa was a baby, Allah told his mother to put him in the river and not to be afraid, because Allah would bring him back to her. Pharaoh\u2019s family found the baby. Pharaoh\u2019s wife said they should keep him and not harm him.","When Musa grew up, he tried to help someone and a man died by accident. Musa was sorry and asked Allah to forgive him, and Allah forgave him. He left the city and went to a place called Madyan. There he helped two women give water to their sheep, and he asked Allah for what is good. He stayed in Madyan for many years.","Musa saw a fire on the mountain and went toward it. Allah spoke to him: I am your Lord. Allah told him to worship Him and to pray. Allah gave him two signs, his stick and his hand. Musa asked Allah to help him and to send his brother Harun with him. Allah said yes. Allah told them to speak to Pharaoh gently, and said, do not be afraid, I am with you both.","Pharaoh\u2019s magicians threw down their ropes. Musa threw his stick and it swallowed up what they had made. The magicians knew it was from Allah and they bowed down and believed. Pharaoh chased Musa and his people to the sea. Musa said that his Lord would guide him. Allah told him to hit the sea with his stick, and the sea opened like two big mountains of water. Musa and his people crossed and were safe.","Allah spoke to Musa again on the mountain and gave him the tablets with guidance. Musa also went to learn from a servant of Allah who had special knowledge. He asked to follow him, and the man said Musa would not be able to be patient. Musa found it hard to stay quiet, and the man explained what he had done.","Musa\u2019s story shows that Allah is with those who trust Him. A baby in a river was brought back to his mother, a man who ran away became a messenger, and the sea became a road."],t.s)
B.aUs=s(["Yusuf dreamed of eleven stars, the sun and the moon bowing to him. His father Ya\u2019qub told him to keep it secret from his brothers. His brothers were jealous because their father loved Yusuf and his little brother very much. They took Yusuf away and threw him into a well.","Yusuf grew up in the house of an important man in Egypt. Someone tried to make him do something wrong. Yusuf said no and asked Allah to protect him. He ran to the door. Even though he had done nothing wrong, he was put in prison. Yusuf preferred prison to doing wrong.","The king had a strange dream. Yusuf explained it: there would be seven good years, and then seven hard years. He said to save the grain in the good years. The king saw how honest Yusuf was and made him trusted over the storehouses of Egypt.","When the hard years came, Yusuf\u2019s brothers came to Egypt to buy food. Yusuf knew them, but they did not know him. Their father Ya\u2019qub was very sad, but he did not give up hope in Allah. At last Yusuf told his brothers who he was. He was kind to them.","Yusuf sent his shirt to his father. When it touched Ya\u2019qub\u2019s face, he could see again. The whole family came to Egypt and was together at last. Yusuf\u2019s dream came true. He thanked Allah and prayed to be a Muslim until the end of his life.","The Prophet Muhammad was asked who is the most honoured in the sight of Allah. He said it is the one who has the most taqwa, and he also spoke of Yusuf as a prophet from a family of prophets."],t.s)
B.b61=s(["The angels told Maryam that Allah would give her a baby boy named Isa. She was surprised. Allah said that when He decides something, He only says be, and it is. When Isa was a baby in the cradle, he spoke. He said that he was a servant of Allah, and that Allah had made him a prophet.","Allah gave Isa signs to show he was a messenger. By Allah\u2019s permission he shaped a clay bird and it flew, and he helped people who were ill. Every sign was by the permission of Allah. Isa told the people to worship Allah, who is his Lord and their Lord.","Some of Isa\u2019s followers believed in Allah. They asked for a table of food from the sky. Isa prayed to Allah, and Allah said He would send it down, and they must be thankful.","Allah told Isa that He would take him up to Himself. The Qur\u2019an says that people did not kill him, and Allah raised him up. Only Allah knows exactly how this happened.","On the Day of Judgement, Allah will ask Isa if he told people to take him and his mother as gods. Isa will say that he only told them what Allah commanded: to worship Allah, his Lord and their Lord. Muslims love and honour Isa as a messenger of Allah."],t.s)
B.b2x=s(["Idris was a prophet who always told the truth. Allah says that He raised him to a high place. The Qur\u2019an tells us no more about his life, so we do not add anything.","Allah says that Idris was one of the patient and the good. On the night the Prophet Muhammad went up to the heavens, he met Idris and Idris welcomed him as a brother and a prophet."],t.s)
B.b7P=s(["Hud was sent to a strong people called Aad. They built tall buildings and they were proud of how powerful they were. Hud told them to worship Allah alone and to be thankful for all He had given them.","Hud did not ask them for any money. He told them to ask Allah to forgive them. They said he was foolish and they would not leave their gods. Hud said he trusted in Allah.","The people saw a cloud and thought it would bring rain. But it was a strong wind that Allah sent, and it destroyed those who would not listen. Allah saved Hud and the believers with him, as a mercy."],t.s)
B.btj=s(["Salih was sent to a people called Thamud. They had built homes in the plains and carved houses in the mountains. Allah gave them a she-camel as a clear sign. Salih told them to let her eat on Allah\u2019s land and not to harm her.","Some proud people did not believe. The ones who believed were not proud. The proud ones said that they did not believe in what Salih had brought. The believers stayed true to Allah.","The people hurt the she-camel and did not listen to Allah\u2019s command. Salih told them to enjoy their homes for three days, and then Allah\u2019s promise came true. Allah saved Salih and the believers."],t.s)
B.b46=s(["Lut was a prophet sent to his people. They did very wrong things that nobody before them had done. Lut told them to fear Allah and listen to him. He did not ask them for any payment. He wanted only to help them.","Angels came to Lut as guests. Lut was worried and sad for them. He told his people to fear Allah and not to shame him in front of his guests. Only Lut\u2019s family who believed were saved.","In the morning, Allah\u2019s command came, and the cities were destroyed. This is a sign for those who think. Allah saved the believers."],t.s)
B.aXf=s(["Ismail was a baby when his father Ibrahim brought him and his mother Hajar to a dry valley. Hajar trusted Allah. She ran between two hills looking for water, seven times. Then, by Allah\u2019s mercy, an angel came and water came out of the ground. This is the spring called Zamzam.","Ismail grew up in Makkah. A tribe saw birds over the water and came to live near the spring. Ismail grew up among them and learned Arabic from them. Allah took care of Hajar and Ismail, just as the angel had said.","Allah says that Ismail kept his promises. He was a messenger and a prophet. He told his family to pray and to give charity, and Allah was pleased with him. Allah also counts him among the patient.","Ibrahim told Ismail that Allah had told him to build a house there. Ismail said he would help. Ismail carried the stones, and Ibrahim built. They asked Allah to accept it and to make them and their children Muslims."],t.s)
B.b2R=s(["Dawud was a young man in an army. Their enemy was a big strong man called Goliath. The believers asked Allah for patience and help. By Allah\u2019s permission, Dawud defeated Goliath. Later, Allah gave him kingship and prophethood.","Allah made Dawud strong and gave him wisdom. The mountains and the birds praised Allah with him. Allah taught him how to shape iron. He often turned back to Allah.","Two men came to Dawud with an argument about sheep. Dawud understood that Allah was testing him. He asked Allah to forgive him and he bowed in prayer, and Allah forgave him.","The Prophet Muhammad told us that Dawud always ate from the work of his own hands, and he used to fast every other day. Allah made reciting the Zabur easy for him."],t.s)
B.bzF=s(["Angels came to Ibrahim with good news. His wife was surprised because she was old. The angels said it was by Allah\u2019s command. Allah gave them a son named Ishaq, and after him a grandson, Ya\u2019qub.","Allah made Ishaq a prophet and a good leader. He told his people to do good things, to pray and to give charity. He worshipped Allah.","Ishaq\u2019s family was a family of prophets. His father was Ibrahim, his son was Ya\u2019qub, and his grandson was Yusuf. The Qur\u2019an does not give more of Ishaq\u2019s own story, so we do not add any."],t.s)
B.b_z=s(["When Yusuf told his father about his dream, Ya\u2019qub said to keep it secret from his brothers. He knew that Shaytan is a clear enemy. He also knew that Allah would teach Yusuf and bless him.","Yusuf\u2019s brothers brought back his shirt with false blood on it and said that a wolf had eaten him. Ya\u2019qub knew they were not telling the truth. He was very sad, but he was patient and asked Allah for help.","Ya\u2019qub took his sorrow only to Allah. He told his sons to go and look for Yusuf, and not to give up hope in Allah\u2019s mercy. When Yusuf\u2019s shirt was put on his face, he could see again. The family was together.","Before he died, Ya\u2019qub asked his sons what they would worship after him. They said they would worship the one God, as their fathers Ibrahim, Ismail and Ishaq did. He told them to stay Muslim until the end."],t.s)
B.b4Y=s(["Shu\u2019ayb was sent to the people of Madyan. He told them to worship Allah alone, and to give full measure and weight when they sold things. He told them not to cheat people or to spread trouble on the earth.","The people laughed at him. They said that they would not leave what their fathers worshipped. Shu\u2019ayb said he only wanted to make things better, as much as he could, and that his help is only from Allah.","When Allah\u2019s command came, Allah saved Shu\u2019ayb and the believers with him. The people who did wrong were destroyed. Shu\u2019ayb said that he had told them the message of his Lord."],t.s)
B.aTU=s(["Dhul-Kifl is named in the Qur\u2019an. Allah says he was patient and that Allah took him into His mercy. The Qur\u2019an tells no story about him, so we do not add one.","Allah calls him patient, one who is among the good, and one of the best people. A person can be remembered by Allah for being patient and good, even if we know only a little about him."],t.s)
B.bmI=s(["Musa asked Allah for help and to send his brother Harun with him. Allah said yes and made Harun a prophet. Harun could speak clearly, and he helped Musa.","When Musa went to the mountain, he told Harun to look after the people. A man made a calf and some people began to worship it. Harun told them it was a test, that their Lord is the Most Kind, and that they should follow him. But they did not listen to him.","When Musa came back, he was upset. Harun told him that he had been afraid the people would split up, and that they had almost hurt him. Musa prayed for them both, and asked Allah to forgive him and his brother."],t.s)
B.biA=s(["Ilyas was a messenger of Allah. He asked his people why they called on a false god and left Allah, the best of creators. His people did not believe him, but Allah\u2019s chosen servants were safe.","Allah says peace be upon Ilyas, and that people after him would speak of him well. He was one of the good and of Allah\u2019s believing servants. The Qur\u2019an tells no more, so we do not add more."],t.s)
B.b1U=s(["Al-Yasa is named in the Qur\u2019an with other prophets. Allah says that He preferred them above all people. The Qur\u2019an tells no event from his life, so we do not add any.","He is named with Ismail, Yunus, Lut and Dhul-Kifl. Allah chose them and remembers them with honour. That is all the Qur\u2019an tells us about him."],t.s)
B.bl7=s(["Allah told Musa\u2019s mother to put her baby in a basket and place it in the river. He told her not to be afraid or sad, because He would bring the baby back to her.","Pharaoh\u2019s family picked the baby up. Pharaoh\u2019s wife loved him and said they should keep him and not harm him. Musa\u2019s mother was very worried, but Allah made her heart strong. She told her daughter to follow the basket.","Baby Musa would not take milk from other women. His sister said she knew a family who could look after him. So Musa was returned to his mother, as Allah had promised. She was happy, and she knew that Allah\u2019s promise is true."],t.s)
B.bgb=s(["Zakariya was old and his wife could not have children. He called to his Lord quietly and asked for a child who would be good and would help after him. He had always found Allah answers his prayers.","Angels called to Zakariya while he was praying. They told him that Allah would give him a son named Yahya. Zakariya was amazed. Allah said it is easy for Him, just as He had made Zakariya when he was nothing.","Zakariya asked for a sign. Allah said that for three nights he would not speak to people. He came out and told his people by signs to praise Allah in the morning and the evening."],t.s)
